-- ============================================================
-- ea1: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- THE SEAT LAYER (Parts 2 to 6, ss 8 to 66).
--
-- SEAT: an employee, or a workman, in Singapore: a person who works under a contract of service
-- for an employer.  This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above
-- as the questions that person would ask: how my job can end, what I must be paid and when,
-- what my employer may take off my salary, my rest days and hours, what I get on retrenchment,
-- retirement or a change of employer, and what my employer may not do with my pay.  Nothing
-- here is new law, and no rule is restated: every answer is a call on a layer 1 rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from
-- a list -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded for the employee.
-- The records and MAYBE inputs the layer 1 rules expect are built inside each question from those
-- answers, and the SAME rule is then called.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure"; "I am not sure"
--     becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * An amount the person does not know is asked as 0, and becomes NOTHING.
--   * Public holidays are asked as up to two dates; "1 January 1900" means there is none.
--   * A pay record has many fields.  The seat asks for basic pay, commissions and other
--     allowances for a month.  The fields that the rule asked about leaves out of its sum (overtime,
--     bonus, productivity incentive, travelling, food and housing allowances, reimbursements) are
--     set to 0 where they do not change the answer; each such place says so in a comment.
--   * The Minister may substitute some figures (the proportions of ss 29, 30, 31, 32, the ceilings of
--     ss 33 and 35).  The person cannot state them, so the Act's own figures are used; a substitution
--     would change those answers (NOTES.md).
--   * The Third Schedule's day rate (seams S6) and the Fourth Schedule's hourly rate (S7) are
--     amounts the person gives, as the schedule's answer for them.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means
-- the Act does not answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- THERE IS NO SEAT FOR AN OFFICIAL.  Where a provision addresses only an official (ss 3, 33(2),
-- 37(1A), 38(3), 41A, 49, 52, 66(5)), the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through
-- the questions below, for what it means to them.

DECLARE `My answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- Why the person's salary for a month is not for a whole month, for s 20A(1).
DECLARE `Why I did not work the whole month` IS ONE OF
    `I started work after the first day of the month`
    `My employment ended before the end of the month`
    `I took unpaid leave for one or more days of the month`
    `I took leave to perform my national service`
    `None of these`

-- How my employer dismissed me, for s 14(2A).
DECLARE `How my employer dismissed me` IS ONE OF
    `With notice`
    `Without notice, but with salary in place of notice`
    `Without notice and without salary in place of notice`

-- What I ask for on a claim, for s 14(2).
DECLARE `What I ask for` IS ONE OF
    `To be reinstated in my job`
    `Compensation`
    `A sum the Commissioner considers just`

-- The right in issue under s 17.
DECLARE `Which right of mine` IS ONE OF
    `To join a registered trade union`
    `To take part in the activities of a registered trade union`
    `To associate with others to organise a trade union`
    `Some other right`

-- The kind of deduction in issue, for ss 27, 30 and the questions that follow.
DECLARE `Which deduction` IS ONE OF
    `For absence from work`
    `For damage to or loss of goods or money I was responsible for`
    `For house accommodation my employer supplied`
    `For an amenity or service my employer supplied`
    `To recover an advance, a loan, an unearned benefit or an overpayment`
    `For my contributions under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`
    `Another deduction I agreed to in writing`
    `Paid to a cooperative society`
    `Prescribed by regulations`
    `Some other deduction`

-- Why my employer asks me to work past the usual limit, for ss 38(2) and 40(2A).
DECLARE `What the work is` IS ONE OF
    `An accident, actual or threatened`
    `Work essential to the life of the community`
    `Work essential for defence or security`
    `Urgent work to be done to machinery or plant`
    `An interruption of work that was impossible to foresee`
    `Work in an industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore, or an essential service`
    `Something else`

-- The property or money a claim for salary is made against, for s 33(3).
DECLARE `Which property or money` IS ONE OF
    `Property my fellow workers and I were working on`
    `Property that was the produce of our work`
    `Movable property we used in our work`
    `Money due to my employer for work we did`
    `Property or money of some other kind`

-- The proceeding my gratuity is owed in, for s 47(1).
DECLARE `Which proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `The winding up of a company`
    `The bankruptcy of my employer, or the distribution of the estate of an employer who died insolvent`
    `The winding up of a VCC, before the operative date`
    `The winding up of a VCC, on the operative date`
    `The winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC, before the operative date`
    `The winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC, on the operative date`
    `Some other proceeding`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- A date that the person gives as 1 January 1900 when there is none.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`my date if there is one` MEANS
    IF day EQUALS Date 1 1 1900 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST day -- input mapping

-- Up to two public holidays, 1 January 1900 meaning none.
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      second IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`my public holidays` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (first EQUALS Date 1 1 1900) AND (second EQUALS Date 1 1 1900) THEN EMPTY -- input mapping
        IF first EQUALS Date 1 1 1900 THEN LIST second -- input mapping
        IF second EQUALS Date 1 1 1900 THEN LIST first -- input mapping
        OTHERWISE LIST first, second -- input mapping

-- A pay record for one month from the three amounts on a payslip.  The fields the rules asked about
-- leave out of the sum, or that no rule on this page reads, are 0 (see each question's comment).
GIVEN basic IS A NUMBER
      commissions IS A NUMBER
      allowances IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pay for a period`
`my monthly pay from my payslip` MEANS
    `Pay for a period` WITH
        `the amounts are for` IS `Pay is fixed for each month` -- input mapping
        `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS basic -- input mapping
        `overtime payments` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the sums asked about
        `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the sums asked about
        `commissions` IS commissions -- input mapping
        `productivity incentive payments` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the sums asked about
        `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the sums asked about
        `travelling allowances` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the sums asked about
        `food allowances` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the sums asked about
        `housing allowances` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the sums asked about
        `allowances of any other kind` IS allowances -- input mapping
        `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of salary
        `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of salary
        `value of a travelling concession` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of salary
        `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of salary
        `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of salary
        `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of salary

-- The Act's ground of dismissal from a yes/no.
GIVEN misconduct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Ground of dismissal`
`my employer's ground from what I know` MEANS
    IF misconduct
    THEN `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` -- input mapping
    ELSE `Ground: some other ground or none` -- input mapping

-- The manner of dismissal in the Act's words, from the person's choice.
GIVEN how IS A `How my employer dismissed me`
GIVETH A `s 14(2A) Manner of dismissal`
`my manner of dismissal from what I say` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `With notice` THEN `s 14(2A) dismissed with notice` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Without notice, but with salary in place of notice` THEN `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice but with payment of any salary in lieu of notice` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Without notice and without salary in place of notice` THEN `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu of such notice` -- input mapping

-- What the person asks for on a claim, in the keel's words.
GIVEN ask IS A `What I ask for`
GIVETH A `Relief a claimant may seek`
`my relief from what I ask for` MEANS
    CONSIDER ask
    WHEN `To be reinstated in my job` THEN `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` -- input mapping
    WHEN Compensation THEN `Relief: compensation` -- input mapping
    WHEN `A sum the Commissioner considers just` THEN `Relief: payment of a sum the Commissioner considers just` -- input mapping

-- The right in issue under s 17, in the section's words.
GIVEN right IS A `Which right of mine`
GIVETH A `s 17 Right of the employee`
`my right in the section's words` MEANS
    CONSIDER right
    WHEN `To join a registered trade union` THEN `s 17(a) the right to join a registered trade union` -- input mapping
    WHEN `To take part in the activities of a registered trade union` THEN `s 17(b) the right to participate in the activities of a registered trade union, whether as an officer of the trade union or otherwise` -- input mapping
    WHEN `To associate with others to organise a trade union` THEN `s 17(c) the right to associate with any other persons for the purpose of organising a trade union in accordance with the provisions of the Trade Unions Act 1940` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Some other right` THEN `s 17 a right that the section does not name` -- input mapping

-- Up to three rest days, public holidays or other holidays, 1 January 1900 meaning none.
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      second IS A DATE
      third IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`my days off` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (d EQUALS Date 1 1 1900)) (LIST first, second, third) -- input mapping

-- The kind of deduction in the section's words, from the person's choice.
GIVEN which IS A `Which deduction`
GIVETH A `s 27(1) Kind of deduction`
`my kind of deduction in the section's words` MEANS
    CONSIDER which
    WHEN `For absence from work` THEN `s 27(1)(a) a deduction for absence from work` -- input mapping
    WHEN `For damage to or loss of goods or money I was responsible for` THEN `s 27(1)(b) a deduction for damage to or loss of goods expressly entrusted to the employee for custody, or for loss of money for which the employee is required to account` -- input mapping
    WHEN `For house accommodation my employer supplied` THEN `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer` -- input mapping
    WHEN `For an amenity or service my employer supplied` THEN `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer` -- input mapping
    WHEN `To recover an advance, a loan, an unearned benefit or an overpayment` THEN `s 27(1)(f) a deduction for the recovery of an advance, loan or unearned employment benefit, or for the adjustment of an overpayment of salary` -- input mapping
    WHEN `For my contributions under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` THEN `s 27(1)(h) a deduction of contributions payable by the employer on behalf of the employee under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Another deduction I agreed to in writing` THEN `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Paid to a cooperative society` THEN `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Prescribed by regulations` THEN `s 27(1)(k) a deduction prescribed` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Some other deduction` THEN `s 27(1) a deduction of some other kind` -- input mapping

-- The case in section 38(2), from the person's choice of what the work is.
GIVEN work IS A `What the work is`
GIVETH A `s 38(2) Case`
`my case under section 38(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER work
    WHEN `An accident, actual or threatened` THEN `s 38(2)(a) accident, actual or threatened` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work essential to the life of the community` THEN `s 38(2)(b) work, the performance of which is essential to the life of the community` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work essential for defence or security` THEN `s 38(2)(c) work essential for defence or security` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Urgent work to be done to machinery or plant` THEN `s 38(2)(d) urgent work to be done to machinery or plant` -- input mapping
    WHEN `An interruption of work that was impossible to foresee` THEN `s 38(2)(e) an interruption of work which it was impossible to foresee` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work in an industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore, or an essential service` THEN `s 38(2)(f) work to be performed by employees in any industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore or any of the essential services as defined under Part 3 of the Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 38(2) some other case` -- input mapping

-- The case in section 40(2A), from the same choice.
GIVEN work IS A `What the work is`
GIVETH A `s 40(2A) Case`
`my case under section 40(2A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER work
    WHEN `An accident, actual or threatened` THEN `s 40(2A)(a) accident, actual or threatened` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work essential to the life of the community` THEN `s 40(2A)(b) work, the performance of which is essential to the life of the community` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work essential for defence or security` THEN `s 40(2A)(c) work essential for defence or security` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Urgent work to be done to machinery or plant` THEN `s 40(2A)(d) urgent work to be done to machinery or plant` -- input mapping
    WHEN `An interruption of work that was impossible to foresee` THEN `s 40(2A)(e) an interruption of work which it was impossible to foresee` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work in an industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore, or an essential service` THEN `s 40(2A)(f) work to be performed by employees in any industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore or any of the essential services as defined under Part 3 of the Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 40(2A) some other case` -- input mapping

-- Whether the work is one of the first five cases (a) to (e), for ss 38(8) and 40(3).
GIVEN work IS A `What the work is`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the work is one of the cases (a) to (e)` MEANS
    CONSIDER work
    WHEN `An accident, actual or threatened` THEN TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work essential to the life of the community` THEN TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work essential for defence or security` THEN TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Urgent work to be done to machinery or plant` THEN TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `An interruption of work that was impossible to foresee` THEN TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Work in an industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore, or an essential service` THEN FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Something else` THEN FALSE -- input mapping

-- The proceeding in section 47(1), from the person's choice.
GIVEN which IS A `Which proceeding`
GIVETH A `s 47(1) Insolvency proceeding`
`my proceeding in the section's words` MEANS
    CONSIDER which
    WHEN `The winding up of a company` THEN `s 47(1)(a) the winding up of a company under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` -- input mapping
    WHEN `The bankruptcy of my employer, or the distribution of the estate of an employer who died insolvent` THEN `s 47(1)(b) the distribution of the property of a bankrupt or of a person dying insolvent under section 352 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` -- input mapping
    WHEN `The winding up of a VCC, before the operative date` THEN `s 47(1)(c) the winding up of a VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date` -- input mapping
    WHEN `The winding up of a VCC, on the operative date` THEN `s 47(1)(d) the winding up of a VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date` -- input mapping
    WHEN `The winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC, before the operative date` THEN `s 47(1)(e) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date` -- input mapping
    WHEN `The winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC, on the operative date` THEN `s 47(1)(f) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Some other proceeding` THEN `s 47(1) some other proceeding` -- input mapping

-- Part 4 applies to a workman or an employee only within the salary ceilings of section 35.  The
-- Minister may substitute other ceilings; the person cannot state them, so the Act's own are used.
GIVEN workman IS A BOOLEAN
      managerial IS A BOOLEAN
      basic IS A NUMBER
      commissions IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` MEANS
    `s 35 Part 4 applies to the employee`
        (`s 35(a) the workman is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(a)` workman measure NOTHING)
        (`s 35(b) the employee is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(b)` workman managerial measure NOTHING)
    WHERE measure MEANS `s 35 the monthly salary measured against the ceiling` (`my monthly pay from my payslip` basic commissions 0) -- any allowance however described is left out of the measure (s 35), so allowances are 0 here

-- A yes/no answer of Part 4, which a person outside Part 4 does not get.
GIVEN applies IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` MEANS
    CONSIDER applies
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN answer
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Part 4 applies only to a workman earning no more than the ceiling, and to another employee, other than one in a managerial or executive position, earning no more than the lower ceiling (s 35); for anyone else the Part gives no answer
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the salary measured against the ceiling cannot be worked out from the facts given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A number from Part 4, which a person outside Part 4 does not get.
GIVEN applies IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      answer IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`if Part 4 applies to me, the number` MEANS
    CONSIDER applies
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN answer
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Part 4 applies only to a workman earning no more than the ceiling, and to another employee, other than one in a managerial or executive position, earning no more than the lower ceiling (s 35); for anyone else the Part gives no answer
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the salary measured against the ceiling cannot be worked out from the facts given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Whether a Commissioner's written order exempts the person under section 41A(1), as a plain fact.
GIVEN made IS A BOOLEAN
      covers IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`I am exempt by an order under section 41A(1)` MEANS
    (`s 41A(1) the employee is exempt from sections 38(1), (5) and (8) and 40(3)` made covers) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Whether a Commissioner's written order directs under section 41A(2) that the entitlement to extra pay does not apply.
GIVEN made IS A BOOLEAN
      covers IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an order under section 41A(2) directs that my entitlement does not apply` MEANS
    (`s 41A(2) the entitlement to be paid for extra work does not apply to the employee` made covers) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Whether section 38 is taken away from the person by section 38(9).
GIVEN fire IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 38(9) takes me out of section 38` MEANS
    (`s 38(9) section 38 applies to the employee` fire) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The kind of property or money in section 33(3), from the person's choice.
GIVEN which IS A `Which property or money`
GIVETH A `s 33(3) Kind of property or money`
`my property or money in the section's words` MEANS
    CONSIDER which
    WHEN `Property my fellow workers and I were working on` THEN `s 33(3)(a) property on which the employees were or are working` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Property that was the produce of our work` THEN `s 33(3)(b) property that was or is the produce of the work of the employees` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Movable property we used in our work` THEN `s 33(3)(c) movable property used or being used by the employees in the course of their work` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Money due to my employer for work we did` THEN `s 33(3)(d) money due to the employer in respect of work done by the employees` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Property or money of some other kind` THEN `s 33(3) property or money of some other kind` -- input mapping

§ `The Employment Act 1968 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Ending my job and changing my job (Part 2, ss 8 to 19)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 8.
@export Under section 8, is a term of my contract of service void because it is less favourable than the Act prescribes?
GIVEN `the term is in my contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the term part of your contract of service?
      `the term sets a condition of my service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term set a condition of your service, such as pay, hours, leave or notice?
      `the term is less favourable to me than the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition less favourable to you than the condition the Employment Act prescribes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8, is a term of my contract of service void` IS
    `s 8 the term is illegal and void to the extent that it is so less favourable` `the term is in my contract of service` `the term sets a condition of my service` `the term is less favourable to me than the Act`

-- s 9(1).
@export Under section 9(1), does my contract of service end when the work is done or the period has run out?
GIVEN `my contract of service is for a specified piece of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract of service for a specified piece of work?
      `the work specified in the contract has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the work specified in the contract been completed?
      `my contract of service is for a specified period of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract of service for a specified period of time?
      `the period of time for which the contract was made has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the period of time for which the contract was made expired?
      `my contract of service was otherwise terminated under Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your contract of service otherwise terminated in accordance with the provisions of Part 2 of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(1), does my contract of service terminate` IS
    `s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` `my contract of service is for a specified piece of work` `the work specified in the contract has been completed` `my contract of service is for a specified period of time` `the period of time for which the contract was made has expired` `my contract of service was otherwise terminated under Part 2`

-- s 9(2).
@export Under section 9(2), is my contract of service deemed to keep running?
GIVEN `my contract of service is for an unspecified period of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract of service for an unspecified period of time?
      `either party has terminated it under Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has either party terminated it in accordance with the provisions of Part 2 of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9(2), is my contract of service deemed to run` IS
    `s 9(2) the contract of service is deemed to run` `my contract of service is for an unspecified period of time` `either party has terminated it under Part 2`

-- s 10(1).
@export Under section 10(1), may a party to my contract of service give the other notice of intention to end it at any time?
GIVEN `I am a party to the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who would give the notice a party to the contract of service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(1), may the party give the other party notice at any time` IS
    `s 10(1) the party may at any time give the other party notice of intention to terminate the contract of service` `I am a party to the contract of service`

-- s 10(3).  Length of service is counted to the day the notice is given.
@export Under section 10(3), what is the least number of days of notice I or my employer must give?
GIVEN `the day my employment began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you start work for this employer?
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the notice given?
      `I work under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (as an employee, not as a self-employed person)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 10(3), what is the least number of days of notice` IS
    `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` (`Dates of the employment` WITH `began on` IS `the day my employment began`, `ended on` IS NOTHING) `the day the notice is given` `I work under a contract of service`

-- s 8 with s 10(2) and (3).
@export Under section 10(2), by how many days is my contract's notice term void because it is shorter than the Act's least notice?
GIVEN `the days of notice my contract says` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of notice does your contract of service say each side must give?
      `the day my employment began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you start work for this employer?
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the notice given?
      `I work under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (as an employee, not as a self-employed person)?
