    `s 10(5) the notice may be given on the day` `the day the notice is given`

-- s 10(5).
@export Under section 10(5), is the notice written?
GIVEN `the notice was given by my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given by your employer? (No if you gave it)
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given?
      `the last day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the notice?
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in writing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(5), is the notice written` IS
    `s 10(5) the notice is written` (`Notice of termination` WITH `given by` IS (IF `the notice was given by my employer` THEN `Party who is the employer` ELSE `Party who is the employee`), `given on` IS `the day the notice is given`, `last day of the notice` IS `the last day of the notice`, `in writing` IS `the notice is in writing`)

-- s 11(1).  The Third Schedule's day rate is an amount the person gives.
