@export Under section 18A(2), is the old employer's right, power, duty or liability in my contract passed to the new employer?
GIVEN `the transfer is completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer been completed?
      `the right, power, duty or liability is the transferor's under my preserved contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right, power, duty or liability the transferor's under or in connection with your contract of service preserved by section 18A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(2), is the transferor's right, power, duty or liability transferred` IS
    `s 18A(2)(a) the transferor's right, power, duty or liability is transferred to the transferee` `the transfer is completed` `the right, power, duty or liability is the transferor's under my preserved contract of service`

-- s 18A(2)(b).
@export Under section 18A(2), is an act or omission of the old employer before the transfer deemed to have been done by the new employer?
GIVEN `the transfer is completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer been completed?
      `the act or omission was done before the transfer by the transferor in respect of my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act or omission done before the transfer by the transferor in respect of your contract of service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done by the transferee` IS
    `s 18A(2)(b) the act or omission is deemed to have been done by the transferee` `the transfer is completed` `the act or omission was done before the transfer by the transferor in respect of my contract`

-- s 18A(2)(c).
@export Under section 18A(2), is an act or omission done in relation to the old employer before the transfer deemed to have been done in relation to the new employer?
GIVEN `the transfer is completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer been completed?
      `the act or omission was done before the transfer by an employee in relation to the transferor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act or omission done before the transfer by an employee employed in the undertaking or part transferred, in relation to the transferor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(2), is the act or omission deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` IS
    `s 18A(2)(c) the act or omission is deemed to have been done in relation to the transferee` `the transfer is completed` `the act or omission was done before the transfer by an employee in relation to the transferor`

@export Under section 18A(3), are my terms and conditions of service the same after the transfer?
GIVEN `the transfer is completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer been completed?
      `my contract of service is preserved under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your contract of service preserved by section 18A(1) (see the question above)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(3), are my terms and conditions of service the same after the transfer` IS
    `s 18A(3) the terms and conditions of service are the same as those enjoyed immediately prior to the transfer` `the transfer is completed` `my contract of service is preserved under subsection (1)`

-- s 18A(4).
@export Under section 18A(4), do subsections (1) and (2) transfer a liability to be prosecuted for an offence?
GIVEN `the liability is a liability to be prosecuted for, convicted of or sentenced for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability a liability to be prosecuted for, convicted of or sentenced for an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(4), do subsections (1) and (2) transfer or affect the liability` IS
    `s 18A(4) subsections (1) and (2) transfer or otherwise affect the liability` `the liability is a liability to be prosecuted for, convicted of or sentenced for an offence`

-- s 18A(5).
@export Under section 18A(5), must the transferor tell the affected employees and their trade union about the transfer?
GIVEN `a transfer under subsection (1) is to take place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a transfer under section 18A(1) to take place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(5), must the transferor notify the affected employees and their trade union` IS
    `s 18A(5) the transferor must notify the affected employees and the trade union of affected employees (if any) of the matters` `a transfer under subsection (1) is to take place`

@export Under section 18A(5), did the transferor tell the affected employees in time?
GIVEN `the day the transferor told us` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transferor tell the affected employees and their trade union about the transfer?
      `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the transfer take place?
      `it was as soon as it was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it as soon as it was reasonable to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(5), did the transferor tell the affected employees in time` IS
    `s 18A(5) the transferor notified as soon as it was reasonable and before the transfer took place` `the day the transferor told us` `the day of the transfer` `it was as soon as it was reasonable`

-- s 18A(5)(a), (b) and (c).
@export Under section 18A(5), does the notification cover all the matters it must?
GIVEN `the notification states the fact, the approximate date and the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification state the fact that the transfer is to take place, the approximate date on which it is to take place and the reasons for it?
      `the notification states the implications and the transferor's measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification state the implications of the transfer and the measures that the transferor envisages taking, or that no measures will be taken?
      `the notification states the transferee's measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification state the measures that the transferee envisages taking, or that no measures will be taken?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(5), is the notification of all the matters` IS
    `s 18A(5)(a), (b) and (c) the notification is of all the matters` `the notification states the fact, the approximate date and the reasons` `the notification states the implications and the transferor's measures` `the notification states the transferee's measures`

-- s 18A(8)(a).
@export Under section 18A(8), is my trade union deemed to be recognised by the new employer for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960?
GIVEN `the trade union was recognised by the transferor for the Industrial Relations Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trade union recognised by the transferor for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 in respect of you?
      `because of the transfer I become an employee of the transferee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, in consequence of the transfer, become an employee of the transferee?
      `most of the transferee's employees are members of the trade union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the majority of the employees employed by the transferee members of the trade union?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(8), is my trade union deemed to be recognised by the transferee` IS
    `s 18A(8)(a) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` `the trade union was recognised by the transferor for the Industrial Relations Act 1960` `because of the transfer I become an employee of the transferee` `most of the transferee's employees are members of the trade union`

-- s 18A(9).
@export Under section 18A(9), may a party refer our dispute to the Commissioner under section 115?
GIVEN `the dispute is between the transferor and an employee, or the transferee and an employee, and arises from the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute or disagreement between the transferor and an employee, or the transferee and an employee, and does it arise from a transfer under section 18A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(9), may a party refer the dispute to the Commissioner` IS
    `s 18A(9) a party may refer the dispute to the Commissioner under section 115, and it is deemed to be a dispute to which that section applies` `the dispute is between the transferor and an employee, or the transferee and an employee, and arises from the transfer`

-- s 18A(12).
@export Under section 18A(12), may the new employer and I negotiate terms of service different from those of my preserved contract?
GIVEN `the parties are the transferee and an employee with a preserved contract, or a trade union representing that employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the parties the transferee and an employee whose contract of service is preserved under section 18A(1), or the transferee and a trade union representing such an employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 18A(12), may the parties negotiate different terms of service` IS
    `s 18A(12) the parties may negotiate for and agree to terms of service different from those of the preserved contract of service` `the parties are the transferee and an employee with a preserved contract, or a trade union representing that employee`

@export Under section 18A(8A), until what date does my union's collective agreement continue with the new employer?
GIVEN `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transfer take place?
      `the date the collective agreement expires` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the collective agreement expire? (1 January 1900 if it does not say)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 18A(8A), until what date does the collective agreement continue` IS
    `s 18A(8A) the last day on which the collective agreement continues in force between the transferee and the trade union` `the day of the transfer` (`my date if there is one` `the date the collective agreement expires`)

-- s 19 is the employer's offence; for the employee it is what the Act makes of an employer who
-- enters into a contract contrary to Part 2.
@export Under section 19, is my employer guilty of an offence for making a contract of service contrary to Part 2?
GIVEN `my employer made the contract or collective agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer enter into the contract of service or collective agreement?
      `it is contrary to Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it contrary to the rules on contracts of service in Part 2 of the Act (ss 8 to 19)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 19, is my employer guilty of an offence` IS
    `s 19 the employer is guilty of an offence` `my employer made the contract or collective agreement` `it is contrary to Part 2`
-- s 19.  The Act points to section 112 for the penalty, and that section is not among the sources, so this question answers NOTHING whatever the facts.
@export Under section 19, what is the penalty on my employer on conviction?
GIVEN `my employer has been convicted of an offence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer been convicted of an offence before?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 19, what is the penalty on conviction` IS
    `s 19 the penalty on conviction` NOTHING NOTHING `my employer has been convicted of an offence before`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Being paid (Part 3, ss 20 to 34)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 20(2).
@export Under section 20(2), does my salary period exceed one month?
GIVEN `the first day of my salary period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your salary period?
      `the last day of my salary period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your salary period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20(2), does my salary period stay within one month` IS
    `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` (`Period of days` WITH `first day` IS `the first day of my salary period`, `last day` IS `the last day of my salary period`)

-- s 20(3).
@export Under section 20(3), is my salary period deemed to be one month?
GIVEN `my employer has fixed a salary period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer fixed a salary period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20(3), is my salary period deemed to be one month` IS
    `s 20(3) the salary period is deemed to be one month` `my employer has fixed a salary period`

-- s 20A(1).  Situation: asked only of a monthly-rated employee who has not worked a whole month.
-- The form can ask "Did you work less than a whole month?" before showing this group.
@export Under section 20A(1), is my salary for the month to be worked out by the formula for an incomplete month?
GIVEN `I am paid by the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your salary fixed by the month?
      `why I did not work the whole month` IS A `Why I did not work the whole month` @desc Why did you not work the whole month?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20A(1), is my salary for the month worked out by the formula` IS
    `s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` `I am paid by the month` (`why I did not work the whole month` EQUALS `I started work after the first day of the month`) (`why I did not work the whole month` EQUALS `My employment ended before the end of the month`) (`why I did not work the whole month` EQUALS `I took unpaid leave for one or more days of the month`) (`why I did not work the whole month` EQUALS `I took leave to perform my national service`)

-- s 20A(1) and (2).  Basic pay, commissions and other allowances make the gross rate of pay (s 2(1));
-- overtime, bonus and the other items it leaves out are 0 here.
@export Under section 20A, how much salary is due to me for a month in which I did not work the whole month, in dollars?
GIVEN `my basic pay for a whole month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a whole month, in dollars, before overtime, bonuses and allowances?
      `my commissions for a whole month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions would you earn for a whole month, in dollars?
      `my other allowances for a whole month` IS A NUMBER @desc What allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances would you get for a whole month, in dollars?
      `the days I am required to work in the month` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in the month are you required to work?
      `the days I worked more than 5 hours` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days of the month did you actually work, on days when you were required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days I worked 5 hours or less` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days of the month did you actually work, on days when you were required to work for 5 hours or less?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 20A, how much salary is due to me for the month` IS
    `s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` (`my monthly pay from my payslip` `my basic pay for a whole month` `my commissions for a whole month` `my other allowances for a whole month`) `the days I am required to work in the month` (`s 20A(2) the number of days actually worked` `the days I worked more than 5 hours` `the days I worked 5 hours or less`)

-- s 21(1).  Public holidays can move the last day: give up to two (1 January 1900 for none).
@export Under section 21(1), by what day must my salary be paid?
GIVEN `the last day of my salary period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your salary period?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after the end of your salary period? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 21(1), by what day must my salary be paid` IS
    `s 21(1) the last day before the expiry of which the salary must be paid` `the last day of my salary period` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

@export Under section 21(1), was my salary paid in time?
GIVEN `the last day of my salary period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your salary period?
      `the day my salary was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your salary paid?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after the end of your salary period? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `it was a payment for overtime work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment an additional payment for overtime work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 21(1), was my salary paid in time` IS
    `s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` `the last day of my salary period` `the day my salary was paid` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`) `it was a payment for overtime work`

-- s 21(2).
@export Under section 21(2), by what day must my payments for overtime be paid?
GIVEN `the last day of the salary period in which I worked the overtime` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the salary period in which you worked the overtime?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 21(2), by what day must my payments for overtime be paid` IS
    `s 21(2) the last day by which the additional payments for overtime work must be paid` `the last day of the salary period in which I worked the overtime` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 21(2).
@export Under section 21(2), were my payments for overtime paid in time?
GIVEN `the last day of the salary period in which I worked the overtime` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the salary period in which you worked the overtime?
      `the day my payments for overtime were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date were your additional payments for overtime paid?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 21(2), were my payments for overtime paid in time` IS
    `s 21(2) the additional payments for overtime work were paid not later than 14 days after the last day of the salary period` `the last day of the salary period in which I worked the overtime` `the day my payments for overtime were paid` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 21(3).
@export Under section 21(3), was my total salary paid to me when my contract of service was completed?
GIVEN `the day my contract of service was completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your contract of service completed?
      `the day my total salary was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your total salary paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 21(3), was my total salary paid when my contract was completed` IS
    `s 21(3) the total salary due was paid on completion of the contract of service` `the day my contract of service was completed` `the day my total salary was paid`

-- s 22.  Situation: asked only of a person who has been dismissed.
-- The form can ask "Have you been dismissed?" before showing this group.
@export Under section 22, by what day must I be paid if I have been dismissed?
GIVEN `the day I was dismissed` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you dismissed?
      `it was not possible to pay me that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it not possible for your employer to pay you on the day you were dismissed?
      `the first rest day or holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first rest day, public holiday or other holiday in the three days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second rest day or holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second rest day, public holiday or other holiday in those three days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the third rest day or holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the third rest day, public holiday or other holiday in those three days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 22, by what day must I be paid after dismissal` IS
    `s 22 the last day on which the total salary and any sum due must be paid` `the day I was dismissed` `it was not possible to pay me that day` (`my days off` `the first rest day or holiday after that day` `the second rest day or holiday after that day` `the third rest day or holiday after that day`)

-- s 22.
@export Under section 22, was I paid in time after I was dismissed?
GIVEN `the day I was dismissed` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you dismissed?
      `the day my total salary and any sum due was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date were your total salary and any sum due paid to you?
      `it was not possible to pay me that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it not possible for your employer to pay you on the day you were dismissed?
      `the first rest day or holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first rest day, public holiday or other holiday in the three days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second rest day or holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second rest day, public holiday or other holiday in those three days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the third rest day or holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the third rest day, public holiday or other holiday in those three days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22, was I paid in time after I was dismissed` IS
    `s 22 the total salary and any sum due was paid on the day of dismissal or, if that was not possible, within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday` `the day I was dismissed` `the day my total salary and any sum due was paid` `it was not possible to pay me that day` (`my days off` `the first rest day or holiday after that day` `the second rest day or holiday after that day` `the third rest day or holiday after that day`)

-- s 23(1) and (2).  Situation: asked only of a person who has ended their own contract of service.
-- The form can ask "Did you end your contract of service?" before showing this group.
@export Under section 23(1), was my total salary paid on the day my contract of service ended, when I ended it with due notice?
GIVEN `I ended it under section 11 or after giving due notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you end your contract of service under section 11 or after giving your employer the due notice that section 10 requires?
      `the day my contract of service ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your contract of service end?
      `the day my total salary was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your total salary paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(1), was my total salary paid on the day my contract ended` IS
    `s 23(1) the total salary due was paid on the day on which the contract of service was terminated` `I ended it under section 11 or after giving due notice` `the day my contract of service ended` `the day my total salary was paid`

@export Under section 23(2), was my total salary paid in time when I left without notice or without waiting for the notice to run out?
GIVEN `I left without notice or did not wait for the notice to expire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave without giving the notice section 10 requires, or without waiting for the notice to expire?
      `the day I ended my contract of service` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you end your contract of service?
      `the day my total salary was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your total salary paid?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after you ended your contract? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23(2), was my total salary paid in time` IS
    `s 23(2) the total salary due was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the day on which the employee terminated the contract of service` `I left without notice or did not wait for the notice to expire` `the day I ended my contract of service` `the day my total salary was paid` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 23(2).  Public holidays can move the last day: give up to two (1 January 1900 for none).
@export Under section 23(2), by what date must my total salary be paid when I leave without notice or without waiting for the notice to run out?
GIVEN `the day I ended my contract of service` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you end your contract of service?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 23(2), by what date must my total salary be paid` IS
    `s 23(2) the last day before the expiry of which the total salary due must be paid` `the day I ended my contract of service` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

@export Under section 23(3), what is the most my employer may deduct from my salary for the notice I did not give?
GIVEN `a court or the Commissioner has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court or the Commissioner made an order to the contrary?
      `the sum I am liable to pay in place of notice` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum, in dollars, are you liable to pay in place of notice under section 11(1)? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 23(3), what is the most my employer may deduct for the notice I did not give` IS
    `s 23(3) the most the employer may deduct from the salary due to the employee` `a court or the Commissioner has ordered otherwise` (`my amount if I know it` `the sum I am liable to pay in place of notice`)

-- s 24.
@export Under section 24(1), may my employer pay me the salary and other sums due on the end of my service without the Comptroller of Income Tax's permission?
GIVEN `the Comptroller has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Comptroller of Income Tax given permission under section 68(7) of the Income Tax Act 1947 for payment to be made to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(1), may my employer pay me without the Comptroller's permission` IS
    `s 24(1) payment of the salary or other sum due on termination of service is to be made to the employee by the employer` `the Comptroller has given permission`

@export Under section 24(2), by what day must the salary and other sums due to me be paid after the Comptroller has been told?
GIVEN `the day the Comptroller received notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Comptroller of Income Tax receive notice that your service ended?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 24(2), by what day must I be paid after the Comptroller has been told` IS
    `s 24(2) the last day by which the payment of the salary or other sum due must be made` `the day the Comptroller received notice` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 24(2).
@export Under section 24(2), was my payment delayed more than 30 days after the Comptroller was told?
GIVEN `the day the Comptroller received notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Comptroller of Income Tax receive notice that your service ended?
      `the day my salary or other sum was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your salary or other sum due paid?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(2), was my payment delayed no more than 30 days` IS
    `s 24(2) the payment was not delayed more than 30 days after the notice was given to and received by the Comptroller` `the day the Comptroller received notice` `the day my salary or other sum was paid` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 25.
@export Under section 25(1), was my salary paid on a working day, during working hours, at my place of work or an agreed place?
GIVEN `it was a working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your salary paid on a working day?
      `it was during working hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it paid during working hours?
      `it was at my place of work or an agreed place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it paid at your place of work, or at another place agreed between you and your employer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(1), was my salary paid on a working day, in working hours, at the right place` IS
    `s 25(1) the payment of salary was made on a working day and during working hours at the place of work or at an agreed place` `it was a working day` `it was during working hours` `it was at my place of work or an agreed place`

@export Under section 25(2), does section 25(1) apply to my salary, which is paid into a bank account?
GIVEN `my salary is paid into a bank account in Singapore in my name or jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your salary paid into an account with a bank in Singapore, in your name or jointly with one or more other people?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(2), does section 25(1) apply to my salary` IS
    `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the payment of the salary` `my salary is paid into a bank account in Singapore in my name or jointly`

-- s 26.
@export Under section 26(1), may my employer make this deduction from my salary?
GIVEN `the Act authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the deduction authorised by or under a provision of the Employment Act?
      `a court or authority orders it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it required by an order of a court or other authority competent to make the order?
      `a tax comptroller's declaration requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it required pursuant to a declaration of the Comptroller of Income Tax, Property Tax or Goods and Services Tax that your employer is an agent for recovery of tax you owe?
      `the Comptroller of Income Tax directs it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it required pursuant to a direction of the Comptroller of Income Tax under section 91 of the Income Tax Act 1947?
      `a MediShield Life recovery body declares it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it required pursuant to a declaration of a MediShield Life Scheme recovery body that your employer is an agent for recovery of an outstanding premium you owe?
      `a CareShield Life recovery body declares it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it required pursuant to a declaration of a CSHL Scheme recovery body that your employer is an agent for recovery of an outstanding premium you owe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26(1), may my employer make this deduction` IS
    `s 26(1) the employer may make the deduction from the salary of the employee` `the Act authorises it` `a court or authority orders it` `a tax comptroller's declaration requires it` `the Comptroller of Income Tax directs it` `a MediShield Life recovery body declares it` `a CareShield Life recovery body declares it`

-- s 27.
@export Under section 27(1), is this deduction one that may be made from my salary?
GIVEN `which deduction` IS A `Which deduction` @desc What is the deduction for?
      `I gave my consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your written consent to the deduction?
      `I withdrew my consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your employer written notice withdrawing your consent before the deduction was made?
      `it is my neglect or default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the deduction is for damage or loss: is the damage or loss directly attributable to your neglect or default?
      `the Commissioner has authorised the amenity or service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is for an amenity or service: has the Commissioner authorised it?
      `it is for my CPF contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is for contributions: are they payable under and in accordance with the Central Provident Fund Act 1953?
      `it is paid to a cooperative society` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is paid to a cooperative society: is it for subscriptions, entrance fees, instalments of loans, interest or other dues you owe the society?
      `regulations prescribe it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the deduction is of a kind prescribed by regulations: do the regulations prescribe it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(1), is this deduction one that may be made` IS
    `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` (`my kind of deduction in the section's words` `which deduction`) ((`s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` (`my kind of deduction in the section's words` `which deduction`) `I gave my consent in writing` `I withdrew my consent in writing`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `it is my neglect or default` `the Commissioner has authorised the amenity or service` `it is for my CPF contributions` `it is paid to a cooperative society` `regulations prescribe it`

@export Under section 27(1B), can I be penalised for withdrawing my written consent to a deduction?
GIVEN `which deduction` IS A `Which deduction` @desc What was the deduction for?
      `I withdrew my consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw your written consent to the deduction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(1B), can I be penalised for withdrawing my consent` IS
    `s 27(1B) the employee can be penalised for withdrawing the written consent` (`my kind of deduction in the section's words` `which deduction`) `I withdrew my consent in writing`

-- s 27(2).
@export Under section 27(2), is my employer's supply of tools and raw materials a service for the purposes of section 27(1)(e)?
GIVEN `the supply is of tools and raw materials required for the purposes of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supply of tools and raw materials required for the purposes of your employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(2), is the supply a service` IS
    `s 27(2) the supply is a service for the purposes of subsection (1)(e)` `the supply is of tools and raw materials required for the purposes of my employment`

-- s 27(3).
@export Under section 27(3), is this thing an employment benefit?
GIVEN `the thing is a benefit I derive from being employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a benefit that you derive from being employed?
      `the thing is salary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing salary?
      `the thing is annual leave beyond what section 88A gives me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which you are entitled under section 88A?
      `the thing is a flexible employment benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a flexible employment benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27(3), is the thing an employment benefit` IS
    `s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` `the thing is a benefit I derive from being employed` `the thing is salary` `the thing is annual leave beyond what section 88A gives me` `the thing is a flexible employment benefit`

-- s 27(3)(b)(i).  The days of paid annual leave are the answer of section 88A, which the person gives (seam S4).
@export Under section 27(3)(b)(i), how many days of annual leave did my employer give me beyond what section 88A entitles me to?
GIVEN `the days of annual leave my employer gave me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of annual leave did your employer give you?
      `the days of paid annual leave section 88A entitles me to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of paid annual leave does section 88A entitle you to? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 27(3)(b)(i), how many days of annual leave beyond section 88A did I get` IS
    `s 27(3)(b)(i) the days of annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which the employee is entitled under section 88A` `the days of annual leave my employer gave me` (`my amount if I know it` `the days of paid annual leave section 88A entitles me to`)

-- s 28.
@export Under section 28(1), may my employer deduct from my salary for my absence?
GIVEN `I was absent from where I am required to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you absent from the place where, by the terms of your employment, you are required to work?
      `the absence was in the time I am required to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the absence for the whole or any part of the period during which you are required to work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 28(1), may my employer deduct from my salary for my absence` IS
    `s 28(1) a deduction under section 27(1)(a) may be made on account of the absence` `I was absent from where I am required to work` `the absence was in the time I am required to work`

@export Under section 28(2), what is the most my employer may deduct from my salary for my absence, in dollars?
GIVEN `I am paid by the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your salary fixed by the month?
      `the days I was absent` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days were you absent?
      `my gross rate of pay for one day` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are paid by the month: what is your gross rate of pay for one day's work, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
      `my salary at the gross rate of pay for the salary period` IS A NUMBER @desc What salary, in dollars, is payable to you at the gross rate of pay for the salary period?
      `the total days I was required to work in the salary period` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in the salary period were you required to work?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 28(2), what is the most my employer may deduct for my absence` IS
    `s 28(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(a)` `I am paid by the month` `the days I was absent` (`my amount if I know it` `my gross rate of pay for one day`) `my salary at the gross rate of pay for the salary period` `the days I was absent` `the total days I was required to work in the salary period`

@export Under section 28(3), may my employer deduct the cost of food supplied to me while I was absent from work?
GIVEN `I was absent otherwise than as the Act or my contract allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you absent from work otherwise than as the Act or your contract of service allows?
      `a court or the Commissioner has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court or the Commissioner made an order to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 28(3), may my employer deduct the cost of food supplied to me while I was absent` IS
    `s 28(3) the employer may deduct from salary due the cost of food supplied during the absence` `I was absent otherwise than as the Act or my contract allows` `a court or the Commissioner has ordered otherwise`

-- s 29.  The one-quarter figure is the Act's own; a substitution by the Minister would change the answer.
@export Under section 29(1), what is the most my employer may deduct from my salary for damage or loss I caused, in dollars?
GIVEN `the damages or loss I caused` IS A NUMBER @desc What damages or loss, in dollars, did your neglect or default cause your employer?
      `one month's wages` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your wages for one month, in dollars?
      `the Commissioner has permitted more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner permitted a larger deduction?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 29(1), what is the most my employer may deduct for damage or loss I caused` IS
    `s 29(1) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(b)` `the damages or loss I caused` `one month's wages` `the Commissioner has permitted more` NOTHING

@export Under section 29(1), may my employer make the deduction for damage or loss now?
GIVEN `I have been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 29(1), may my employer make the deduction for damage or loss now` IS
    `s 29(1) the deduction under section 27(1)(b) may be made now` `I have been given an opportunity of showing cause`

-- s 29(1).  The bar as a question of its own: the deduction may not be made until the employee has been given the opportunity.
@export Under section 29(1), is my employer still barred from making the deduction for damage or loss?
GIVEN `I have been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been given an opportunity of showing cause against the deduction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 29(1), is my employer barred from making the deduction for damage or loss` IS
    `s 29(1) the bar on making the deduction under section 27(1)(b) applies` `I have been given an opportunity of showing cause`

-- s 30.
@export Under section 30(2), what is the most my employer may deduct from my salary for accommodation, an amenity or a service, in dollars?
GIVEN `the value of what my employer supplied` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in dollars, of the house accommodation, amenity or service your employer supplied?
      `deductions already made for these in the salary period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has already been deducted for house accommodation, amenities and services in the salary period, in dollars?
      `my salary payable for the salary period` IS A NUMBER @desc What salary, in dollars, is payable to you for the salary period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
