      `my contract fixes work on 5 days or fewer in a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract of service require you to work on no more than 5 days in a week?
      `I am engaged in the fire services or in work with long hours of stand-by` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged in the fire services, or in work which by its nature involves long hours of inactive or stand-by employment?
      `the Commissioner has made a written order about my hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner made a written order, after considering your employer's operational needs and your health and safety, exempting you or your class of employees from the daily and weekly limits?
      `that order covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that order cover you?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 38(1), what is the limit of hours in one day` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the number` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 38(1) the limit of hours in one day` `my contract fixes fewer than 8 hours on one or more days of the week` `my contract fixes work on 5 days or fewer in a week` (`section 38(9) takes me out of section 38` `I am engaged in the fire services or in work with long hours of stand-by`) (`I am exempt by an order under section 41A(1)` `the Commissioner has made a written order about my hours` `that order covers me`))

