    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 38(9) section 38 applies to the employee` `I am engaged in the fire services or in work with long hours of stand-by`)

-- s 39.
@export Under section 39, may my employer agree with me that I be paid by the task?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the agreement is that I am paid an agreed rate for the task, the specific amount of work required, and not by the day or by the piece` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement that you are paid an agreed rate for the task, the specific amount of work required to be performed, and not by the day or by the piece?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39, does this Part prevent my employer from agreeing that I be paid by the task` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 39 this Part prevents the employer from agreeing that the salary be paid by the task` `the agreement is that I am paid an agreed rate for the task, the specific amount of work required, and not by the day or by the piece`)

-- s 40(1).  Situation: asked only of a person in regular shift work.
@export Under section 40(1), does section 40 apply to me?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `I am engaged under my contract in regular shift work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged under your contract of service in regular shift work?
      `I have otherwise consented in writing to the hours of work in section 40` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you otherwise consented in writing to work in accordance with the hours of work specified in section 40?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(1), does section 40 apply to me` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 40(1) section 40 applies to the employee` `I am engaged under my contract in regular shift work` `I have otherwise consented in writing to the hours of work in section 40`)

-- s 40(1).
@export Under section 40(1), what is the limit of hours in one week?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `I am engaged under my contract in regular shift work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged under your contract of service in regular shift work?
      `I have otherwise consented in writing to the hours of work in section 40` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you otherwise consented in writing to work in accordance with the hours of work specified in section 40?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
