    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 40(1) the average number of hours worked per week over the 3 weeks is within the limit` `the total hours I worked over the 3 continuous weeks`)

-- s 40(2).
@export Under section 40(2), is the consent I gave for the hours of work in section 40 valid?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
