    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 40(2) the consent given by the employee under this section is valid` `I gave consent in writing` `section 40 and section 38 were explained to me` `I was told the times my hours begin and end` `I was told the number of working days in each week` `I was told my weekly rest day`)

-- s 40(2A).
@export Under section 40(2A), may my employer require me to exceed the weekly limit and work on a rest day because of the work to be done?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `I am engaged under my contract in regular shift work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged under your contract of service in regular shift work?
      `I have otherwise consented in writing to the hours of work in section 40` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you otherwise consented in writing to work in accordance with the hours of work specified in section 40?
      `the work I am asked to do` IS A `What the work is` @desc What kind of work are you asked to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(2A), may my employer require me to exceed the limit of hours and work on a rest day` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 40(2A) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` (`my case under section 40(2A)` `the work I am asked to do`) (`s 40(1) section 40 applies to the employee` `I am engaged under my contract in regular shift work` `I have otherwise consented in writing to the hours of work in section 40`))

-- s 40(3).
@export Under section 40(3), may I work this many hours in the day?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the hours I work in the day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours do you work in the day?
      `the work I am asked to do` IS A `What the work is` @desc What kind of work are you asked to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(3), may I work this many hours in the day` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 40(3) the employee may work the hours in the day` `the hours I work in the day` (`the work is one of the cases (a) to (e)` `the work I am asked to do`))

-- s 40(4).
@export Under section 40(4), what is the least payment due to me for the extra work over the 3 weeks at my employer's request, in dollars?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the total hours I worked over the 3 continuous weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you work in all over the 3 continuous weeks?
      `my hourly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your hourly basic rate of pay, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
      `I work the extra hours at my employer's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work the extra hours at your employer's request?
      `a written order says the entitlement to extra pay does not apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written order of the Commissioner under section 41A(2) direct that your entitlement to be paid for extra work does not apply to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 40(4), what is the least payment due for the extra work` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the number` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 40(4) the least payment for the extra work` `the total hours I worked over the 3 continuous weeks` (`my amount if I know it` `my hourly basic rate of pay`) `I work the extra hours at my employer's request` `a written order says the entitlement to extra pay does not apply to me`)

-- s 41.  In sections 36, 38 and 40 a "week" is a continuous period of 7 days commencing at midnight on Sunday; one question gives its first day and the next its last.
@export Under section 41, on what date does the week that holds this day begin?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc Which date do you want the week for?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 41, on what date does the week begin` IS
    (`s 41 the week that holds the day` `the day`)'s `first day`

@export Under section 41, on what date does the week that holds this day end?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc Which date do you want the week for?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 41, on what date does the week end` IS
    (`s 41 the week that holds the day` `the day`)'s `last day`

-- s 41A(1).  The order is the Commissioner's; the question is what it means to the person.
@export Under section 41A(1), am I exempt from the daily limit, the overtime cap and the limit on daily hours by a written order of the Commissioner?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the Commissioner has made a written order about my hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner made a written order, after considering your employer's operational needs and your health and safety, exempting you or your class of employees?
      `that order covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that order cover you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41A(1), am I exempt from sections 38(1), (5) and (8) and 40(3)` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 41A(1) the employee is exempt from sections 38(1), (5) and (8) and 40(3)` `the Commissioner has made a written order about my hours` `that order covers me`)

-- s 41A(2).
@export Under section 41A(2), does the entitlement to be paid for extra work not apply to me by a written order of the Commissioner?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the Commissioner has made a written order about extra pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner made a written order, after considering your employer's operational needs and your interests, directing that the entitlement to be paid for extra work does not apply to you or your class of employees?
      `that order about extra pay covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that order cover you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41A(2), does my entitlement to be paid for extra work not apply` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 41A(2) the entitlement to be paid for extra work does not apply to the employee` `the Commissioner has made a written order about extra pay` `that order about extra pay covers me`)

-- s 41A(3).  The duty as a yes/no question; the deontic in layer 1 carries the same rule.
@export Under section 41A(3), must my employer display the Commissioner's order where I work?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the Commissioner has made an order that exempts me or says my entitlement does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner exempted you under section 41A(1), or directed under section 41A(2) that your entitlement does not apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41A(3), must my employer display the order` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 41A(3) the employer must display the order` `the Commissioner has made an order that exempts me or says my entitlement does not apply`)

-- s 41A(3).
@export Under section 41A(3), has my employer displayed the Commissioner's order where I work?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the Commissioner has made an order that exempts me or says my entitlement does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner exempted you under section 41A(1), or directed under section 41A(2) that your entitlement does not apply?
      `the order or a copy is displayed conspicuously where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order, or a copy of it, displayed conspicuously in the place where you are employed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41A(3), has my employer displayed the order` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 41A(3) the employer has displayed the order` `the Commissioner has made an order that exempts me or says my entitlement does not apply` `the order or a copy is displayed conspicuously where I work`)


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Retrenchment, retirement, gratuities and annual wage supplements (Part 4, ss 45 to 53)`
-- These sections are in Part 4, so each question asks the five facts that decide whether Part 4 reaches the person (s 35).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 45.  Situation: asked only of a person who has been dismissed.
@export Under section 45, am I entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the day my continuous service with my employer began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your continuous service with your employer begin?
      `the day I was dismissed` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you dismissed?
      `I was dismissed for redundancy or reorganisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed on the ground of redundancy, or by reason of a reorganisation of your employer's profession, business, trade or work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 45, am I entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 45 the employee is entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` `the day my continuous service with my employer began` `the day I was dismissed` `I was dismissed for redundancy or reorganisation`)

-- s 46.  Situation: asked only of a person whose service has ceased.
@export Under section 46, am I entitled to a retirement benefit on the end of my service?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the day my continuous service with my employer began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your continuous service with your employer begin?
      `the day my service ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your service with your employer end?
      `the benefit is a retirement benefit other than sums payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit a retirement benefit, other than the sums payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46, am I entitled to a retirement benefit on the end of my service` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 46 the employee is entitled to a retirement benefit on the cessation of service` `the day my continuous service with my employer began` `the day my service ended` `the benefit is a retirement benefit other than sums payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`)

-- s 47(1).  Situation: asked only of a person whose employer is being wound up or is bankrupt, or has died insolvent.
@export Under section 47(1), is the gratuity or sum I am owed among the debts to be paid in priority?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the proceeding` IS A `Which proceeding` @desc In which proceeding are you owed the gratuity?
      `a collective agreement or an award provides for a gratuity or other sum on retirement or termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a collective agreement or an award provide for the payment of a gratuity or other sum of money to you on retirement or on the termination of your services?
      `the gratuity or sum is due and owing to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the gratuity or other sum of money due and owing to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 47(1), is the gratuity or sum I am owed included among the debts to be paid in priority` IS
    `if Part 4 applies to me, the yes or no` (`Part 4 applies to me from what I say` `I am a workman` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `my basic pay for a month` `my commissions for a month`) (`s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` (`my proceeding in the section's words` `the proceeding`) `a collective agreement or an award provides for a gratuity or other sum on retirement or termination` `the gratuity or sum is due and owing to me`)

-- s 47(1).
@export Under section 47(1), does the gratuity or sum I am owed rank after the preferential debts?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (a person doing manual labour, and the other kinds the Act names)?
      `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `my basic pay for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for a month, in dollars, before overtime and bonuses?
      `my commissions for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What commissions do you earn in a month, in dollars?
      `the proceeding` IS A `Which proceeding` @desc In which proceeding are you owed the gratuity?
