-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Salary owed by a contractor: the principal's liability (Part 6, ss 65 and 66)`
-- Situation: asked only of a workman whose employer is a contractor or subcontractor.
-- The form can ask "Does your employer work for another business as a contractor?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 65.
@export Under section 65, is the principal liable to pay me my salary?
GIVEN `a principal contracted with my employer's contractor for the supply of labour or for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a principal, in the course of or for the purposes of its trade or business, contract with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by or under the contractor of the whole or any part of any work undertaken by the principal?
      `salary is due to me by the contractor or a subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is salary due to you, a workman, by the contractor or a subcontractor under the contractor, for labour supplied or for work done in the course of that work?
      `the contract is for constructional work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract for constructional work?
      `the principal is also a constructional contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the principal also a constructional contractor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65, is the principal liable to pay my salary` IS
    `s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` `a principal contracted with my employer's contractor for the supply of labour or for work` `salary is due to me by the contractor or a subcontractor` `the contract is for constructional work` `the principal is also a constructional contractor`

-- s 65(1).
@export Under section 65(1), is the contractor or a subcontractor, who is not my employer, jointly and severally liable with my employer to pay me?
GIVEN `a principal contracted with my employer's contractor for the supply of labour or for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a principal, in the course of or for the purposes of its trade or business, contract with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by or under the contractor of the whole or any part of any work undertaken by the principal?
      `salary is due to me by the contractor or a subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is salary due to you, a workman, by the contractor or a subcontractor under the contractor, for labour supplied or for work done in the course of that work?
      `the person is my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you are asking about your employer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(1), is the contractor or subcontractor jointly and severally liable with my employer` IS
    `s 65(1) the contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is jointly and severally liable with the employer to pay the workman` `a principal contracted with my employer's contractor for the supply of labour or for work` `salary is due to me by the contractor or a subcontractor` `the person is my employer`

-- s 65(1).
@export Under section 65(1), what salary can I claim from the principal, in dollars?
GIVEN `the salary of mine under my own employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the salary, in dollars, of yours under the employer by whom you are immediately employed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 65(1), what salary can I claim from the principal` IS
    `s 65(1) the salary claimed from the principal` `the salary of mine under my own employer`

-- s 65(1A).
@export Under section 65(1A), what is the most a principal, contractor or subcontractor who is not my employer is liable for, in dollars?
GIVEN `the person is my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you are asking about your employer?
      `the salary due` IS A NUMBER @desc What salary, in dollars, is due to you?
      `the salary I earn in one month for work done by my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What salary, in dollars, do you earn in one month for work done for your employer?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 65(1A), what is the most the principal or contractor is liable for` IS
    `s 65(1A) the most a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is liable for` `the person is my employer` `the salary due` `the salary I earn in one month for work done by my employer`

-- s 65(1).  The sentence takes section 33, the priority of salary, out of the Act that applies to a claim on the principal.
@export Under section 65(1), does section 33 on the priority of salary apply to my salary claimed from the principal?
GIVEN `my salary is claimed from the principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the salary claimed from the principal (and not from the employer)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(1), does section 33 on the priority of salary apply to my salary claimed from the principal` IS
    `s 65(1) section 33 relating to priority of salary applies to the salary claimed from the principal` `my salary is claimed from the principal`

-- s 65(2).
@export Under section 65(2), may I lodge a claim for the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016?
GIVEN `I wish to recover salary from a person liable under section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to recover salary from a person liable under section 65?
      `I submitted a mediation request to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you submitted to the Commissioner, under section 3(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016, a mediation request for the mediation under Part 2 of that Act of every dispute for which the claim will be lodged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(2), may I lodge the claim for the salary` IS
    `s 65(2) the workman may lodge the claim for the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016` `I wish to recover salary from a person liable under section 65` `I submitted a mediation request to the Commissioner`

-- s 65(2A).  Public holidays can move the last day: give up to two (1 January 1900 for none).
@export Under section 65(2A), by what date must I submit the mediation request?
GIVEN `the day my salary becomes due for payment under Part 3` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your salary become due for payment in accordance with Part 3?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 65(2A), by what date must I submit the mediation request` IS
    `s 65(2A) the last day for submitting the mediation request` `the day my salary becomes due for payment under Part 3` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 65(2A) and (2B).
@export Under section 65(2A), did I submit the mediation request within 60 days after my salary became due?
GIVEN `the day my salary becomes due for payment under Part 3` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your salary become due for payment in accordance with Part 3?
      `the day I submitted the mediation request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you submit the mediation request to the Commissioner?
      `the last day the Commissioner extended the period to` IS A DATE @desc If the Commissioner extended the period, to what date? (1 January 1900 if not extended)
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after the date your salary became due? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(2A), did I submit the mediation request in time` IS
    `s 65(2A) the mediation request was submitted within 60 days after the date on which the salary becomes due for payment` `the day my salary becomes due for payment under Part 3` `the day I submitted the mediation request` (`my date if there is one` `the last day the Commissioner extended the period to`) (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 65(2B).
@export Under section 65(2B), by what date must I submit the mediation request if the Commissioner extended the period?
GIVEN `the day my salary becomes due for payment under Part 3` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your salary become due for payment in accordance with Part 3?
      `the last day the Commissioner extended the period to` IS A DATE @desc To what date did the Commissioner extend the period? (1 January 1900 if not extended)
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after the date your salary became due? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 65(2B), by what date must I submit the mediation request as extended` IS
    `s 65(2B) the last day for submitting the mediation request as extended` (`s 65(2A) the last day for submitting the mediation request` `the day my salary becomes due for payment under Part 3` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)) (`my date if there is one` `the last day the Commissioner extended the period to`)

-- s 65(2C).
@export Under section 65(2C)(a), do subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) apply to my claim for salary?
GIVEN `I lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lodge a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under section 65?
      `the day I lodged the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you lodge the claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(2C)(a), do subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) apply to my claim` IS
    `s 65(2C)(a) subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` `I lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under section 65` `the day I lodged the claim`

-- s 65(2C).
@export Under section 65(2C)(b), do the old rules in force before 1 April 2017 still apply to my claim for salary?
GIVEN `I lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lodge a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under section 65?
      `the day I lodged the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you lodge the claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(2C)(b), do the old rules still apply to my claim` IS
    `s 65(2C)(b) the repealed section 65(1C) and (2) as in force immediately before 1 April 2017 continue to apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` `I lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under section 65` `the day I lodged the claim`

-- s 65(3).
@export Under section 65(3), does section 65 prevent a person who paid my salary from suing my employer to get it back?
GIVEN `the person paid salary to a workman as the result of a claim under section 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, who as the result of a claim made under section 65 has paid salary to a workman?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(3), does the section prevent the person from suing the employer` IS
    `s 65(3) this section prevents the person from instituting civil proceedings against the employer for the recovery of the salary paid` `the person paid salary to a workman as the result of a claim under section 65`

-- s 65(4).
@export Under section 65(4), does section 65 prevent me from recovering my salary from my employer instead?
GIVEN `I recover salary from my employer instead of the principal or contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you recover salary under the Employment Act from your employer instead of the principal, contractor or subcontractor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(4), does the section prevent me from recovering from my employer instead` IS
    `s 65(4) this section prevents the workman from recovering salary from the employer instead` `I recover salary from my employer instead of the principal or contractor`

-- s 65(5).
@export Under section 65(5), is the Government or a statutory body a principal for the purposes of section 65?
GIVEN `the person is the Government or a statutory body or authority acting in the discharge of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Government or a statutory body or authority acting in the course of or in the discharge of its functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(5), is the person a principal` IS
    `s 65(5) the person is a principal for the purposes of this section` `the person is the Government or a statutory body or authority acting in the discharge of its functions`

-- s 66(1).
@export Under section 66(1), may the person act as a contractor or subcontractor?
GIVEN `the Minister has required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner?
      `the person is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(1), may the person act as a contractor or subcontractor` IS
    `s 66(1) the person may act as a contractor or a subcontractor` `the Minister has required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered` `the person is registered`

-- s 66(1).  The bar as a question of its own: it begins with the Minister's notification and is lifted once the person is registered.
@export Under section 66(1), is the person barred from acting as a contractor or subcontractor?
GIVEN `the Minister has required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner?
      `the person is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(1), is the person barred from acting as a contractor or subcontractor` IS
    `s 66(1) the prohibition on acting as a contractor or a subcontractor without registration applies to the person` `the Minister has required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered` `the person is registered`

-- s 66(2).
@export Under section 66(2), is the application for registration acceptable?
GIVEN `the application is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for registration in the prescribed form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(2), is the application for registration acceptable` IS
    `s 66(2) the application for registration is acceptable` `the application is in the prescribed form`

-- s 66(3).
@export Under section 66(3), is a registered contractor or subcontractor deemed to be the employer of the workmen it employs?
GIVEN `the person is registered as a contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person registered under section 66 as a contractor or subcontractor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(3), is the person deemed to be the employer of the workmen` IS
    `s 66(3) the person is deemed to be the employer of the workmen employed by that person` `the person is registered as a contractor or subcontractor`

-- s 66(4).  Public holidays can move the last day: give up to two (1 January 1900 for none).
