GIVEN `the day of the change of name` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contractor or subcontractor change its name?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after that day? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 66(4), by what date must the contractor apply for re-registration` IS
    `s 66(4) the last day for applying for re-registration` `the day of the change of name` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 66(4).
@export Under section 66(4), was the application for re-registration made within 7 days of the change of name?
GIVEN `the contractor is registered and changed its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contractor or subcontractor registered, and did it change the name under which it carries on business?
      `the day of the change of name` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it change its name?
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written application for re-registration and cancellation of the previous registration made to the Commissioner?
      `the first public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the first public holiday in the days after the change of name? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
      `the second public holiday after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the second public holiday in those days? (1 January 1900 if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(4), was the application for re-registration made in time` IS
    `s 66(4) the application for re-registration was made within 7 days of the change of name` `the contractor is registered and changed its name` `the day of the change of name` `the day the application was made` (`my public holidays` `the first public holiday after that day` `the second public holiday after that day`)

-- s 66(7).
@export Under section 66(7), is a person guilty of an offence for contravening section 66?
