    `s 66(7) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person contravenes section 66`

-- s 66(7).  The Act points to section 112 for the penalty, and that section is not among the sources, so this question answers NOTHING whatever the facts.
@export Under section 66(7), what is the penalty on conviction?
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been convicted of an offence before?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 66(7), what is the penalty on conviction` IS
    `s 66(7) the penalty on conviction` NOTHING NOTHING `the person has been convicted of an offence before`

