-- ea2: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation "version in force from 5/12/2025", with the
-- Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019 -- THE SEAT LAYER for the line ranges of part ea2 (Parts 6A to 14).
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).
--
-- SEAT: an employee working in Singapore, or a person about to start work there, asking on facts they can state whether the Act
-- covers them, what they are owed (pay, rest, leave, notice, termination benefits), when, and what they can do if it is not given.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law.  There is never a seat for an official: where a provision addresses only an official, the rule is in
-- layer 1 and the person meets it through the questions below (for example what an inspecting officer may do to them).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  The records and MAYBE inputs the layer-1 modules expect
-- are built inside each question from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure"; "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that
--     cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A pay rate or a figure from a regulation that the person does not know is asked as 0 and becomes NOTHING.
--   * The daily rate of pay (the Third Schedule's answer, seam S6) is asked of the person: this layer has no Third Schedule.
--   * The public holidays: the person says whether one falls on the day in question; the module takes the full list, and this
--     layer builds a list of at most that one day (assumption, NOTES.md).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on
-- these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ea2)").  Never read NOTHING as no.

DECLARE `ea2 seat: my answer` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: Yes`
    `ea2 seat: No`
    `ea2 seat: I am not sure`

DECLARE `ea2 seat: how my employment ended` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: it has not ended`
    `ea2 seat: the specified work was completed or the specified period expired`
    `ea2 seat: I resigned`
    `ea2 seat: my employer dismissed me`
    `ea2 seat: it ended in some other way`

DECLARE `ea2 seat: the ground on which my employer dismissed me` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service`
    `ea2 seat: redundancy or a reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work`
    `ea2 seat: some other ground, or none`

DECLARE `ea2 seat: the kind of day` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: a working day`
    `ea2 seat: a rest day`
    `ea2 seat: a public holiday`
    `ea2 seat: a day substituted for a public holiday`
    `ea2 seat: a day of paid annual leave`
    `ea2 seat: a day of paid sick leave`
    `ea2 seat: a day of childcare leave`
    `ea2 seat: a day of leave without pay`
    `ea2 seat: a day within a maternity benefit period`
    `ea2 seat: a day I am not required to work under my contract of service`

DECLARE `ea2 seat: who is asking` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: the Commissioner for Labour`
    `ea2 seat: an inspecting officer`
    `ea2 seat: someone else`

DECLARE `ea2 seat: the relief I want` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: reinstatement in my former employment`
    `ea2 seat: compensation`
    `ea2 seat: some other sum`

DECLARE `ea2 seat: the absence I take` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: 4 weeks before and 4 weeks after the confinement`
    `ea2 seat: the first 8 of 12 agreed weeks`
    `ea2 seat: 8 agreed weeks`

DECLARE `ea2 seat: my employer is` IS ONE OF
    `ea2 seat: the Government`
    `ea2 seat: a statutory authority`
    `ea2 seat: someone else`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `ea2 seat: my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `ea2 seat: Yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: No` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ea2 seat: my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- A date that the person may or may not have.
GIVEN `I have it` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` MEANS
    IF `I have it` THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- The public holidays: at most the one day the person says is a public holiday.
GIVEN falls IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`ea2 seat: the public holiday on that day` MEANS
    IF falls THEN LIST day ELSE EMPTY -- input mapping

-- The completed months from one day to another (the day is counted when add months reaches it).
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      finish IS A DATE
      counted IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ea2 seat: helper: the completed months counted so far` MEANS
    IF `add months` start (counted PLUS 1) AT MOST finish AND counted LESS THAN 1200
    THEN `ea2 seat: helper: the completed months counted so far` start finish (counted PLUS 1)
    ELSE counted -- input mapping

GIVEN start IS A DATE
      finish IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ea2 seat: my completed months of service` MEANS
    `ea2 seat: helper: the completed months counted so far` start finish 0 -- input mapping

GIVEN ended IS A `ea2 seat: how my employment ended`
GIVETH A `How the employment ended`
`ea2 seat: how my employment ended, as the Act names it` MEANS
    CONSIDER ended
    WHEN `ea2 seat: it has not ended` THEN `Ending: it has not ended` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: the specified work was completed or the specified period expired` THEN `Ending: the specified work was completed or the specified period expired` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: I resigned` THEN `Ending: the employee resigned` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: my employer dismissed me` THEN `Ending: the employer dismissed the employee` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: it ended in some other way` THEN `Ending: it ended in some other way` -- input mapping

GIVEN ground IS A `ea2 seat: the ground on which my employer dismissed me`
GIVETH A `Ground of dismissal`
`ea2 seat: the ground of my dismissal, as the Act names it` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `ea2 seat: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` THEN `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: redundancy or a reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work` THEN `Ground: redundancy or reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: some other ground, or none` THEN `Ground: some other ground or none` -- input mapping

GIVEN kind IS A `ea2 seat: the kind of day`
GIVETH A `Kind of day`
`ea2 seat: the kind of day, as the Act names it` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a working day` THEN `Day: a working day` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a rest day` THEN `Day: a rest day` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a public holiday` THEN `Day: a public holiday` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a day substituted for a public holiday` THEN `Day: a day substituted for a public holiday` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a day of paid annual leave` THEN `Day: a day of paid annual leave` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a day of paid sick leave` THEN `Day: a day of paid sick leave` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a day of childcare leave` THEN `Day: a day of childcare leave` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a day of leave without pay` THEN `Day: a day of no-pay leave` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a day within a maternity benefit period` THEN `Day: a day within a maternity benefit period` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a day I am not required to work under my contract of service` THEN `Day: a day the employee is not required to work` -- input mapping

GIVEN who IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking`
GIVETH A `Official or body the Act names`
`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `ea2 seat: the Commissioner for Labour` THEN `Official: the Commissioner for Labour` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: an inspecting officer` THEN `Official: an inspecting officer` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: someone else` THEN `Official: an authorised person` -- input mapping

GIVEN relief IS A `ea2 seat: the relief I want`
GIVETH A `Relief a claimant may seek`
`ea2 seat: the relief, as the Act names it` MEANS
    CONSIDER relief
    WHEN `ea2 seat: reinstatement in my former employment` THEN `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: compensation` THEN `Relief: compensation` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: some other sum` THEN `Relief: payment of a sum the Commissioner considers just` -- input mapping

GIVEN absence IS A `ea2 seat: the absence I take`
GIVETH A `s 76(1A) Pattern of absence`
`ea2 seat: the absence, as the Act names it` MEANS
    CONSIDER absence
    WHEN `ea2 seat: 4 weeks before and 4 weeks after the confinement` THEN `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(a)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: the first 8 of 12 agreed weeks` THEN `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(b)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: 8 agreed weeks` THEN `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(c)` -- input mapping

GIVEN employer IS A `ea2 seat: my employer is`
GIVETH A `Kind of employer`
`ea2 seat: my employer, as the Act names it` MEANS
    CONSIDER employer
    WHEN `ea2 seat: the Government` THEN `Employer who is the Government` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: a statutory authority` THEN `Employer who is a statutory authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: someone else` THEN `Employer who is a body corporate` -- input mapping

-- A notice of termination from what the person knows.
GIVEN `my employer gave it` IS A BOOLEAN
      given IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice of termination`
`ea2 seat: the notice of termination` MEANS
    `Notice of termination` WITH
        `given by` IS IF `my employer gave it` THEN `Party who is the employer` ELSE `Party who is the employee` -- input mapping
        `given on` IS given -- input mapping
        `last day of the notice` IS last -- input mapping
        `in writing` IS TRUE -- input mapping

-- The dates of the employment.
GIVEN began IS A DATE
      `it has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      ended IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Dates of the employment`
`ea2 seat: the dates of my employment` MEANS
    `Dates of the employment` WITH
        `began on` IS began -- input mapping
        `ended on` IS IF `it has ended` THEN JUST ended ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- s 68(4): whether a medical officer has certified the work as suited to the child's capacity.
GIVEN answer IS A `ea2 seat: my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ea2 seat: the certificate of a medical officer on the work` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `ea2 seat: Yes` THEN `s 68(4) the work is suited to the capacity of the child` (JUST TRUE) TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: No` THEN `s 68(4) the work is suited to the capacity of the child` (JUST TRUE) FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea2 seat: I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- Section 72(1), from what the person says about the work.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      `the work is approved and supervised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is in a training school or institute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an apprenticeship programme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ea2 seat: sections 68 and 69 apply to the work` MEANS
    `s 72(1) sections 68 and 69 apply to the employment` (`s 67A "young person" the person is a young person` age) `the work is approved and supervised` `the work is in a training school or institute` `it is an apprenticeship programme` -- input mapping

-- The first and the last day of a period, when there is one.
GIVEN period IS A MAYBE (`Period of days`)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ea2 seat: the first day of the period if there is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (`first day` OF p) -- input mapping
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the facts do not fix a period
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN period IS A MAYBE (`Period of days`)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ea2 seat: the last day of the period if there is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (`last day` OF p) -- input mapping
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the facts do not fix a period
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `The Employment Act 1968, Parts 6A to 14 -- my questions`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Part 6A -- part-time employees (s 66A)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 66A(1) and (2).  A part-time employee is an employee required by the contract to work for less than 35 hours a week,
-- unless the Minister has declared that the employee, or the class, is not to be regarded as part-time.
@export Under section 66A, am I a part-time employee for the purposes of Part 6A?
GIVEN `I am an employee` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Are you an employee (a person who has entered into a contract of service with an employer)?
      `the hours a week my contract of service requires me to work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week does your contract of service require you to work?
      `the Minister has declared that I or my class of employees is not to be regarded as part-time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, declared that you, or your class of employees, are not to be regarded as part-time employees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66A, am I a part-time employee for the purposes of Part 6A` IS
    `s 66A(1) gathered with (2): the employee is a part-time employee for the purposes of this Part`
        (`s 66A(1) the person is a part-time employee` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `I am an employee`) `the hours a week my contract of service requires me to work`)
        (`s 66A(2) the employee is regarded as a part-time employee for the purposes of this Part` `the Minister has declared that I or my class of employees is not to be regarded as part-time`)


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Part 7 -- domestic workers (s 67)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 67.  The Minister may by notification apply the Act, or any of its provisions, to domestic workers.  The provision applies to you only if he has.
@export Under section 67, does a provision of the Act apply to me as a domestic worker?
GIVEN `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette applied the provision to domestic workers like me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, applied that provision of the Act to all domestic workers, or to a group, class or number of domestic workers that includes you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 67, does a provision of the Act apply to me as a domestic worker` IS
    `s 67 the provision of the Act applies to the domestic worker` `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette applied the provision to domestic workers like me`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Part 8 -- children and young persons (ss 67A to 75)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 67A.  A child is a person who has not completed the 15th year of age (under 15).
@export Under section 67A, am I a child?
GIVEN `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 67A, am I a child` IS
    `s 67A "child" the person is a child` `my age in completed years`

-- s 67A.  A young person has completed the 15th year of age but not the 16th (15 only).
@export Under section 67A, am I a young person?
GIVEN `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 67A, am I a young person` IS
    `s 67A "young person" the person is a young person` `my age in completed years`

-- s 68(1) to (4) with s 72(1).  A person must not employ a child except in an industrial undertaking in which only members of the same family are employed,
-- or, from 13 years of age, in light work suited to the child's capacity in a non-industrial undertaking (a medical officer's certificate on that being conclusive).
-- Section 72(1) takes approved training work out of the section.
@export Under section 68, may an employer employ me as a child?
GIVEN `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `the undertaking is an industrial undertaking` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Is the place where you work an industrial undertaking (a factory, mine, workshop, construction or transport undertaking)?
      `only members of my family are employed in the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are only members of your own family employed there?
      `the work is light work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work light work?
      `a medical officer has certified the work as suited to my capacity` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Has a medical officer certified that the work is suited to your capacity?
      `the work is approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore?
      `the work is carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute?
      `the employment is under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employment under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 68, may an employer employ me as a child` IS
    `s 68(1) the person may employ the child`
        (`s 67A "child" the person is a child` `my age in completed years`)
        (`s 68(2) a child may be employed in the undertaking` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the undertaking is an industrial undertaking`) `only members of my family are employed in the undertaking`)
        (`s 68(3) a child may be employed in the undertaking` `my age in completed years` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the undertaking is an industrial undertaking`) `the work is light work` (`ea2 seat: the certificate of a medical officer on the work` `a medical officer has certified the work as suited to my capacity`))
        (`ea2 seat: sections 68 and 69 apply to the work` `my age in completed years` `the work is approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education` `the work is carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute` `the employment is under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education`)

-- s 69 with s 72(1).  A young person must not be employed in an industrial undertaking which the Minister has declared one in which a young person must not be employed.
@export Under section 69, may a young person be employed in this industrial undertaking?
GIVEN `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `the Minister has declared the undertaking to be one in which a young person must not be employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, declared the undertaking to be one in which a young person must not be employed?
      `the work is approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore?
      `the work is carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute?
      `the employment is under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employment under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 69, may a young person be employed in this industrial undertaking` IS
    `s 69 the young person may be employed in the undertaking`
        (`s 67A "young person" the person is a young person` `my age in completed years`)
        `the Minister has declared the undertaking to be one in which a young person must not be employed`
        (`ea2 seat: sections 68 and 69 apply to the work` `my age in completed years` `the work is approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education` `the work is carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute` `the employment is under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education`)

-- s 71(2).  Contravening a Minister's order that sets a minimum rate of salary for children or young persons is an offence.
@export Under section 71(2), is an employer guilty of an offence if they pay a child or young person less than the minimum rate of salary?
GIVEN `the minimum rate of salary the order prescribes` IS A NUMBER @desc What minimum rate of salary, in dollars, does the Minister's order prescribe for the work? (0 if there is no order or you do not know)
      `the salary I am paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What salary, in dollars, are you paid for the same period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 71(2), is an employer guilty of an offence if they pay a child or young person less than the minimum rate of salary` IS
    `s 71(2) the person is guilty of an offence` (`ea2 seat: my amount if I know it` `the minimum rate of salary the order prescribes`) `the salary I am paid`

-- s 71(2).  A fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both; a second or subsequent offence: $10,000, 2 years, or both.
@export Under section 71(2), what is the penalty for contravening an order on minimum salary?
GIVEN `it is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence?
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 71(2), what is the penalty for contravening an order on minimum salary` IS
    `s 71(2) the penalty on conviction` `it is a second or subsequent offence`

-- s 73.  A child or young person must not be employed as a workman in the circumstances or on the conditions the Minister has prohibited by regulations (reading 1, fork F14).
@export Under section 73, may I, as a child or young person, be employed as a workman?
GIVEN `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in completed years?
      `my work is that of a workman` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Is your work that of a workman (manual labour under the First Schedule of the Act)?
      `the Minister has prohibited the circumstances or conditions of my employment by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister, by regulations under the Act, prohibited the circumstances or the conditions on which you are employed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73, may I, as a child or young person, be employed as a workman` IS
    `s 73 the child or young person may be employed as a workman` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `my work is that of a workman`) (`my age in completed years` LESS THAN 16) `the Minister has prohibited the circumstances or conditions of my employment by regulations`

-- s 74.  A person who employs a child or young person in contravention of Part 8 or its regulations, or a parent or guardian who knowingly or negligently suffers or permits it, is guilty of an offence.
@export Under section 74, is a person guilty of an offence for employing me in breach of Part 8?
GIVEN `the person employed me, a child or young person, in contravention of Part 8 or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person employ you, as a child or young person, in contravention of Part 8 of the Act or the regulations made under it?
      `the person is my parent or guardian who knowingly or negligently suffered or permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your parent or guardian, who knowingly or negligently suffered or permitted that employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74, is a person guilty of an offence for employing me in breach of Part 8` IS
    `s 74 the person is guilty of an offence` `the person employed me, a child or young person, in contravention of Part 8 or its regulations` `the person is my parent or guardian who knowingly or negligently suffered or permitted it`

-- s 74.  A fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both; where the child or young person suffers serious injury or death, a fine of $5,000 and imprisonment not exceeding 2 years.
@export Under section 74, what is the penalty for employing a child or young person in breach of Part 8?
GIVEN `I suffered serious injury or death resulting from a breach of Part 8 or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer serious injury (or did the child or young person die) as a result of the breach?
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 74, what is the penalty for employing a child or young person in breach of Part 8` IS
    `s 74 the penalty on conviction` `I suffered serious injury or death resulting from a breach of Part 8 or its regulations`

-- s 75.  A child or young person in respect of whom an offence mentioned in Part 8 has been committed may be brought before a Youth Court.
@export Under section 75, may I be brought before a Youth Court?
GIVEN `an offence mentioned in Part 8 has been committed in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an offence mentioned in Part 8 of the Act been committed in respect of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 75, may I be brought before a Youth Court` IS
    `s 75 the child or young person may be brought before a Youth Court` `an offence mentioned in Part 8 has been committed in respect of me`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Part 9 -- maternity protection (ss 76 to 87)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 76(1).  Every female employee is entitled to absent herself from work for her confinement, in one of the 3 ways in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c).
-- The section does not say that a person who is not a female employee is not entitled; that case answers NOTHING.
@export Under section 76(1), am I entitled to absent myself from work for my confinement?
GIVEN `I am an employee` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Are you an employee (a person who has entered into a contract of service with an employer)?
      `I am female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a female?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(1), am I entitled to absent myself from work for my confinement` IS
    `s 76(1) the female employee is entitled to absent herself from work` (`s 76(1) the person is a female employee` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `I am an employee`) `I am female`)

-- s 76(1)(a)(i).  The 4 weeks immediately before the confinement: 28 days, ending the day before.
@export Under section 76(1)(a), on what date does my 4 weeks before the confinement begin?
GIVEN `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you (or will you be) confined (the birth, or the miscarriage after 22 weeks)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 76(1)(a), on what date does my 4 weeks before the confinement begin` IS
    `first day` OF (`s 76(1)(a)(i) the 4 weeks immediately before the confinement` `the day of my confinement`)

-- s 76(1)(a)(ii).  The 8 weeks immediately after the confinement: 56 days, counting the day of confinement.
@export Under section 76(1)(a), on what date does my 8 weeks after the confinement end?
GIVEN `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you (or will you be) confined (the birth, or the miscarriage after 22 weeks)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 76(1)(a), on what date does my 8 weeks after the confinement end` IS
    `last day` OF (`s 76(1)(a)(ii) the 8 weeks immediately after the confinement` `the day of my confinement`)

-- s 76(1)(b).  The 12 weeks, as agreed, must commence not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement and not later than the day of her confinement; a first day outside those limits is outside the text, so the answer is no.
@export Under section 76(1)(b), do the 12 weeks I agreed with my employer begin inside the 28 days before my confinement or on the day of it?
GIVEN `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you (or will you be) confined (the birth, or the miscarriage after 22 weeks)?
      `the first day of the 12 weeks I agreed with my employer` IS A DATE @desc On what date do the 12 weeks you and your employer agreed begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(1)(b), do the 12 weeks I agreed with my employer begin inside the 28 days before my confinement or on the day of it` IS
    `s 76(1)(b) the agreed 12 weeks begin inside the window` `the day of my confinement` `the first day of the 12 weeks I agreed with my employer`

-- s 76(1)(c)(i).  The 8 weeks, as agreed, must commence not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement and not later than the day of her confinement; a first day outside those limits is outside the text, so the answer is no.
@export Under section 76(1)(c)(i), do the 8 weeks I agreed with my employer begin inside the 28 days before my confinement or on the day of it?
GIVEN `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you (or will you be) confined (the birth, or the miscarriage after 22 weeks)?
      `the first day of the 8 weeks I agreed with my employer` IS A DATE @desc On what date do the 8 weeks you and your employer agreed begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(1)(c)(i), do the 8 weeks I agreed with my employer begin inside the 28 days before my confinement or on the day of it` IS
    `s 76(1)(c)(i) the agreed 8 weeks begin inside the window` `the day of my confinement` `the first day of the 8 weeks I agreed with my employer`

-- s 76(1A) with s 76(1)(a), (b) and (c).  The benefit period depends on the absence taken: NOTHING when the agreed start is outside the window the paragraph allows.
@export Under section 76(1A), on what date does my benefit period begin?
GIVEN `the absence I take` IS A `ea2 seat: the absence I take` @desc Which absence do you take?
      `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you (or will you be) confined (the birth, or the miscarriage after 22 weeks)?
      `the first day of the absence I agreed with my employer` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the absence you agreed with your employer begin? (If you take the 4 weeks before and the 8 weeks after the confinement, give the day of your confinement.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 76(1A), on what date does my benefit period begin` IS
    `ea2 seat: the first day of the period if there is one` (`s 76(1A) the benefit period` (`ea2 seat: the absence, as the Act names it` `the absence I take`) `the day of my confinement` `the first day of the absence I agreed with my employer`)

-- s 76(1A).  The last day of the benefit period.
@export Under section 76(1A), on what date does my benefit period end?
GIVEN `the absence I take` IS A `ea2 seat: the absence I take` @desc Which absence do you take?
      `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you (or will you be) confined (the birth, or the miscarriage after 22 weeks)?
      `the first day of the absence I agreed with my employer` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the absence you agreed with your employer begin? (If you take the 4 weeks before and the 8 weeks after the confinement, give the day of your confinement.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 76(1A), on what date does my benefit period end` IS
    `ea2 seat: the last day of the period if there is one` (`s 76(1A) the benefit period` (`ea2 seat: the absence, as the Act names it` `the absence I take`) `the day of my confinement` `the first day of the absence I agreed with my employer`)

-- s 76(1A).  Payment at the gross rate of pay for each day of the benefit period.  The gross rate per day is the Third Schedule's (seam S6), asked of the person.
@export Under section 76(1A), what sum is payable to me for the days of my benefit period?
GIVEN `the days of my benefit period for which payment is due` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days of the benefit period is payment due?
      `my gross rate of pay per day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your gross rate of pay for one day, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 76(1A), what sum is payable to me for the days of my benefit period` IS
    `s 76(1A) the sum payable for the days of the benefit period` `the days of my benefit period for which payment is due` (`ea2 seat: my amount if I know it` `my gross rate of pay per day`)

-- s 76(2B) (confinements from 22 August 2015).  Not entitled if she has not served her employer for at least 3 months (counting as the section says);
-- the earlier tiers, (2) and (2A), are in layer 1 and are not asked here: they concern confinements before 22 August 2015.
-- If she has served long enough, this subsection gives no answer.
@export Under section 76(2B), am I entitled to pay during the benefit period given how long I have served my employer?
GIVEN `the day I delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you deliver?
      `I have a certified estimated delivery date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a medical practitioner certify an estimated delivery date for this confinement?
      `the estimated delivery date a medical practitioner certified` IS A DATE @desc What estimated delivery date did the medical practitioner certify? (Any date if none)
      `the completed months I served my employer before the day of my confinement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed months had you served your employer before the day of your confinement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(2B), am I entitled to pay during the benefit period given how long I have served my employer` IS
    `s 76(2B) the female employee is entitled to pay during the benefit period` `the day I delivered` (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `I have a certified estimated delivery date` `the estimated delivery date a medical practitioner certified`) `the completed months I served my employer before the day of my confinement`

-- s 76(3).  For the days she worked during the benefit period before the confinement, the employee is paid an amount equivalent to a day's pay for each of those days (gross rate).
