-- s 84(1).  The tiers by date (before 1 May 2013, from 1 May 2013 to 21 August 2015, from 22 August 2015) are in layer 1; the facts decide which applies.
-- JUST FALSE: the text says the notice does not have that effect in the cases it names; NOTHING: it does not say.
@export Under section 84(1), does the notice of dismissal deprive me of a payment under Part 9?
GIVEN `the notice of dismissal was given without sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice of dismissal given without sufficient cause?
      `the day the notice of dismissal was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of dismissal given?
      `I have a certified estimated delivery date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a medical practitioner certify an estimated delivery date for this confinement?
      `the estimated delivery date a medical practitioner certified` IS A DATE @desc What estimated delivery date did the medical practitioner certify? (Any date if none)
      `I have been confined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been confined?
      `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you confined? (Any date if not yet)
      `my pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your pregnancy certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given?
      `the completed months I had served my employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed months had you served your employer immediately before the day the notice was given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), does the notice of dismissal deprive me of a payment under Part 9` IS
    `s 84(1) the notice of dismissal has the effect of depriving her of a payment under this Part` `the notice of dismissal was given without sufficient cause` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `I have a certified estimated delivery date` `the estimated delivery date a medical practitioner certified`) (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `I have been confined` `the day of my confinement`) `my pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given` `the completed months I had served my employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given`

-- s 84(1A).  Where there are several certifications, the relevant estimated delivery date is the one certified closest before the notice.  The seat takes one certification; layer 1 takes a list.
@export Under section 84(1A), which certified estimated delivery date is the relevant one for my notice of dismissal?
GIVEN `the day the notice of dismissal is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the notice of dismissal given?
      `the estimated delivery date` IS A DATE @desc What estimated delivery date did the medical practitioner certify?
      `the day it was certified` IS A DATE @desc On what date was that estimated delivery date certified?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 84(1A), which certified estimated delivery date is the relevant one for my notice of dismissal` IS
    `s 84(1A) the estimated delivery date that is relevant` `the day the notice of dismissal is given` (LIST (`s 84(1A) Certified estimated delivery date` WITH `the estimated delivery date` IS `the estimated delivery date`, `the day it was certified` IS `the day it was certified`))

-- s 84(2).  She may lodge a claim for reinstatement or compensation if she is in the circumstances in (1)(a), (b) or (c) and considers the notice was not given for sufficient cause, and the Employment Claims Act 2016 s 3 allows the claim.
@export Under section 84(2), may I lodge a claim for reinstatement or compensation after a dismissal in the circumstances of section 84(1)?
GIVEN `I am in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the circumstances of section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c)?
      `I consider that the notice of dismissal was not given for sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consider that the notice of dismissal was not given for sufficient cause?
      `section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 allows the claim` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Does section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 allow the claim?
      `the relief I want` IS A `ea2 seat: the relief I want` @desc What do you want to claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(2), may I lodge a claim for reinstatement or compensation after a dismissal in the circumstances of section 84(1)` IS
    `s 84(2) the female employee may lodge a claim for the relief` `I am in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c)` `I consider that the notice of dismissal was not given for sufficient cause` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 allows the claim`) (`ea2 seat: the relief, as the Act names it` `the relief I want`)

-- s 84(3)(a).  Where the Tribunal is satisfied she has been dismissed without sufficient cause on a claim for reinstatement, it may direct the employer to reinstate her and pay the wages she would have earned.
@export Under section 84(3)(a), may the Tribunal direct my employer to reinstate me?
GIVEN `the body hearing my claim is the Employment Claims Tribunal` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Is the body hearing your claim the Employment Claims Tribunal?
      `my claim is for reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for reinstatement?
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that I was dismissed without sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Tribunal satisfied that you have been dismissed without sufficient cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(3)(a), may the Tribunal direct my employer to reinstate me` IS
    `s 84(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate her and to pay her the wages she would have earned` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the body hearing my claim is the Employment Claims Tribunal`) `my claim is for reinstatement` `the Tribunal is satisfied that I was dismissed without sufficient cause`

-- s 84(3)(b).  On a claim for compensation, the Tribunal that is satisfied she was dismissed without sufficient cause may direct the employer to pay her compensation in wages.
@export Under section 84(3)(b), may the Tribunal direct my employer to pay me compensation in wages?
GIVEN `the body hearing my claim is the Employment Claims Tribunal` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Is the body hearing your claim the Employment Claims Tribunal?
      `my claim is for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for compensation?
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that I was dismissed without sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Tribunal satisfied that you have been dismissed without sufficient cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(3)(b), may the Tribunal direct my employer to pay me compensation in wages` IS
    `s 84(3)(b) the Tribunal may direct the employer to pay her compensation in wages` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the body hearing my claim is the Employment Claims Tribunal`) `my claim is for compensation` `the Tribunal is satisfied that I was dismissed without sufficient cause`

-- s 84A(1).  Dismissal on the ground of redundancy or a reorganisation, with the dated tiers as in s 84(1).
@export Under section 84A(1), does a notice of dismissal for redundancy or reorganisation deprive me of a payment under Part 9?
GIVEN `the notice of dismissal was given on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice of dismissal given on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation of your employer's profession, business, trade or work?
      `the day the notice of dismissal was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of dismissal given?
      `I have a certified estimated delivery date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a medical practitioner certify an estimated delivery date for this confinement?
      `the estimated delivery date a medical practitioner certified` IS A DATE @desc What estimated delivery date did the medical practitioner certify? (Any date if none)
      `I have been confined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been confined?
      `the day of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you confined? (Any date if not yet)
      `my pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your pregnancy certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given?
      `the completed months I had served my employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed months had you served your employer immediately before the day the notice was given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84A(1), does a notice of dismissal for redundancy or reorganisation deprive me of a payment under Part 9` IS
    `s 84A(1) the notice of dismissal has the effect of depriving her of a payment under this Part` `the notice of dismissal was given on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `I have a certified estimated delivery date` `the estimated delivery date a medical practitioner certified`) (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `I have been confined` `the day of my confinement`) `my pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given` `the completed months I had served my employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given`

-- s 84A(3).  A payment mentioned in subsection (1) is in addition to any retrenchment benefit or other payment.
@export Under section 84A(3), is my payment under Part 9 in addition to a retrenchment benefit?
GIVEN `the payment is a payment referred to in section 84A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment one that section 84A(1) refers to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84A(3), is my payment under Part 9 in addition to a retrenchment benefit` IS
    `s 84A(3) the payment is in addition to a retrenchment benefit or other payment` `the payment is a payment referred to in section 84A(1)`

-- s 86.  A term by which a female employee relinquishes a right to maternity benefit, or removes or reduces her employer's liability, is void.
@export Under section 86, is a term of my contract of service that gives up my maternity benefit void?
GIVEN `a term of my contract of service relinquishes a right to maternity benefit under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a term of your contract of service by which you give up a right to maternity benefit under Part 9?
      `the term purports to deprive me of that right or to remove or reduce my employer's liability to make a payment under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to deprive you of that right, or to remove or reduce your employer's liability to make a payment under Part 9?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86, is a term of my contract of service that gives up my maternity benefit void` IS
    `s 86 the term of the contract of service is void` `a term of my contract of service relinquishes a right to maternity benefit under Part 9` `the term purports to deprive me of that right or to remove or reduce my employer's liability to make a payment under Part 9`

-- s 87(1).  An employer who without reasonable cause fails to grant maternity leave, fails to pay in accordance with Part 9 (other than s 87A), or contravenes s 81, is guilty of an offence.
@export Under section 87(1), is my employer guilty of an offence for not giving or paying my maternity benefit?
GIVEN `my employer failed, without reasonable cause, to grant me maternity leave that I am entitled to and request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail, without reasonable cause, to grant you maternity leave that you are entitled to and requested?
      `my employer failed to pay me in accordance with a provision of Part 9 other than section 87A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to pay you in accordance with a provision of Part 9 other than section 87A?
      `my employer acted in contravention of section 81` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer act in contravention of section 81 (notice of dismissal during your absence)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87(1), is my employer guilty of an offence for not giving or paying my maternity benefit` IS
    `s 87(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` `my employer failed, without reasonable cause, to grant me maternity leave that I am entitled to and request` `my employer failed to pay me in accordance with a provision of Part 9 other than section 87A` `my employer acted in contravention of section 81`

-- s 87(1).  A fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
@export Under section 87(1), what is the penalty for an employer who commits that offence?
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 87(1), what is the penalty for an employer who commits that offence` IS
    `s 87(1) the penalty on conviction`

-- s 87A(8) "child".  The employee's own child by birth, an adopted child or stepchild, or a child the employee is fostering as the paragraph describes.
@export Under section 87A(8), is the person my child for the purposes of childcare leave?
GIVEN `the person is my own child by birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your own child by birth?
      `the person is my adopted child or stepchild` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your adopted child or your stepchild?
      `the person is a child I am fostering as section 87A(8) describes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a child you are fostering as section 87A(8) describes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(8), is the person my child for the purposes of childcare leave` IS
    `s 87A(8) "child" the person is a child of the employee` `the person is my own child by birth` `the person is my adopted child or stepchild` `the person is a child I am fostering as section 87A(8) describes`

-- s 87A(1) with s 87A(8) "relevant period".  Where an employee has served an employer for at least 3 months and has a child below 7 at some time in the relevant period, she is entitled to childcare leave of 2 days for it; otherwise the "where" fails and the answer is no.
@export Under section 87A(1), am I entitled to childcare leave for the relevant period?
GIVEN `the completed months I have served my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed months have you served your employer?
      `the day my child was born` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your child born?
      `my employer and I agreed the 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and your employer agree on a 12-month period for childcare leave?
      `the first day of the 12 months we agreed` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the 12 months you agreed begin? (Any date if none)
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(1), am I entitled to childcare leave for the relevant period` IS
    `s 87A(1) the entitlement to childcare leave for the relevant period arises` `the completed months I have served my employer` (LIST `the day my child was born`) (`s 87A(8) "relevant period" the period` (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `my employer and I agreed the 12 months` `the first day of the 12 months we agreed`) `the calendar year`)

-- s 87A(1) with s 87A(8) "relevant period".  2 days for each relevant period, if the employee has served the employer for at least 3 months and has a child below 7 at some time in the period.
-- The relevant period is the 12 months the employee and employer agreed, else the calendar year.
@export Under section 87A(1), how many days of childcare leave am I entitled to for the relevant period?
GIVEN `the completed months I have served my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc How many completed months have you served your employer?
      `the day my child was born` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your child born?
      `my employer and I agreed the 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and your employer agree on a 12-month period for childcare leave?
      `the first day of the 12 months we agreed` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the 12 months you agreed begin? (Any date if none)
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 87A(1), how many days of childcare leave am I entitled to for the relevant period` IS
    `s 87A(1) the days of childcare leave the employee is entitled to for the relevant period` `the completed months I have served my employer` (LIST `the day my child was born`) (`s 87A(8) "relevant period" the period` (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `my employer and I agreed the 12 months` `the first day of the 12 months we agreed`) `the calendar year`)

-- s 87A(2)(a).  The entitlement is 2 days for each relevant period, and no more than 14 days in all in respect of each child.
@export Under section 87A(2)(a), am I entitled to the days of childcare leave I now claim for this child?
GIVEN `the days of childcare leave already granted in respect of the child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave have already been granted in respect of this child?
      `the days of childcare leave I now claim in respect of the child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave do you now claim in respect of this child?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(2)(a), am I entitled to the days of childcare leave I now claim for this child` IS
    `s 87A(2)(a) the employee is entitled to the days now claimed in respect of the child` `the days of childcare leave already granted in respect of the child` `the days of childcare leave I now claim in respect of the child`

-- s 87A(2)(a).  14 days in all for each child.
@export Under section 87A(2)(a), how many days of childcare leave remain within the limit for this child?
GIVEN `the days of childcare leave already granted in respect of the child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave have already been granted in respect of this child?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 87A(2)(a), how many days of childcare leave remain within the limit for this child` IS
    `s 87A(2)(a) the days that remain within the 14-day limit for the child` `the days of childcare leave already granted in respect of the child`

-- s 87A(3).  The total days off: childcare leave, rest days, public holidays, annual leave and sick leave added together.
@export Under section 87A(3), how many days off in all am I entitled to in a year?
GIVEN `the days of childcare leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave are you entitled to?
      `the rest days under section 36` IS A NUMBER @desc How many rest days under section 36?
      `the holidays under section 88` IS A NUMBER @desc How many public holidays under section 88?
      `the days of annual leave under section 88A` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of annual leave under section 88A?
      `the days of sick leave under section 89` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of sick leave under section 89?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 87A(3), how many days off in all am I entitled to in a year` IS
    `s 87A(3) the total days off the employee is entitled to` `the days of childcare leave` `the rest days under section 36` `the holidays under section 88` `the days of annual leave under section 88A` `the days of sick leave under section 89`

-- s 87A(4).  Childcare leave not taken by the last day of the relevant period is lost, and is not paid in lieu.
@export Under section 87A(4), how many days of my childcare leave do I lose if I do not take them by the last day of the relevant period?
GIVEN `the days of childcare leave I took by the last day of the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave did you take by the last day of the relevant period?
      `my entitlement for the relevant period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your entitlement for the relevant period, in days?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 87A(4), how many days of my childcare leave do I lose if I do not take them by the last day of the relevant period` IS
    `s 87A(4) the days of the entitlement that are lost` `the days of childcare leave I took by the last day of the relevant period` `my entitlement for the relevant period in days`

-- s 87A(4)(a).  No: the days not taken by then are lost.
@export Under section 87A(4)(a), am I still entitled to the days of childcare leave I did not take by the last day of the relevant period?
GIVEN `the days of childcare leave I took by the last day of the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave did you take by the last day of the relevant period?
      `my entitlement for the relevant period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your entitlement for the relevant period, in days?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(4)(a), am I still entitled to the days of childcare leave I did not take by the last day of the relevant period` IS
    `s 87A(4)(a) the employee is still entitled to the days not taken by the last day` `the days of childcare leave I took by the last day of the relevant period` `my entitlement for the relevant period in days`

-- s 87A(4)(b).  No payment in lieu.
@export Under section 87A(4)(b), am I entitled to payment in lieu of childcare leave I did not take by the last day of the relevant period?
GIVEN `the days of childcare leave I took by the last day of the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave did you take by the last day of the relevant period?
      `my entitlement for the relevant period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your entitlement for the relevant period, in days?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(4)(b), am I entitled to payment in lieu of childcare leave I did not take by the last day of the relevant period` IS
    `s 87A(4)(b) the employee is entitled to payment in lieu of the days not taken` `the days of childcare leave I took by the last day of the relevant period` `my entitlement for the relevant period in days`

-- s 87A(5).  The gross rate of pay for each day of childcare leave taken.
@export Under section 87A(5), how much must my employer pay me for the childcare leave I took?
GIVEN `the days of childcare leave I took` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave did you take?
      `my gross rate of pay per day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your gross rate of pay for one day, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 87A(5), how much must my employer pay me for the childcare leave I took` IS
    `s 87A(5) the amount the employer must pay for the childcare leave taken` `the days of childcare leave I took` (`ea2 seat: my amount if I know it` `my gross rate of pay per day`)

-- s 87A(5A).  Not on a day of no-pay leave.
@export Under section 87A(5A), am I entitled to paid childcare leave on a day of no-pay leave?
GIVEN `the day is a day of no-pay leave` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Is the day one of no-pay leave (leave without pay, as the Act defines it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(5A), am I entitled to paid childcare leave on a day of no-pay leave` IS
    `s 87A(5A) the employee is entitled to take paid childcare leave on the day` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the day is a day of no-pay leave`)

-- s 87A(6)(a).  If her employment ends (by resignation, dismissal, completion of the contract or any other reason) before she has taken the 2 days, she ceases to be entitled to that leave.
@export Under section 87A(6)(a), do I cease to be entitled to childcare leave I have not yet taken when my employment ends?
GIVEN `how my employment ended` IS A `ea2 seat: how my employment ended` @desc How did your employment end (or has it not ended)?
      `the days of my childcare leave not yet taken when the employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave had you not yet taken when the employment ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
