    `s 87A(6)(a) the employee ceases to be entitled to the leave not yet taken` (`ea2 seat: how my employment ended, as the Act names it` `how my employment ended`) `the days of my childcare leave not yet taken when the employment ended`

-- s 87A(6)(b).  If her employment ends before she has taken the 2 days, she is not entitled to any payment in lieu.
@export Under section 87A(6)(b), am I not entitled to payment in lieu of childcare leave not yet taken when my employment ends?
GIVEN `how my employment ended` IS A `ea2 seat: how my employment ended` @desc How did your employment end (or has it not ended)?
      `the days of my childcare leave not yet taken when the employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of childcare leave had you not yet taken when the employment ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(6)(b), am I not entitled to payment in lieu of childcare leave not yet taken when my employment ends` IS
    `s 87A(6)(b) the employee is not entitled to payment in lieu of the leave not yet taken` (`ea2 seat: how my employment ended, as the Act names it` `how my employment ended`) `the days of my childcare leave not yet taken when the employment ended`

-- s 87A(7).  An employer who fails to pay the gross rate of pay for a day of childcare leave taken is guilty of an offence.
@export Under section 87A(7), is my employer guilty of an offence for not paying me my gross rate of pay for childcare leave?
GIVEN `my employer failed to pay my gross rate of pay for a day of childcare leave I took` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to pay your gross rate of pay for a day of childcare leave you took?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87A(7), is my employer guilty of an offence for not paying me my gross rate of pay for childcare leave` IS
    `s 87A(7) the employer is guilty of an offence` `my employer failed to pay my gross rate of pay for a day of childcare leave I took`

-- s 87A(7A).  An employer who fails, without reasonable cause, to grant childcare leave to an employee entitled to it who requests it is guilty of an offence.
@export Under section 87A(7A), is my employer guilty of an offence for not granting me childcare leave?
GIVEN `my employer failed to grant me childcare leave that I am entitled to and requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to grant you childcare leave that you are entitled to and requested?
      `my employer had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
