    `s 87A(7B) the penalty on conviction of a person convicted under subsection (7) or (7A)` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the employer is a repeat offender`)

-- s 87A(7B).  Where an employer convicted under subsection (7) or (7A) is a repeat offender (as subsection (7C) describes), the higher penalty applies; where the employer is not, the "Where" fails and the answer is no.
@export Under section 87A(7B), does the penalty for a repeat offender apply to my employer?
GIVEN `the employer is a repeat offender` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Has the employer already been convicted of such an offence in the way section 87A(7C) describes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
