-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Part 10 -- public holidays, annual leave and sick leave (ss 88 to 90)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 88(1).  An employee is entitled to a paid holiday at the gross rate of pay on each public holiday while the employment lasts (including the day it begins and the day it ends).
@export Under section 88(1), am I entitled to a paid holiday on a public holiday?
GIVEN `the public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the public holiday?
      `the day I began my employment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you begin your employment?
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employment ended?
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employment end? (Any date if it has not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(1), am I entitled to a paid holiday on a public holiday` IS
    `s 88(1) the employee is entitled to a paid holiday at the gross rate of pay on the public holiday` `the public holiday` (`ea2 seat: the dates of my employment` `the day I began my employment` `my employment has ended` `the day my employment ended`)

-- s 88(1)(a).  By agreement between employer and employee a day may be substituted for the public holiday.
@export Under section 88(1)(a), may the employer and I agree to substitute another day for a public holiday?
GIVEN `my employer and I agreed to substitute the day for a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and your employer agree to substitute another day for the public holiday?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(1)(a), may the employer and I agree to substitute another day for a public holiday` IS
    `s 88(1)(a) the day may be substituted for the public holiday` `my employer and I agreed to substitute the day for a public holiday`

-- s 88(1)(b).  The working day next following the rest day.
@export Under section 88(1)(b), which day is my paid holiday if a public holiday falls on my rest day?
GIVEN `the public holiday falls on my rest day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the public holiday fall on your rest day?
      `the working day next following that rest day` IS A DATE @desc What is the working day next following that rest day?
