    `s 89(8) the employer is deemed to fulfil its obligation under subsection (7A)` `the Commissioner has by written order directed that my employer has fulfilled the obligation` `my employer provides a healthcare scheme for its employees` `my employer complies with the other requirement the Minister prescribed by regulations`

-- s 89(10).
@export Under section 89(10), does section 89 apply to me for treatment that is for cosmetic purposes?
GIVEN `in the opinion of the medical practitioner the treatment is for cosmetic purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the opinion of the medical practitioner performing the examination, is the treatment for cosmetic purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 89(10), does section 89 apply to me for treatment that is for cosmetic purposes` IS
    `s 89(10) section 89 applies to the employee` `in the opinion of the medical practitioner the treatment is for cosmetic purposes`

-- s 90(1).
@export Under section 90(1), is my employer guilty of an offence for employing me contrary to Part 10 or not paying my salary under it?
GIVEN `my employer employed me contrary to the provisions of Part 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer employ you contrary to the provisions of Part 10?
      `my employer failed to pay my salary in accordance with the provisions of Part 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to pay your salary in accordance with the provisions of Part 10?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 90(1), is my employer guilty of an offence for employing me contrary to Part 10 or not paying my salary under it` IS
    `s 90(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` `my employer employed me contrary to the provisions of Part 10` `my employer failed to pay my salary in accordance with the provisions of Part 10`

-- s 90(1).  A fine not exceeding $5,000 (second or subsequent offence: $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both).
-- The first-offence imprisonment cell is JUST 0, standing in for "no imprisonment is stated" (NOTES.md, finding on the imprisonment cell).
@export Under section 90(1), what is the penalty on an employer who commits that offence?
GIVEN `it is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence?
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 90(1), what is the penalty on an employer who commits that offence` IS
    `s 90(1) the penalty on conviction` `it is a second or subsequent offence`

-- s 90(2)(a).
@export Under section 90(2)(a), may my employer and I negotiate terms of service more favourable than sections 88A and 89?
GIVEN `the terms of service are more favourable than those in sections 88A and 89` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms of service more favourable to you than those in sections 88A and 89?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 90(2)(a), may my employer and I negotiate terms of service more favourable than sections 88A and 89` IS
    `s 90(2)(a) the employer and the employees or their trade union may negotiate for and agree to the terms` `the terms of service are more favourable than those in sections 88A and 89`

-- s 90(2)(b).
@export Under section 90(2)(b), is it an offence for my employer to grant me terms more favourable than sections 88A and 89?
GIVEN `the terms of service are more favourable than those in sections 88A and 89` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms of service more favourable to you than those in sections 88A and 89?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 90(2)(b), is it an offence for my employer to grant me terms more favourable than sections 88A and 89` IS
    `s 90(2)(b) it is an offence for the employer to grant the terms` `the terms of service are more favourable than those in sections 88A and 89`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Part 12 -- records, pay slips, returns and secrecy (ss 95 to 102)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 95(1).  An employer must make and keep an employee record for each employee and former employee.
@export Under section 95(1), must my employer make and keep an employee record for me?
GIVEN `I am an employee of the employer or a former employee of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employee of the employer, or a former employee of the employer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 95(1), must my employer make and keep an employee record for me` IS
    `s 95(1) the employer must make and keep an employee record for the person` `I am an employee of the employer or a former employee of the employer`

-- s 95(1) with (3).  The employer failed to comply if it did not make the record, did not keep it for the retention period, or it lacks the particulars or is incomplete or inaccurate (s 95(3)).
@export Under section 95(1), did my employer fail to comply with the duty to make and keep my employee record?
GIVEN `my employer made my employee record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer make an employee record for you?
      `my employer kept the record for the record retention period prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer keep it for the record retention period prescribed?
      `the record contains the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the record contain the prescribed particulars?
      `the record is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record incomplete or inaccurate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 95(1), did my employer fail to comply with the duty to make and keep my employee record` IS
    `s 95(1) the employer failed to comply` `my employer made my employee record` `my employer kept the record for the record retention period prescribed` `the record contains the prescribed particulars` `the record is incomplete or inaccurate`

-- s 95(2).
@export Under section 95(2), did my employer fail to ensure that my employee record was readily accessible to me?
GIVEN `my employee record was readily accessible to me during the record retention period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your employee record readily accessible to you during the record retention period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 95(2), did my employer fail to ensure that my employee record was readily accessible to me` IS
    `s 95(2) the employer failed to ensure that the employee record is readily accessible` `my employee record was readily accessible to me during the record retention period`

-- s 95A(1).  Applies to an employee who entered into a contract of service on or after 1 April 2016 for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum.
@export Under section 95A(1), does my employer have to give me a written record of my key employment terms?
GIVEN `the day I entered into my contract of service` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you enter into your contract of service?
      `my employment is for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment under the contract for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 95A(1), does my employer have to give me a written record of my key employment terms` IS
    `s 95A(1) section 95A applies to the employee` `the day I entered into my contract of service` `my employment is for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service`

-- s 95A(2).  Not later than 14 days after the day the employee starts employment (or the number of days prescribed in substitution), by s 50 of the Interpretation Act.
-- The seat asks whether a public holiday falls on the 14th day and gives the module a list of that one day (assumption, NOTES.md); the prescribed substitute number of days is asked as 0 when none.
@export Under section 95A(2), by what date must my employer give me the written record of my key employment terms?
GIVEN `the day I start employment` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you start employment?
      `the number of days prescribed in substitution` IS A NUMBER @desc Has a different number of days been prescribed instead of 14? Give it, or 0 if none.
      `the 14th day after I start is a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the 14th day after the day you start employment a public holiday?
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a contrary intention appear in the Act or the contract about how the days are counted?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 95A(2), by what date must my employer give me the written record of my key employment terms` IS
    `s 95A(2) the last day for giving the written record of the key employment terms` `the day I start employment` (`ea2 seat: my amount if I know it` `the number of days prescribed in substitution`) (`ea2 seat: the public holiday on that day` `the 14th day after I start is a public holiday` (`the day I start employment` PLUS 14)) `a contrary intention appears`

-- s 95A(2).  The employer failed to comply if section 95A applies, it was not exempted, and the record was not given by the last day (or it is incomplete or inaccurate, s 95A(5)).
@export Under section 95A(2), did my employer fail to give me a written record of my key employment terms in time?
GIVEN `section 95A applies to me` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Does section 95A apply to you (see the question on section 95A(1))?
      `the Minister has by order exempted my employer from the provision in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister, by order in the Gazette, exempted your employer from the provision in respect of you?
      `the last day for giving me the written record` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for giving you the written record?
      `my employer has given me the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer given you the written record?
      `the day my employer gave me the written record` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employer give you the record? (Any date if not yet)
      `the written record is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the written record incomplete or inaccurate?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 95A(2), did my employer fail to give me a written record of my key employment terms in time` IS
    `s 95A(2) the employer failed to comply` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `section 95A applies to me`) `the Minister has by order exempted my employer from the provision in respect of me` (JUST `the last day for giving me the written record`) (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `my employer has given me the record` `the day my employer gave me the written record`) `the written record is incomplete or inaccurate` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 95A(3).
@export Under section 95A(3), is my employer's duty to give me a written record satisfied by an electronic record or a website?
GIVEN `an electronic record containing the key employment terms was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by me for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give you an electronic record of the key employment terms in a way that you can access and use for later reference?
      `the key employment terms are published on an Internet website authorised by my employer and readily accessible to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the key employment terms published on an Internet website authorised by your employer and readily accessible to you?
      `my employer disseminated the address of that website to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer tell you the address of that website?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 95A(3), is my employer's duty to give me a written record satisfied by an electronic record or a website` IS
    `s 95A(3) the requirement to give a written record is satisfied` `an electronic record containing the key employment terms was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by me for subsequent reference` `the key employment terms are published on an Internet website authorised by my employer and readily accessible to me` `my employer disseminated the address of that website to me`

-- s 96(1)(a).
@export Under section 96(1)(a), did my employer fail to give me a pay slip for my salary period?
GIVEN `my employer paid my salary for the salary period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer pay your salary for the salary period?
      `my employer gave me the pay slip within the time prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give you the pay slip within the time prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 96(1)(a), did my employer fail to give me a pay slip for my salary period` IS
    `s 96(1)(a) the employer failed to give the employee a pay slip` `my employer paid my salary for the salary period` `my employer gave me the pay slip within the time prescribed`

-- s 96(1)(b).
@export Under section 96(1)(b), did my employer fail to give me a pay slip for a sum paid under section 22 or 23?
GIVEN `my employer paid a sum under section 22 or 23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer pay a sum under section 22 or 23?
      `my employer gave me a pay slip for that sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give you a pay slip for that sum?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 96(1)(b), did my employer fail to give me a pay slip for a sum paid under section 22 or 23` IS
    `s 96(1)(b) the employer failed to give the employee a pay slip for the sum paid` `my employer paid a sum under section 22 or 23` `my employer gave me a pay slip for that sum`

-- s 96(2).
@export Under section 96(2), does the pay slip I was given meet the requirements of form and information?
GIVEN `the pay slip is in the form prescribed, if a form is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the pay slip in the form prescribed (if a form is prescribed)?
      `the pay slip contains all the information prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the pay slip contain all the information prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 96(2), does the pay slip I was given meet the requirements of form and information` IS
    `s 96(2) the pay slip given meets the requirements of form and information` `the pay slip is in the form prescribed, if a form is prescribed` `the pay slip contains all the information prescribed`

-- s 96(3).
@export Under section 96(3), is my employer's duty to give me a pay slip satisfied by an electronic record?
GIVEN `an electronic record containing the prescribed information of a pay slip was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by me for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give you an electronic record of the prescribed pay slip information in a way that you can access and use for later reference?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 96(3), is my employer's duty to give me a pay slip satisfied by an electronic record` IS
    `s 96(3) the requirement to give a pay slip is satisfied` `an electronic record containing the prescribed information of a pay slip was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by me for subsequent reference`

-- s 96(4).
@export Under section 96(4), is my employer taken to have failed to give me a pay slip if the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate?
GIVEN `the pay slip given to me is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the pay slip you were given incomplete or inaccurate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 96(4), is my employer taken to have failed to give me a pay slip if the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate` IS
    `s 96(4) the employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1)` `the pay slip given to me is incomplete or inaccurate`

-- s 96A.  Where the notification applies to the employer, the employer must furnish the information it requires.
@export Under section 96A, did my employer fail to comply with a requirement of the notification on retrenchment?
GIVEN `the notification applies to my employer` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Does the Retrenchment Reporting Notification apply to your employer (see the questions under the Notification)?
      `my employer met every requirement in the notification concerning the information on the retrenchment` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Did your employer meet every requirement in the notification about giving information on the retrenchment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 96A, did my employer fail to comply with a requirement of the notification on retrenchment` IS
    `s 96A the employer failed to comply with a requirement in the notification` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the notification applies to my employer`) (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `my employer met every requirement in the notification concerning the information on the retrenchment`)

-- s 97(1).
@export Under section 97(1), must my employer furnish the particulars and information in a return the Commissioner requires?
GIVEN `the Commissioner has by notification in the Gazette required my employer or its class to forward a return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner for Labour, by notification in the Gazette, required your employer (or its class of employer) to forward a return?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 97(1), must my employer furnish the particulars and information in a return the Commissioner requires` IS
    `s 97(1) the employer must furnish the particulars and information prescribed in the return` `the Commissioner has by notification in the Gazette required my employer or its class to forward a return`

-- s 98(1).
@export Under section 98(1), is my employer required to furnish fuller or further returns?
GIVEN `the Commissioner has given my employer written notice requiring fuller or further returns within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner for Labour given your employer written notice requiring fuller or further returns within a reasonable time stated in the notice?
      `the matter is one as to which a return is required under the Act or the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one as to which a return is required under the Employment Act or the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 98(1), is my employer required to furnish fuller or further returns` IS
    `s 98(1) the employer is required to furnish the fuller or further returns` `the Commissioner has given my employer written notice requiring fuller or further returns within a reasonable time` `the matter is one as to which a return is required under the Act or the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990`

-- s 99.
@export Under section 99, must a person complete and deliver a return or attend and produce books when the Commissioner gives written notice?
GIVEN `the Commissioner has given the person written notice for the purpose of obtaining full information in respect of an employer's employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner for Labour given the person written notice for the purpose of obtaining full information about an employer's employees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 99, must a person complete and deliver a return or attend and produce books when the Commissioner gives written notice` IS
    `s 99 the person must complete and deliver the return, or attend and produce the books, documents, accounts and returns, as the notice requires` `the Commissioner has given the person written notice for the purpose of obtaining full information in respect of an employer's employees`

-- s 101(1)(a).
@export Under section 101(1)(a), is my employer guilty of an offence for wilfully refusing or neglecting to furnish particulars required?
GIVEN `my employer wilfully refused to furnish or authenticate the particulars or information as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer wilfully refuse to furnish or authenticate the particulars or information as required?
      `my employer neglected to furnish or authenticate the particulars or information as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer neglect to furnish or authenticate the particulars or information as required?
      `my employer has proved a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer proved a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(1)(a), is my employer guilty of an offence for wilfully refusing or neglecting to furnish particulars required` IS
    `s 101(1)(a) the employer is guilty of an offence` `my employer wilfully refused to furnish or authenticate the particulars or information as required` `my employer neglected to furnish or authenticate the particulars or information as required` `my employer has proved a lawful excuse`

-- s 101(1)(b).
@export Under section 101(1)(b), is my employer guilty of an offence for furnishing false particulars in response to a notice?
GIVEN `my employer wilfully furnished or caused to be furnished false particulars or information in respect of a matter specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer wilfully furnish, or cause to be furnished, false particulars or information about a matter specified in the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(1)(b), is my employer guilty of an offence for furnishing false particulars in response to a notice` IS
    `s 101(1)(b) the employer is guilty of an offence` `my employer wilfully furnished or caused to be furnished false particulars or information in respect of a matter specified in the notice`

-- s 101(1)(c).
@export Under section 101(1)(c), is my employer guilty of an offence for refusing to answer a question necessary for a required return?
GIVEN `my employer refused to answer, or wilfully gave a false answer to, a question necessary for obtaining information required under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer refuse to answer, or wilfully give a false answer to, a question necessary for obtaining information required under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(1)(c), is my employer guilty of an offence for refusing to answer a question necessary for a required return` IS
    `s 101(1)(c) the employer is guilty of an offence` `my employer refused to answer, or wilfully gave a false answer to, a question necessary for obtaining information required under the Act`

-- s 101(1).  A fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
@export Under section 101(1), what is the penalty for an employer guilty of an offence about returns?
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 101(1), what is the penalty for an employer guilty of an offence about returns` IS
    `s 101(1) the penalty on conviction`

-- s 101(1).  A further fine not exceeding $500 for every day the offence continues after conviction.
@export Under section 101(1), what is the greatest further fine for each day an offence of false particulars continues?
GIVEN `the days during which the offence continues` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days after conviction does the offence continue?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 101(1), what is the greatest further fine for each day an offence of false particulars continues` IS
    `s 101(1) the greatest further fine for a continuing offence` `the days during which the offence continues`

-- s 101(1).  The offence is deemed to continue from the day the false particulars were furnished until true particulars have been furnished; on or after the day the true ones are furnished the deeming stops.  The text says nothing of a day before the false particulars.
@export Under section 101(1), is the offence of false particulars deemed to continue on a given day?
GIVEN `the day the false particulars were furnished` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the false particulars, information or answers furnished?
      `true particulars have been furnished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have true particulars, information or answers been furnished since?
      `the day the true particulars were furnished` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the true ones furnished? (Any date if not yet)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(1), is the offence of false particulars deemed to continue on a given day` IS
    `s 101(1) the false-particulars offence is deemed to continue on the day` `the day the false particulars were furnished` (`ea2 seat: a date if I have one` `true particulars have been furnished` `the day the true particulars were furnished`) `the day I am asking about`

-- s 101(2).
@export Under section 101(2), is the Commissioner's certificate sufficient prima facie evidence that my employer's returns were not furnished or are incorrect?
GIVEN `the certificate is under the hand of the Commissioner and states that the returns have not been furnished or are incorrect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a certificate under the hand of the Commissioner for Labour stating that the returns have not been furnished or are incorrect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(2), is the Commissioner's certificate sufficient prima facie evidence that my employer's returns were not furnished or are incorrect` IS
    `s 101(2) the certificate is sufficient prima facie evidence of the facts it states` `the certificate is under the hand of the Commissioner and states that the returns have not been furnished or are incorrect`

-- s 101(3).
@export Under section 101(3), do subsections (1) and (2) apply to information furnished on the retrenchment of an employee?
GIVEN `the information is furnished or required to be furnished under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information furnished, or required to be furnished, under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of an employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(3), do subsections (1) and (2) apply to information furnished on the retrenchment of an employee` IS
    `s 101(3) subsections (1) and (2) apply to the information` `the information is furnished or required to be furnished under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of an employee`

-- s 102(1) (first limb).  A return or answer must not be published without the previous written consent of the person having control; with it, the text forbids nothing.
@export Under section 102(1), must a return or answer not be published without the previous written consent?
GIVEN `the previous written consent of the person having control, management or superintendence was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the previous written consent of the person having the control, management or superintendence of the business given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(1), must a return or answer not be published without the previous written consent` IS
    `s 102(1) the return or answer must not be published` `the previous written consent of the person having control, management or superintendence was given`

-- s 102(1) (second limb).  Except for the purposes of a prosecution, a person not engaged on the statistics must not be permitted to see an individual return.
@export Under section 102(1), must a person be refused sight of an individual return?
GIVEN `the person is engaged in connection with the collection or preparation of statistics under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person engaged in connection with the collection or preparation of statistics under the Act?
      `it is for the purposes of a prosecution under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purposes of a prosecution under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(1), must a person be refused sight of an individual return` IS
    `s 102(1) the person must not be permitted to see the individual return` `the person is engaged in connection with the collection or preparation of statistics under the Act` `it is for the purposes of a prosecution under the Act`

-- s 102(2).
@export Under section 102(2), must a person engaged in statistics make a declaration?
GIVEN `the person is engaged in connection with the collection, preparation or publication of statistics under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person engaged in connection with the collection, preparation or publication of statistics under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(2), must a person engaged in statistics make a declaration` IS
    `s 102(2) the person must make the declaration in the prescribed form` `the person is engaged in connection with the collection, preparation or publication of statistics under the Act`

-- s 102(2).
@export Under section 102(2), is a person guilty of an offence for knowingly acting contrary to the declaration?
GIVEN `the person has made the declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person made the declaration?
      `the person knowingly acted in contravention of the declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person knowingly act in contravention of the declaration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(2), is a person guilty of an offence for knowingly acting contrary to the declaration` IS
    `s 102(2) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person has made the declaration` `the person knowingly acted in contravention of the declaration`

-- s 102(2).  A fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
@export Under section 102(2), what is the penalty for acting contrary to the declaration?
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 102(2), what is the penalty for acting contrary to the declaration` IS
    `s 102(2) the penalty on conviction`

-- s 102(3).
@export Under section 102(3), may a publication disclose particulars of a return so that they can be identified with an individual or business?
GIVEN `the publication discloses the particulars comprised in a return, or arranges them in a way which would enable a person to identify them as relating to an individual person or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the publication disclose the particulars in a return, or arrange them so that a person could identify them as relating to an individual or a business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(3), may a publication disclose particulars of a return so that they can be identified with an individual or business` IS
    `s 102(3) the publication may disclose or arrange the particulars in that way` `the publication discloses the particulars comprised in a return, or arranges them in a way which would enable a person to identify them as relating to an individual person or business`

-- s 102(4).
@export Under section 102(4), is a person guilty of an offence for publishing information disclosed in breach of section 102?
GIVEN `the person has possession of information that to the person's knowledge has been disclosed in contravention of section 102` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have possession of information that, to the person's knowledge, was disclosed in contravention of section 102?
      `the person publishes or communicates the information to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person publish or communicate the information to another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(4), is a person guilty of an offence for publishing information disclosed in breach of section 102` IS
    `s 102(4) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person has possession of information that to the person's knowledge has been disclosed in contravention of section 102` `the person publishes or communicates the information to another person`

-- s 102(4).  A fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
@export Under section 102(4), what is the penalty for publishing information disclosed in breach of section 102?
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
DECIDE `Under section 102(4), what is the penalty for publishing information disclosed in breach of section 102` IS
    `s 102(4) the penalty on conviction`

-- s 102(5).
@export Under section 102(5), do subsections (1) to (4) apply to information furnished on the retrenchment of an employee?
GIVEN `the information is furnished under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information furnished under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of an employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(5), do subsections (1) to (4) apply to information furnished on the retrenchment of an employee` IS
    `s 102(5) subsections (1) to (4) apply to the information` `the information is furnished under section 96A by an employer on the retrenchment of an employee`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Part 13 -- inspection, arrest and secrecy (ss 103 to 107)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 103(1).  The Commissioner for Labour and an inspecting officer have the powers in the subsection; the Act is silent on anyone else here.
@export Under section 103(1), does the person asking have the powers of the Commissioner for Labour or an inspecting officer?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1), does the person asking have the powers of the Commissioner for Labour or an inspecting officer` IS
    `s 103(1) the official has the powers in this subsection` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`)

-- s 103(1)(a).
@export Under section 103(1)(a), may the person enter and search my workplace?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the official has reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of an offence under the Act or of a civil contravention can be found in the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the official has reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of an offence under the Act or of a civil contravention can be found in the premises?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(a), may the person enter and search my workplace` IS
    `s 103(1)(a) the official may enter and search the premises` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the official has reasonable cause to believe that evidence of the commission of an offence under the Act or of a civil contravention can be found in the premises`

-- s 103(1)(aa).
@export Under section 103(1)(aa), may the person enter my place of employment without previous notice to audit my terms and conditions?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the place is a place of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the place is a place of employment?
      `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the time is a reasonable time?
      `the purpose is conducting an audit in relation to the terms and conditions of employment of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the purpose is conducting an audit in relation to the terms and conditions of employment of an employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(aa), may the person enter my place of employment without previous notice to audit my terms and conditions` IS
    `s 103(1)(aa) the official may enter the place of employment without previous notice` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the place is a place of employment` `the time is a reasonable time` `the purpose is conducting an audit in relation to the terms and conditions of employment of an employee`

-- s 103(1)(b).
@export Under section 103(1)(b), may the person examine me orally?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the person is reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(b), may the person examine me orally` IS
    `s 103(1)(b) the official may examine the person orally and reduce the answer or statement into writing` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the person is reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act`

-- s 103(1)(c).
@export Under section 103(1)(c), may the person require me to produce a document and answer questions about it?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the official has reason to believe that the person has the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the official has reason to believe that the person has the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(c), may the person require me to produce a document and answer questions about it` IS
    `s 103(1)(c) the official may require the person to produce the document and to answer questions about it` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the official has reason to believe that the person has the document`

-- s 103(1)(d).
@export Under section 103(1)(d), may the person examine a notice or document my employer must keep?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the notice or document is required to be kept under the Act or its regulations, or is required to be produced under paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice or document is required to be kept under the Act or its regulations, or is required to be produced under paragraph (c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(d), may the person examine a notice or document my employer must keep` IS
    `s 103(1)(d) the official may examine the notice or document` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the notice or document is required to be kept under the Act or its regulations, or is required to be produced under paragraph (c)`

-- s 103(1)(e).
@export Under section 103(1)(e), may the person make copies of or retain a notice or document?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the notice or document is one mentioned in paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice or document is one mentioned in paragraph (d)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(e), may the person make copies of or retain a notice or document` IS
    `s 103(1)(e) the official may make copies of or retain the notice or document` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the notice or document is one mentioned in paragraph (d)`

-- s 103(1)(f).
@export Under section 103(1)(f), may the person retain samples of materials or substances used at my workplace for analysis?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the materials or substances are used or handled by employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the materials or substances are used or handled by employees?
      `the employer or the employer's representative has been notified of the samples taken or removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the employer or the employer's representative has been notified of the samples taken or removed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(f), may the person retain samples of materials or substances used at my workplace for analysis` IS
    `s 103(1)(f) the official may retain the samples for analysis` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the materials or substances are used or handled by employees` `the employer or the employer's representative has been notified of the samples taken or removed`

-- s 103(1)(g).
@export Under section 103(1)(g), may the person photograph or record the premises or people who know the facts?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the photograph or recording is of the premises or of persons reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the photograph or recording is of the premises or of persons reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act?
      `the official thinks the photograph or recording necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the official thinks the photograph or recording necessary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(g), may the person photograph or record the premises or people who know the facts` IS
    `s 103(1)(g) the official may take the photograph or audio or video recording` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the photograph or recording is of the premises or of persons reasonably believed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances relevant to the carrying out of the provisions of the Act` `the official thinks the photograph or recording necessary`

-- s 103(1)(h).
@export Under section 103(1)(h), may the person require me to produce an article and take it into custody?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the article is relevant to an investigation under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the article is relevant to an investigation under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1)(h), may the person require me to produce an article and take it into custody` IS
    `s 103(1)(h) the official may require the person to produce the article and, if necessary, take it into custody` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the article is relevant to an investigation under the Act`

-- s 103(2).
@export Under section 103(2), am I bound to state truly the facts I am acquainted with when examined orally?
GIVEN `the person is the person mentioned in subsection (1)(b), examined orally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is the person mentioned in subsection (1)(b), examined orally?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(2), am I bound to state truly the facts I am acquainted with when examined orally` IS
    `s 103(2) the person examined is bound to state truly the facts and circumstances with which the person is acquainted` `the person is the person mentioned in subsection (1)(b), examined orally`

-- s 103(3).
@export Under section 103(3), must my statement be read over to me and signed after correction?
GIVEN `the statement was made by the person mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the statement was made by the person mentioned in subsection (1)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(3), must my statement be read over to me and signed after correction` IS
    `s 103(3) the statement must be read over to the person and, after correction, signed by the person` `the statement was made by the person mentioned in subsection (1)(b)`

-- s 103(4).  On being required to by the person, the Commissioner or inspecting officer must show credentials.
@export Under section 103(4), must the person show me their credentials?
GIVEN `the person has required the official to show his or her credentials` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person has required the official to show his or her credentials?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(4), must the person show me their credentials` IS
    `s 103(4) the Commissioner or the inspecting officer must show his or her credentials` `the person has required the official to show his or her credentials`

-- s 104.
@export Under section 104, must the person notify my employer of their presence when they enter my workplace?
GIVEN `the official entered a place of employment under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the official entered a place of employment under section 103?
      `the official considers that notifying the employer may be prejudicial to the efficient performance of his or her duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the official considers that notifying the employer may be prejudicial to the efficient performance of his or her duties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 104, must the person notify my employer of their presence when they enter my workplace` IS
    `s 104 the official must notify the employer or the employer's representative of his or her presence` `the official entered a place of employment under section 103` `the official considers that notifying the employer may be prejudicial to the efficient performance of his or her duties`

-- s 105(1).
@export Under section 105(1), may an inspecting officer arrest me without warrant for an offence under section 21, 22 or 23?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person is committing or has committed an offence under section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person is committing or has committed an offence under section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34?
      `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person has abetted the commission of such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person has abetted the commission of such an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(1), may an inspecting officer arrest me without warrant for an offence under section 21, 22 or 23` IS
    `s 105(1) the inspecting officer may arrest the person without warrant` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person is committing or has committed an offence under section 21, 22 or 23 read with section 34` `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person has abetted the commission of such an offence`

-- s 105(2).
@export Under section 105(2), may an inspecting officer arrest me without warrant as an officer, member or partner who consented to the offence?
GIVEN `who is asking` IS A `ea2 seat: who is asking` @desc Who is asking, or doing this to you: the Commissioner for Labour, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `the person is an officer or a member of a body corporate or an unincorporated association, or a partner of a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is an officer or a member of a body corporate or an unincorporated association, or a partner of a partnership?
      `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person consented to, connived in or by neglect caused the commission of an offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person consented to, connived in or by neglect caused the commission of an offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(2), may an inspecting officer arrest me without warrant as an officer, member or partner who consented to the offence` IS
    `s 105(2) the inspecting officer may arrest the person without warrant` (`ea2 seat: the official, as the Act names them` `who is asking`) `the person is an officer or a member of a body corporate or an unincorporated association, or a partner of a partnership` `the inspecting officer reasonably suspects the person consented to, connived in or by neglect caused the commission of an offence mentioned in subsection (1)(a)`

-- s 105(3).
@export Under section 105(3), must the inspecting officer produce me before a Magistrate's Court after arresting me without warrant?
GIVEN `an inspecting officer arrested the person without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an inspecting officer arrested the person without warrant?
      `the person was released on bail or on his or her own bond under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person was released on bail or on his or her own bond under subsection (5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(3), must the inspecting officer produce me before a Magistrate's Court after arresting me without warrant` IS
    `s 105(3) the inspecting officer must produce the person arrested before a Magistrate's Court` `an inspecting officer arrested the person without warrant` `the person was released on bail or on his or her own bond under subsection (5)`

-- s 105(4).  An inspecting officer must not detain a person arrested without warrant longer than is reasonable in the circumstances, and the period must not exceed 48 hours exclusive of the journey.
@export Under section 105(4), must an inspecting officer not detain me in custody for a given number of hours after an arrest without warrant?
GIVEN `the hours the person arrested without warrant has been detained, not counting the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court` IS A NUMBER @desc Please give the number for this: the hours the person arrested without warrant has been detained, not counting the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court.
      `the detention is longer than is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the detention is longer than is reasonable in the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(4), must an inspecting officer not detain me in custody for a given number of hours after an arrest without warrant` IS
    `s 105(4) the inspecting officer must not detain the person in custody for that long` `the hours the person arrested without warrant has been detained, not counting the time necessary for the journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court` `the detention is longer than is reasonable in the circumstances`

-- s 105(5).
@export Under section 105(5), may an inspecting officer release me on bail or on my own bond after arrest?
GIVEN `the person has been arrested by an inspecting officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person has been arrested by an inspecting officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(5), may an inspecting officer release me on bail or on my own bond after arrest` IS
    `s 105(5) an inspecting officer may release the person on bail or on his or her own bond` `the person has been arrested by an inspecting officer`

-- s 105A(1).
@export Under section 105A(1), must the inspecting officer touch or confine my body to arrest me?
GIVEN `the person submits to arrest by word or action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person submits to arrest by word or action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105A(1), must the inspecting officer touch or confine my body to arrest me` IS
    `s 105A(1) the inspecting officer must touch or confine the body of the person to be arrested` `the person submits to arrest by word or action`

-- s 105A(2).
@export Under section 105A(2), may the inspecting officer use all means necessary to arrest me if I resist?
GIVEN `the person forcibly resists or tries to evade arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person forcibly resists or tries to evade arrest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105A(2), may the inspecting officer use all means necessary to arrest me if I resist` IS
    `s 105A(2) the inspecting officer may use all means necessary to effect the arrest` `the person forcibly resists or tries to evade arrest`

-- s 105B(1).
@export Under section 105B(1), may I be subjected to more restraint than is necessary to prevent my escape?
GIVEN `the restraint is more than is necessary to prevent the person's escape` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the restraint is more than is necessary to prevent the person's escape?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105B(1), may I be subjected to more restraint than is necessary to prevent my escape` IS
    `s 105B(1) the person arrested may be subjected to the restraint` `the restraint is more than is necessary to prevent the person's escape`

-- s 105B(2).
@export Under section 105B(2), may the inspecting officer use handcuffs or a similar means of restraint on me?
GIVEN `the restraint is to prevent the person inflicting bodily injury to himself, herself or others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the restraint is to prevent the person inflicting bodily injury to himself, herself or others?
      `the restraint is to prevent the person damaging property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the restraint is to prevent the person damaging property?
      `the restraint is to prevent the person creating a disturbance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the restraint is to prevent the person creating a disturbance?
      `the restraint is to prevent the person escaping from custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the restraint is to prevent the person escaping from custody?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105B(2), may the inspecting officer use handcuffs or a similar means of restraint on me` IS
    `s 105B(2) the inspecting officer may use handcuffs or a similar means of restraint` `the restraint is to prevent the person inflicting bodily injury to himself, herself or others` `the restraint is to prevent the person damaging property` `the restraint is to prevent the person creating a disturbance` `the restraint is to prevent the person escaping from custody`

-- s 105B(3).
@export Under section 105B(3), may handcuffs or a similar means of restraint be used on me as punishment?
GIVEN `the restraint is used for the purpose of punishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the restraint is used for the purpose of punishment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105B(3), may handcuffs or a similar means of restraint be used on me as punishment` IS
    `s 105B(3) the handcuffs or similar means of restraint may be used` `the restraint is used for the purpose of punishment`

-- s 105C(1).
@export Under section 105C(1), may the inspecting officer take possession of an article found on me?
GIVEN `the person is arrested by the inspecting officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is arrested by the inspecting officer?
      `the article is necessary wearing apparel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the article is necessary wearing apparel?
      `the inspecting officer has reason to believe the article was connected with the offence for which the person is being arrested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the inspecting officer has reason to believe the article was connected with the offence for which the person is being arrested?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105C(1), may the inspecting officer take possession of an article found on me` IS
    `s 105C(1) the inspecting officer may take possession of the article found upon the person` `the person is arrested by the inspecting officer` `the article is necessary wearing apparel` `the inspecting officer has reason to believe the article was connected with the offence for which the person is being arrested`

-- s 105C(2).
@export Under section 105C(2), may the inspecting officer search me if the officer is not of my sex?
GIVEN `the inspecting officer is of the same sex as the person to be searched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the inspecting officer is of the same sex as the person to be searched?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105C(2), may the inspecting officer search me if the officer is not of my sex` IS
    `s 105C(2) the inspecting officer may make the search` `the inspecting officer is of the same sex as the person to be searched`

-- s 105C(2).  Whenever it is necessary to cause a person to be searched, the search must be made by an inspecting officer of the same sex as the person.
@export Under section 105C(2), must a search of me be made by an inspecting officer of my sex?
GIVEN `it is necessary to cause the person to be searched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is necessary to cause the person to be searched?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105C(2), must a search of me be made by an inspecting officer of my sex` IS
    `s 105C(2) the search must be made by an inspecting officer of the same sex as the person` `it is necessary to cause the person to be searched`

-- s 105E.
@export Under section 105E, may the inspecting officer take an offensive weapon from me when arresting me?
GIVEN `the inspecting officer is making an arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the inspecting officer is making an arrest?
      `the article is an offensive weapon the person arrested has about his or her person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the article is an offensive weapon the person arrested has about his or her person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105E, may the inspecting officer take an offensive weapon from me when arresting me` IS
    `s 105E the inspecting officer may take the offensive weapon from the person arrested` `the inspecting officer is making an arrest` `the article is an offensive weapon the person arrested has about his or her person`

-- s 105F.
@export Under section 105F, may the inspecting officer pursue and arrest me anywhere in Singapore if I escape from lawful custody?
GIVEN `the person in lawful custody escaped or was rescued from the custody of the inspecting officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person in lawful custody escaped or was rescued from the custody of the inspecting officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105F, may the inspecting officer pursue and arrest me anywhere in Singapore if I escape from lawful custody` IS
    `s 105F the inspecting officer may immediately pursue and arrest the person in any place within Singapore` `the person in lawful custody escaped or was rescued from the custody of the inspecting officer`

-- s 106.
@export Under section 106, may an inspecting officer reveal my employer's manufacturing or commercial secret?
GIVEN `the secret is a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the secret is a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer?
      `the person reveals it in the performance of his or her duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person reveals it in the performance of his or her duties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 106, may an inspecting officer reveal my employer's manufacturing or commercial secret` IS
    `s 106 the person may reveal the manufacturing or commercial secret` `the secret is a manufacturing or commercial secret that came to the person's knowledge in the course of his or her duty as an inspecting officer` `the person reveals it in the performance of his or her duties`

-- s 106A(1).
@export Under section 106A(1), what must be done with a document, article or thing taken from me?
GIVEN `the Commissioner or an inspecting officer took possession of the document, article or thing under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioner or an inspecting officer took possession of the document, article or thing under this Part?
      `the document, article or thing is produced in a criminal trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document, article or thing is produced in a criminal trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE (`s 106A(1) What must be done with the thing taken`)
DECIDE `Under section 106A(1), what must be done with a document, article or thing taken from me` IS
    `s 106A(1) what must be done with the document, article or thing` `the Commissioner or an inspecting officer took possession of the document, article or thing under this Part` `the document, article or thing is produced in a criminal trial`

-- s 106A(2).
@export Under section 106A(2), may a Magistrate order a document, article or thing taken from me to be forfeited or disposed of?
GIVEN `the report of the document, article or thing was made to a Magistrate under subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the report of the document, article or thing was made to a Magistrate under subsection (1)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 106A(2), may a Magistrate order a document, article or thing taken from me to be forfeited or disposed of` IS
    `s 106A(2) the Magistrate may order the document, article or thing to be forfeited or to be disposed of` `the report of the document, article or thing was made to a Magistrate under subsection (1)(b)`

-- s 106A(3).
@export Under section 106A(3), does section 106A prejudice a right to retain or dispose of property that exists apart from it?
GIVEN `the right to retain or dispose of the property exists in law apart from section 106A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the right to retain or dispose of the property exists in law apart from section 106A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 106A(3), does section 106A prejudice a right to retain or dispose of property that exists apart from it` IS
    `s 106A(3) section 106A prejudices the right to retain or dispose of the property` `the right to retain or dispose of the property exists in law apart from section 106A`

-- s 107(a).  Seen from the person required: what they risk.
@export Under section 107(a), am I guilty of an offence for refusing to produce a document or article when required?
GIVEN `the person neglected or refused to produce a document or article as required under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person neglected or refused to produce a document or article as required under section 103?
      `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person had a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(a), am I guilty of an offence for refusing to produce a document or article when required` IS
    `s 107(a) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person neglected or refused to produce a document or article as required under section 103` `the person had a reasonable excuse`

-- s 107(b).
@export Under section 107(b), am I guilty of an offence for making a false statement to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer?
GIVEN `the person made to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer exercising the powers under section 103 a statement, oral or in writing, that is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person made to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer exercising the powers under section 103 a statement, oral or in writing, that is false in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(b), am I guilty of an offence for making a false statement to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` IS
    `s 107(b) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person made to the Commissioner or an inspecting officer exercising the powers under section 103 a statement, oral or in writing, that is false in a material particular`

-- s 107(c).
@export Under section 107(c), am I guilty of an offence for hindering or obstructing the Commissioner or an inspecting officer?
GIVEN `the person hindered or obstructed the Commissioner or an inspecting officer in the exercise of the powers under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person hindered or obstructed the Commissioner or an inspecting officer in the exercise of the powers under section 103?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(c), am I guilty of an offence for hindering or obstructing the Commissioner or an inspecting officer` IS
    `s 107(c) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person hindered or obstructed the Commissioner or an inspecting officer in the exercise of the powers under section 103`

-- s 107.  A fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
