-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019 (S 200/2019)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- S 200/2019 para 1.  The Notification came into operation on 1 April 2019.
@export Under paragraph 1 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, is the Notification in operation on a day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 1 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, is the Notification in operation on a day` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 1 the Notification is in operation on the day` `the day`

-- S 200/2019 para 2(1) "retrench".  To terminate the employee's contract of service at the initiative of the employer by reason of redundancy or a reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work.
@export Under paragraph 2(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, was the termination of my contract of service a retrenchment?
GIVEN `my employer terminated my contract of service at its own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer terminate your contract of service at its own initiative?
      `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the reason redundancy or a reorganisation of your employer's profession, business, trade or work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 2(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, was the termination of my contract of service a retrenchment` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 2(1) "retrench" the termination is a retrenchment` `my employer terminated my contract of service at its own initiative` `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work`

-- S 200/2019 para 2(1) "working day".  A day that is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.
@export Under paragraph 2(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, is a given day a working day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `the day is a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a public holiday?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 2(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, is a given day a working day` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 2(1) "working day" the day is one` `the day` (`ea2 seat: the public holiday on that day` `the day is a public holiday` `the day`)

-- S 200/2019 para 2(2).  An employee whose contract of service has no end date, or whose contracted term is at least 6 months.
@export Under paragraph 2(2) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the Notification refer to me as an employee?
GIVEN `my contract of service specifies an end date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract of service specify an end date?
      `the term of my employment in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months is the term of your employment under the contract? (0 if no end date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 2(2) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the Notification refer to me as an employee` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 2(2) the employee is one to whom the Notification refers` `my contract of service specifies an end date` `the term of my employment in months`

-- S 200/2019 para 2(3).  An employer has 10 or more employees at the time the notice of retrenchment is given.
@export Under paragraph 2(3) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does my employer have 10 or more employees?
GIVEN `the number of employees my employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees does your employer have at the time the notice of retrenchment is given?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 2(3) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does my employer have 10 or more employees` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 2(3) the employer has 10 or more employees` `the number of employees my employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given`

-- S 200/2019 para 3(1).  The Notification applies to an employer who gives a notice of retrenchment to an employee it refers to, on or after 1 November 2021.
@export Under paragraph 3(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the Notification apply to my employer?
GIVEN `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employer give the notice of retrenchment?
      `my employer terminated my contract of service at its own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer terminate your contract of service at its own initiative?
      `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the reason redundancy or a reorganisation of your employer's profession, business, trade or work?
      `my contract of service specifies an end date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract of service specify an end date?
      `the term of my employment in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months is the term of your employment under the contract? (0 if no end date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 3(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the Notification apply to my employer` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 3(1) the Notification applies to the employer` `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` (`S 200/2019 para 2(1) "retrench" the termination is a retrenchment` `my employer terminated my contract of service at its own initiative` `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work`) (`S 200/2019 para 2(2) the employee is one to whom the Notification refers` `my contract of service specifies an end date` `the term of my employment in months`)

-- S 200/2019 para 2(1), 2(3), 3(1).  The second reading of the headcount (fork F20): the definition of "employer" as one with 10 or more employees still operates, counted at the time the notice of retrenchment is given.  An employer with fewer is outside it.
@export Under paragraph 3(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the Notification apply to my employer if the definition of employer with 10 or more employees still operates?
GIVEN `the number of employees my employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees does your employer have at the time the notice of retrenchment is given?
      `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employer give the notice of retrenchment?
      `my employer terminated my contract of service at its own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer terminate your contract of service at its own initiative?
      `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the reason redundancy or a reorganisation of your employer's profession, business, trade or work?
      `my contract of service specifies an end date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract of service specify an end date?
      `the term of my employment in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months is the term of your employment under the contract? (0 if no end date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 3(1) of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the Notification apply to my employer if the definition of employer with 10 or more employees still operates` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 3(1) the Notification applies to the employer, if the 10-employee definition still operates` `the number of employees my employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given` `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` (`S 200/2019 para 2(1) "retrench" the termination is a retrenchment` `my employer terminated my contract of service at its own initiative` `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of my employer's profession, business, trade or work`) (`S 200/2019 para 2(2) the employee is one to whom the Notification refers` `my contract of service specifies an end date` `the term of my employment in months`)

-- S 200/2019 para 4.  Not later than 5 working days after the day the employer gives the notice of retrenchment.  The seat takes at most one public holiday in that period (assumption, NOTES.md).
@export Under paragraph 4 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, by what date must my employer give the Commissioner the retrenchment report?
GIVEN `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employer give the notice of retrenchment?
      `a public holiday falls in the days after the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a public holiday fall in the days after the notice, before the report is due?
      `the date of that public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is that public holiday? (Any date if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under paragraph 4 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, by what date must my employer give the Commissioner the retrenchment report` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 4 the last day for giving the retrenchment report` `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` (`ea2 seat: the public holiday on that day` `a public holiday falls in the days after the notice` `the date of that public holiday`)

-- S 200/2019 para 4.  In time if given on or before the last day.
@export Under paragraph 4 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, was the retrenchment report given in time?
GIVEN `the day the retrenchment report was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the retrenchment report given?
      `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employer give the notice of retrenchment?
      `a public holiday falls in the days after the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a public holiday fall in the days after the notice, before the report is due?
      `the date of that public holiday` IS A DATE @desc On what date is that public holiday? (Any date if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 4 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, was the retrenchment report given in time` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 4 the retrenchment report was given in time` `the day the retrenchment report was given` `the day my employer gave the notice of retrenchment` (`ea2 seat: the public holiday on that day` `a public holiday falls in the days after the notice` `the date of that public holiday`)

-- S 200/2019 para 5.  The report must be in the form provided at the website of the Ministry of Manpower, unless the Commissioner allows otherwise.
@export Under paragraph 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the form of the retrenchment report meet the Notification?
GIVEN `the report is in the form provided at the website of the Ministry of Manpower` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report in the form provided at the website of the Ministry of Manpower?
      `the Commissioner has allowed otherwise in this case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner for Labour allowed otherwise in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, does the form of the retrenchment report meet the Notification` IS
    `S 200/2019 para 5 the requirement as to the form of the report is met` `the report is in the form provided at the website of the Ministry of Manpower` `the Commissioner has allowed otherwise in this case`

-- S 200/2019 paras 3(2), 4 and 5 together.  The employer met every requirement only if the report contains all the Schedule's information, was given in time, and is in the form required.
-- The Schedule's lists of items are in layer 1 and are not asked here: the person says whether the report contained all the information.
@export Under paragraph 3(2), 4 and 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, did my employer meet every requirement concerning the retrenchment report?
GIVEN `the report contains all the information specified in the Schedule` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Does the retrenchment report contain all the information specified in the Schedule to the Notification?
      `the retrenchment report was given in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the retrenchment report given in time?
      `the requirement as to the form of the report is met` IS A `ea2 seat: my answer` @desc Is the report in the form required (or has the Commissioner allowed otherwise)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under paragraph 3(2), 4 and 5 of the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, did my employer meet every requirement concerning the retrenchment report` IS
    `S 200/2019 the employer met every requirement concerning the report` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the report contains all the information specified in the Schedule`) `the retrenchment report was given in time` (`ea2 seat: what I say, as a fact` `the requirement as to the form of the report is met`)

-- ============================================================
-- ea3: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 2, ea3: THE EMPLOYEE'S SEAT over Part 15 to the Fifth Schedule.
--
-- SEAT: an employee working in Singapore (or a person about to start work there) who asks, on facts they can state,
-- whether the Act covers them, what they are owed, when, and what they can do if it is not given.  This layer phrases the
-- rules of Part 15 (claims, complaints and investigations), Part 15A (administrative penalties), Part 16 (procedure) and the
-- five Schedules, already encoded in the modules imported above, as the questions that person would ask.  Nothing here
-- is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the modules' inputs from the person's answers and calls the rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact
-- the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure" (`ea3 My answer`).  Where the rule needs the
--     fact, "I am not sure" is settled by asking the rule both ways: the answer is given only if both give the same answer,
--     and is NOTHING if they differ.
--   * A fact about an official's or a court's own conduct (an order made "pursuant to the decision", the Commissioner's
--     "opinion") is not asked of the employee; where a rule needs it, the question builds the input from the facts the
--     employee can state, and says so in a comment.
--   * Public holidays: the person cannot be asked for a list of them.  Wherever section 50(b) of the Interpretation Act
--     moves a last day that is a Sunday or a public holiday, the seat passes NO public holiday, so only a Sunday moves
--     the last day (assumed, not ruled: NOTES.md, Marginal readings).  A last day that is a public holiday and not a Sunday
--     is therefore not moved by the seat; layer 1 takes the list.
--   * The amounts and periods that regulations prescribe are asked as plain inputs; the encoding takes no figure from outside the Act.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on
-- these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ea3)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  A provision that addresses only an official, a court or the employer's side (the
-- Commissioner's own procedure, an authorised officer's notice, the employer's reconsideration and appeal under s 126C, the
-- regulation-making ceilings) is encoded in layer 1 for what it decides and has no question here.  Where such a provision
-- means something to the employee (the duty to summon the employer, a successor's continuing the inquiry, the discharge of
-- an order after imprisonment, immunity of an officer), it has a question.  NOTES.md, "Seat (ea3)", lists the encoded
-- provisions with no question and says why.

DECLARE `ea3 My answer` IS ONE OF
    `ea3 Yes`
    `ea3 No`
    `ea3 I am not sure`

DECLARE `ea3 Court` IS ONE OF
    `ea3 a Magistrate's Court`
    `ea3 a District Court`
    `ea3 some other court`

DECLARE `ea3 How my pay is fixed` IS ONE OF
    `ea3 for each month`
    `ea3 for each completed piece of work`
    `ea3 for each hour`
    `ea3 for each day`
    `ea3 in some other way`

DECLARE `ea3 My work pattern after my confinement` IS ONE OF
    `ea3 I work the same number of days in every week`
    `ea3 the number of days I work varies from week to week, in a pattern that repeats over a number of fixed weeks`
    `ea3 the number of days I work varies from week to week, with no regular pattern`
    `ea3 my work pattern is none of these`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure", settled by asking the rule both ways.
GIVEN answer IS A `ea3 My answer`
      rule IS A FUNCTION FROM BOOLEAN TO MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ea3 the rule's answer whether or not I am sure` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `ea3 Yes` THEN rule TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea3 No` THEN rule FALSE -- input mapping
    -- the answer is given only if it is the same whichever way the fact is
    WHEN `ea3 I am not sure` THEN IF (rule TRUE) EQUALS (rule FALSE) THEN rule TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `ea3 My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ea3 what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `ea3 Yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea3 No` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea3 I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A date that counts only if the thing happened.
GIVEN happened IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ea3 the day, if it happened` MEANS
    IF happened THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ea3 my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- No public holiday is passed (see the header).
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`ea3 the public holidays the seat passes` MEANS LIST

-- A court from the person's choice.
GIVEN court IS A `ea3 Court`
GIVETH A `Official or body the Act names`
`ea3 the court I mean` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `ea3 a Magistrate's Court` THEN `Body: a Magistrate's Court` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea3 a District Court` THEN `Body: a District Court` -- input mapping
    WHEN `ea3 some other court` THEN `Body: a Youth Court` -- input mapping: any court that is neither of the two; section 129(2) says nothing of it

-- A pay record from the three items the Third Schedule's rates turn on.  The other items are excluded from the gross rate of
-- pay or the basic rate of pay (s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" (a) to (e), "basic rate of pay" (a) to (e)) or are not read by the Schedule,
-- so a fixed 0 stands for each.
GIVEN work IS A NUMBER
      commissions IS A NUMBER
      `other allowances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pay for a period`
`ea3 my pay record` MEANS
    `Pay for a period` WITH
        `the amounts are for` IS `Pay is fixed for each month` -- placeholder: no rule reads it here
        `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS work -- input mapping
        `overtime payments` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the gross rate and the basic rate
        `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the gross rate and the basic rate
        `commissions` IS commissions -- input mapping
        `productivity incentive payments` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the gross rate and the basic rate
        `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the gross rate and the basic rate
        `travelling allowances` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the gross rate and the basic rate
        `food allowances` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the gross rate and the basic rate
        `housing allowances` IS 0 -- placeholder: left out of the gross rate and the basic rate
        `allowances of any other kind` IS `other allowances` -- input mapping (counts in the gross rate, not in the basic rate)
        `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS 0 -- placeholder: not part of salary
        `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS 0 -- placeholder: not part of salary
        `value of a travelling concession` IS 0 -- placeholder: not part of salary
        `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS 0 -- placeholder: not part of salary
        `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS 0 -- placeholder: not part of salary
        `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS 0 -- placeholder: not part of salary

-- A week from the days the person is required to work in it.
GIVEN full IS A NUMBER
      short IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` MEANS
    `sch 3 Days required in a week` WITH
        `days required to work for more than 5 hours` IS full -- input mapping
        `days required to work for 5 hours or less` IS short -- input mapping

-- The Third Schedule's facts, from what the person states about a monthly rate.  The fields that the item chosen does not read take a fixed placeholder.
GIVEN arrangement IS A `sch 3 Arrangement of pay`
      `the monthly pay` IS A `Pay for a period`
      `the first week` IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
      `the second week` IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
      weeks IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
      `the daily rate under an approved formula` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 Facts about the pay`
`ea3 my monthly pay facts` MEANS
    `sch 3 Facts about the pay` WITH
        `the arrangement of pay` IS arrangement -- input mapping
        `the pay earned in the 14 days before the event` IS `ea3 my pay record` 0 0 0 -- placeholder: read only by item 1
        `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days` IS 0 -- placeholder: read only by item 1
        `the monthly pay` IS `the monthly pay` -- input mapping
        `the days required in the first week` IS `the first week` -- input mapping
        `the days required in the second week` IS `the second week` -- input mapping
        `the weeks for the average` IS weeks -- input mapping
        `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved` IS `the daily rate under an approved formula` -- input mapping

-- The "weeks for the average" of the Third Schedule, item 5, when the item does not read them: every field a fixed placeholder.
GIVETH A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
`ea3 the weeks that no item reads` MEANS
    `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average` WITH
        `the purpose of the calculation` IS `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks` IS FALSE -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the termination of the contract` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the first 3 weeks of the employee's employment` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of absence or period of absence` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the day of absence or period of absence` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only by item 4

-- The "weeks for the average" for an employee who has been employed 3 weeks or more: the purpose, and the 3 weeks immediately before the event the purpose's paragraph names.
GIVEN purpose IS A `sch 3 item 5 Purpose of the calculation`
      first IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
      second IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
      third IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
GIVETH A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
`ea3 my 3 weeks for the average` MEANS
    `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average` WITH
        `the purpose of the calculation` IS purpose -- input mapping
        `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks` IS FALSE -- placeholder: the seat asks about 3 weeks or more of employment
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the termination of the contract` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` THEN (LIST first, second, third) ELSE (LIST)) -- input mapping to the paragraph the purpose names
        `the first 3 weeks of the employee's employment` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only when employed for less than 3 weeks
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of absence or period of absence` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` THEN (LIST first, second, third) ELSE (LIST)) -- input mapping to the paragraph the purpose names
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the day of absence or period of absence` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only when employed for less than 3 weeks
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` THEN (LIST first, second, third) ELSE (LIST)) -- input mapping to the paragraph the purpose names
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS (LIST) -- placeholder: read only when employed for less than 3 weeks

GIVEN earned IS A `Pay for a period`
      `days worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 Facts about the pay`
`ea3 my piece rate facts` MEANS
    `sch 3 Facts about the pay` WITH
        `the arrangement of pay` IS `sch 3 item 1 piece rates` -- input mapping
        `the pay earned in the 14 days before the event` IS earned -- input mapping
        `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days` IS `days worked` -- input mapping
        `the monthly pay` IS `ea3 my pay record` 0 0 0 -- placeholder: read only by items 2 to 4
        `the days required in the first week` IS `ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0 -- placeholder: read only by items 2 to 4
        `the days required in the second week` IS `ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0 -- placeholder: read only by item 3
        `the weeks for the average` IS `ea3 the weeks that no item reads` -- placeholder: read only by item 4
        `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved` IS NOTHING -- placeholder: read only by item 4

§ `The Employment Act 1968 -- my questions (Part 15 to the Fifth Schedule)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If I make a claim to the Commissioner for Labour (s 115)`
-- Situation: asked of an employee who has, or is thinking of making, a claim against an employer.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 115(1A).  The Commissioner must not inquire into a dispute unless it is of a type the regulations prescribe, or a claim about it was lodged before 1 April 2017.
@export Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute?
GIVEN `my kind of dispute is of a type that regulations made under section 139 prescribe` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Is your kind of dispute one of the types that the regulations made under section 139 prescribe?
      `I have lodged a claim with the Commissioner about this dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged a claim about this dispute with the Commissioner?
      `the day I lodged the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge your claim? (Any date if you have not lodged one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(1A), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my kind of dispute` IS
    `ea3 the rule's answer whether or not I am sure` `my kind of dispute is of a type that regulations made under section 139 prescribe` (GIVEN prescribed YIELD `s 115(1A) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into or deciding the dispute` prescribed (`ea3 the day, if it happened` `I have lodged a claim with the Commissioner about this dispute` `the day I lodged the claim`))

-- s 115(2).  The Commissioner must not inquire into matters arising earlier than one year before the claim was lodged or the contract of
-- service ended; and a claim about the way the job ended must be lodged within 6 months of its ending.
@export Under section 115(2), is my claim in time?
GIVEN `the day the matter I claim about arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the matter you claim about arise?
      `the day I lodged my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge your claim with the Commissioner?
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employment ended?
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employment end? (Any date if it has not ended.)
      `my claim is about something that arose out of the way my employment ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim about something that arose out of, or as the result of, the way your employment ended (for example, being dismissed)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(2), is my claim in time` IS
    `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` `the day the matter I claim about arose` `the day I lodged my claim` (`ea3 the day, if it happened` `my employment has ended` `the day my employment ended`) `my claim is about something that arose out of the way my employment ended` `ea3 the public holidays the seat passes`

-- s 115(1) with (1A) and (2).  Whether the Commissioner can deal with the dispute.
@export Under section 115(1), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my dispute with my employer?
GIVEN `my dispute is with my employer or with a person the Act makes liable to pay me salary due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute between you and your employer, or a person who is liable under the Act to pay you salary due?
      `my dispute arises out of a term of my contract of service or out of a provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the dispute arise out of a term of your contract of service, or out of a provision of the Employment Act?
      `my kind of dispute is of a type that regulations made under section 139 prescribe` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Is your kind of dispute one of the types that the regulations made under section 139 prescribe?
      `I have lodged a claim with the Commissioner about this dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged a claim about this dispute with the Commissioner?
      `the day I lodged the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge your claim? (Any date if you have not lodged one.)
      `the day the matter I claim about arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the matter you claim about arise?
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employment ended?
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employment end? (Any date if it has not ended.)
      `my claim is about something that arose out of the way my employment ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim about something that arose out of, or as the result of, the way your employment ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(1), can the Commissioner inquire into and decide my dispute with my employer` IS
    `ea3 the rule's answer whether or not I am sure` `my kind of dispute is of a type that regulations made under section 139 prescribe`
        (GIVEN prescribed YIELD
            `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute`
                `my dispute is with my employer or with a person the Act makes liable to pay me salary due`
                `my dispute arises out of a term of my contract of service or out of a provision of the Act`
                (`s 115(1A) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into or deciding the dispute` prescribed (`ea3 the day, if it happened` `I have lodged a claim with the Commissioner about this dispute` `the day I lodged the claim`))
                (`s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` `the day the matter I claim about arose` `the day I lodged the claim` (`ea3 the day, if it happened` `my employment has ended` `the day my employment ended`) `my claim is about something that arose out of the way my employment ended` `ea3 the public holidays the seat passes`))

-- s 115(2A).  The Commissioner may direct the parties to attend a mediation by an approved mediator or a conciliation by a conciliation officer.
@export Under section 115(2A), can the Commissioner direct me and my employer to attend mediation or conciliation?
GIVEN `my dispute is one the Commissioner can inquire into under section 115(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your dispute one that the Commissioner can inquire into under section 115(1)?
      `the mediation is by an approved mediator under the Employment Claims Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the mediation be conducted by an approved mediator, as the Employment Claims Act 2016 defines one?
      `the conciliation is by a conciliation officer under the Industrial Relations Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the conciliation be conducted by a conciliation officer, as the Industrial Relations Act 1960 defines one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(2A), can the Commissioner direct me and my employer to attend mediation or conciliation` IS
    `s 115(2A) the Commissioner may direct the parties to attend the mediation or conciliation` `my dispute is one the Commissioner can inquire into under section 115(1)` `the mediation is by an approved mediator under the Employment Claims Act 2016` `the conciliation is by a conciliation officer under the Industrial Relations Act 1960`

-- s 115(3).  The Commissioner may hear and decide the claim of a subcontractor for labour.
@export Under section 115(3), can the Commissioner decide my claim as a subcontractor for labour against the contractor or subcontractor?
GIVEN `I am a subcontractor for labour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you supply the labour needed for work that a contractor or subcontractor has contracted to do for a principal or contractor, under your own contract with that contractor or subcontractor?
      `my claim is against a contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim against that contractor or subcontractor?
      `my claim is for a sum due for labour I provided under my contract with the contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for a sum due to you for labour that you provided under your contract with them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(3), can the Commissioner decide my claim as a subcontractor for labour against the contractor or subcontractor` IS
    `s 115(3) the Commissioner may hear and decide the claim of the subcontractor for labour` `I am a subcontractor for labour` `my claim is against a contractor or subcontractor` `my claim is for a sum due for labour I provided under my contract with the contractor or subcontractor`

-- s 115(3A).  An order for payment to an employee in a managerial or executive position must not exceed $20,000.
@export Under section 115(3A), is the sum I claim within the limit on what the Commissioner can order?
GIVEN `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a managerial or an executive position?
      `the sum of money I ask the Commissioner to order` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum of money, in dollars, do you ask the Commissioner to order to be paid to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(3A), is the sum I claim within the limit on what the Commissioner can order` IS
    `s 115(3A) the order for the payment of money is within the limit` `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position` `the sum of money I ask the Commissioner to order`

-- s 115(3B) and (3C).  An order made in your absence may be set aside or varied on your application, made no later than 14 days after the order.
@export Under section 115(3C), can I still apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence?
GIVEN `the Commissioner made the order in my absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commissioner make the order when you were not there?
      `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commissioner make the order?
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you apply to set it aside or vary it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(3C), can I still apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` IS
    -- the person asking is the party absent, so "the application is made by that party" is fixed at TRUE
    `s 115(3B) and (3C) the Commissioner may set aside or vary the order on the application` `the Commissioner made the order in my absence` TRUE (`s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` `the day of the order` `the day I apply` `ea3 the public holidays the seat passes`)

-- s 115(3C).  The last day for the application: 14 days after the date of the order, moved on by the Interpretation Act's s 50(b) if it falls on an excluded day.
@export Under section 115(3C), what is the last day on which I can apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence?
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commissioner make the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 115(3C), what is the last day on which I can apply to set aside or vary an order the Commissioner made in my absence` IS
    `s 115(3C) the last day for making the application` `the day of the order` `ea3 the public holidays the seat passes`

-- s 115(4).  "Employer" includes the transferor and the transferee of an undertaking or part of one referred to in s 18A.
@export Under section 115(4), is the new owner of my employer's undertaking my employer for a claim before the Commissioner?
GIVEN `my employer's undertaking, or part of it, has been transferred as section 18A describes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer's undertaking, or the part you work in, been transferred to a new owner as section 18A describes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(4), is the new owner of my employer's undertaking my employer for a claim before the Commissioner` IS
    `s 115(4) "employer" the person is one` `my employer's undertaking, or part of it, has been transferred as section 18A describes` NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If my employer owes money to someone who owes me (s 116)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 116(1).  After an order against your employer, the Commissioner may order another person who owes your employer money, under a contract you worked on, to pay it to the Commissioner.
@export Under section 116(1), can the Commissioner order a person who owes my employer money under a contract I worked on to pay it to the Commissioner?
GIVEN `the Commissioner has made an order against my employer for my salary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner made an order under section 115 against your employer, or a person liable, to pay you?
      `I am a workman or a subcontractor for labour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman, or a subcontractor for labour? (Section 116 reaches only a sum payable to one of them.)
      `the inquiry finds a contract between my employer and another person, in the course of which I did the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inquiry find a contract between your employer and another person, in the course of carrying out which you did the work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(1), can the Commissioner order a person who owes my employer money under a contract I worked on to pay it to the Commissioner` IS
    `s 116(1) the Commissioner may order the other person to pay the money to the Commissioner` `the Commissioner has made an order against my employer for my salary` `I am a workman or a subcontractor for labour` `the inquiry finds a contract between my employer and another person, in the course of which I did the work`

-- s 116(3).  If that person is liable as a principal under s 65, and what they admit owing my employer is not enough, they still owe me the balance.
@export Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer?
GIVEN `that person is liable as a principal under section 65 to pay my salary` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Is that person liable, as my employer's principal under section 65, to pay my salary?
      `the most that person is liable for under section 65` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the most that person is liable for under section 65? (0 if you do not know.)
      `the salary my employer owes me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much salary, in dollars, does your employer owe you?
      `the money that person admits owing my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc How much money, in dollars, does that person admit owing your employer?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 116(3), how much of my salary does that person still owe me after paying what they admit owing my employer` IS
    CONSIDER `ea3 what I say, as a fact` `that person is liable as a principal under section 65 to pay my salary`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST liable THEN `s 116(3) the balance of the salary for which the other person remains liable` (JUST liable) (`ea3 my amount if I know it` `the most that person is liable for under section 65`) `the salary my employer owes me` `the money that person admits owing my employer`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If I want to appeal against the Commissioner's decision (s 117)`
-- Situation: asked of an employee who is dissatisfied with a decision or order of the Commissioner.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 117(1).  You may appeal to the General Division of the High Court within 14 days after the decision or order.
@export Under section 117(1), am I in time to appeal to the High Court against the Commissioner's decision?
GIVEN `I am dissatisfied with the decision or order of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the Commissioner's decision or order?
      `the day of the decision or order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commissioner make the decision or order?
      `the day I appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117(1), am I in time to appeal to the High Court against the Commissioner's decision` IS
    `s 117(1) the person may appeal to the General Division of the High Court` `I am dissatisfied with the decision or order of the Commissioner` (`s 117(1) the appeal is made within 14 days after the decision or order` `the day of the decision or order` `the day I appeal` `ea3 the public holidays the seat passes`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What making a claim costs me (s 118)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 118(1).  No fee other than the registration fee in the Second Schedule is charged by the Commissioner.
@export Under section 118(1), may the Commissioner charge me a fee other than the registration fee?
GIVEN `the fee` IS A `s 118(1) Kind of fee` @desc Which fee do you mean: the registration fee at the rate in the Second Schedule, or a fee of any other kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 118(1), may the Commissioner charge me a fee other than the registration fee` IS
    `s 118(1) the Commissioner may charge the fee` `the fee`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `How my claim is made and heard (s 119)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 119(1)(a).  You lodge a memorandum at the Commissioner's office or make your claim in person.
@export Under section 119(1)(a), have I made my claim in a way the Act provides?
GIVEN `I have lodged a memorandum at the office of the Commissioner saying shortly what I claim and the remedy I seek` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged a memorandum at the Commissioner's office saying shortly what your claim is about and the remedy you want?
      `I have made my claim to the Commissioner in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made your claim to the Commissioner in person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(a), have I made my claim in a way the Act provides` IS
    `s 119(1)(a) the claim is made in a way that paragraph (a) provides` `I have lodged a memorandum at the office of the Commissioner saying shortly what I claim and the remedy I seek` `I have made my claim to the Commissioner in person`

-- s 119(1)(b).  On receiving your claim and the registration fee, the Commissioner must summon your employer in writing, giving reasonable notice of the nature of the claim and the time and place of the inquiry.
@export Under section 119(1)(b), is the Commissioner bound to summon my employer in writing once I have made my claim and paid the registration fee?
GIVEN `the Commissioner has received my memorandum or my verbal claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner received your memorandum, or your claim made in person?
      `the Commissioner has received the registration fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner received the registration fee for your claim (see schedule 2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(b), is the Commissioner bound to summon my employer in writing once I have made my claim and paid the registration fee` IS
    `s 119(1)(b) the Commissioner's duty to summon the party against whom the claim is made has arisen` `the Commissioner has received my memorandum or my verbal claim` `the Commissioner has received the registration fee`

-- s 119(1)(d).  A counterclaim against you must be notified in writing, with its nature and amount, not less than 3 days before the inquiry.
@export Under section 119(1)(d), did my employer give notice of its counterclaim against me in time?
GIVEN `the day my employer gave notice of the counterclaim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer give written notice of its counterclaim?
      `the day of the inquiry` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the inquiry?
      `the notice was in writing and stated the nature and amount of the counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice in writing, and did it state the nature and amount of the counterclaim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(d), did my employer give notice of its counterclaim against me in time` IS
    `s 119(1)(d) the notice of the counterclaim is given not less than 3 days before the date of the inquiry` `the day my employer gave notice of the counterclaim` `the day of the inquiry` `the notice was in writing and stated the nature and amount of the counterclaim`

-- s 119(1)(e).  A party must be present at a preliminary inquiry that the Commissioner holds between the issuing of the summons and the hearing, of which the party has been notified in writing.
@export Under section 119(1)(e), must I be present at the preliminary inquiry?
GIVEN `the Commissioner holds a preliminary inquiry between the issuing of the summons and the hearing of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commissioner holding a preliminary inquiry between the issuing of the summons and the hearing of your claim?
      `I have been notified in writing of the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been notified in writing of the inquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(e), must I be present at the preliminary inquiry` IS
    `s 119(1)(e) the party must be present at the preliminary inquiry` `the Commissioner holds a preliminary inquiry between the issuing of the summons and the hearing of my claim` `I have been notified in writing of the inquiry`

-- s 119(1)(f).  At the preliminary inquiry the parties may amend or withdraw the whole claim or a portion of it, make a counterclaim, or reach a settlement.
@export Under section 119(1)(f), may I take this step at the preliminary inquiry?
GIVEN `the step` IS A `s 119(1)(f) Step at the preliminary inquiry` @desc Which step do you want to take at the preliminary inquiry: amend the whole claim or a portion of it, withdraw the whole claim or a portion of it, make a counterclaim, reach a settlement, or a step of some other kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(f), may I take this step at the preliminary inquiry` IS
    `s 119(1)(f) the parties may take the step at the preliminary inquiry` `the step`

-- s 119(1)(g).  Where a settlement is effected at the preliminary inquiry, the Commissioner must make an order recording its terms, which has effect as if made after a hearing.
@export Under section 119(1)(g), will the Commissioner record the terms of our settlement in an order?
GIVEN `a settlement is effected at the preliminary inquiry in respect of my claim or a portion of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and your employer reached a settlement at the preliminary inquiry in respect of your claim or a portion of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(g), will the Commissioner record the terms of our settlement in an order` IS
    `s 119(1)(g) the Commissioner must make an order recording the terms of the settlement` `a settlement is effected at the preliminary inquiry in respect of my claim or a portion of it`

-- s 119(1)(h).  At the time and place appointed the parties must attend and state their case; the Commissioner then gives a decision and makes the order in the prescribed form.
@export Under section 119(1)(h), must I attend the hearing and state my case?
GIVEN `it is the time and place appointed for the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the time and place appointed for the hearing of your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(h), must I attend the hearing and state my case` IS
    `s 119(1)(h) the parties must attend and state their case` `it is the time and place appointed for the hearing`

-- s 119(1)(i).  If you are duly summoned and do not turn up, the Commissioner may decide in your absence.
@export Under section 119(1)(i), can the Commissioner decide the claim without me if I do not attend?
GIVEN `I have been duly summoned by the Commissioner to attend the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been duly summoned by the Commissioner to attend the inquiry?
      `I do not attend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you fail to attend?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(i), can the Commissioner decide the claim without me if I do not attend` IS
    `s 119(1)(i) the Commissioner may hear the claim and make the decision in the person's absence` `I have been duly summoned by the Commissioner to attend the inquiry` `I do not attend`

-- s 119(1)(j).  Any person interested is entitled to a copy of the record of a case on payment of the prescribed fee.
@export Under section 119(1)(j), am I entitled to a copy of the record of my case?
GIVEN `I am interested in the dispute, decision or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person interested in the dispute, decision or order?
      `I have paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the fee that the regulations prescribe for a copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1)(j), am I entitled to a copy of the record of my case` IS
    `s 119(1)(j) the person is entitled to a copy of the record` `I am interested in the dispute, decision or order` `I have paid the prescribed fee`

-- s 119(2)(a).  The Commissioner is not bound to act formally or to follow the Evidence Act 1893.
@export Under section 119(2)(a), is the Commissioner bound to follow formal procedure or the Evidence Act 1893 when hearing my claim?
GIVEN `the Commissioner is hearing my claim or conducting proceedings under Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commissioner hearing your claim, or conducting proceedings, under Part 15?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(2)(a), is the Commissioner bound to follow formal procedure or the Evidence Act 1893 when hearing my claim` IS
    `s 119(2)(a) the Commissioner is bound to act in a formal manner or in accordance with the Evidence Act 1893` `the Commissioner is hearing my claim or conducting proceedings under Part 15`

-- s 119(2)(b).  The Commissioner must act according to equity, good conscience and the merits of the case, without regard to technicalities.
@export Under section 119(2)(b), must the Commissioner decide my claim on equity, good conscience and the merits, without regard to technicalities?
GIVEN `the Commissioner is hearing my claim or conducting proceedings under Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commissioner hearing your claim, or conducting proceedings, under Part 15?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(2)(b), must the Commissioner decide my claim on equity, good conscience and the merits, without regard to technicalities` IS
    `s 119(2)(b) the Commissioner must act according to equity, good conscience and the merits of the case without regard to technicalities` `the Commissioner is hearing my claim or conducting proceedings under Part 15`

-- s 119(3).  All proceedings before the Commissioner are held in private.
@export Under section 119(3), will the hearing of my claim be held in private?
GIVEN `my claim is before the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim being heard by the Commissioner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(3), will the hearing of my claim be held in private` IS
    `s 119(3) the proceeding is to be held in private` `my claim is before the Commissioner`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Who may speak for me before the Commissioner (s 120)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 120.  An employee who belongs to a recognised trade union may be represented by an officer of it; never by an advocate, solicitor or paid agent.
@export Under section 120, may I be represented before the Commissioner by this person?
GIVEN `I belong to a trade union that my employer recognises under Part 3 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a trade union that your employer has recognised under Part 3 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960?
      `the person is an officer of that trade union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer of that trade union?
      `the person is an advocate or solicitor or a paid agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an advocate or solicitor, or a paid agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 120, may I be represented before the Commissioner by this person` IS
    -- the party is the employee, so "the party is an employer" and "the person is one of the employer's employees" are fixed at FALSE
    `s 120 the party may be represented by the person` `I belong to a trade union that my employer recognises under Part 3 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` FALSE `the person is an officer of that trade union` FALSE `the person is an advocate or solicitor or a paid agent`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If several of us have the same claim, or I want to split mine (ss 121 to 123)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 121(1).  Where it appears to the Commissioner that several employees have a common or similar claim against the same employer, each need not claim separately.
@export Under section 121(1), must each of us with the same claim against our employer make a separate claim?
GIVEN `it appears to the Commissioner that several of us have a common claim or similar claims against the same employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Commissioner that several employees (or subcontractors for labour) have a common claim or similar claims against the same employer or person liable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 121(1), must each of us with the same claim against our employer make a separate claim` IS
    `s 121(1) it is necessary for each of the employees or subcontractors for labour to make a separate claim` `it appears to the Commissioner that several of us have a common claim or similar claims against the same employer`

-- s 121(2).  The Commissioner must require your personal attendance if the Commissioner thinks your employer's interest is likely to be prejudiced by your not attending.
@export Under section 121(2), must I attend in person if the Commissioner thinks my employer would be prejudiced by my absence?
GIVEN `the Commissioner is of the opinion that my employer's interest is or is likely to be prejudiced by my not attending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commissioner of the opinion that your employer's interest is or is likely to be prejudiced by your not attending in person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 121(2), must I attend in person if the Commissioner thinks my employer would be prejudiced by my absence` IS
    `s 121(2) the Commissioner must require the personal attendance of the employee or subcontractor for labour` `the Commissioner is of the opinion that my employer's interest is or is likely to be prejudiced by my not attending`

-- s 122.  Nothing in Part 15 limits or affects the jurisdiction of any court.
@export Under section 122, does Part 15 limit the power of a court to hear a case about my employment?
GIVEN `the jurisdiction in question is that of a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power in question the jurisdiction of a court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 122, does Part 15 limit the power of a court to hear a case about my employment` IS
    `s 122 this Part limits or affects the jurisdiction of the court` `the jurisdiction in question is that of a court`

-- s 123.  A claim must not be divided and pursued in separate proceedings for the sole purpose of bringing each within the Commissioner's jurisdiction.
@export Under section 123, may I divide my claim into several claims so that each comes within the Commissioner's jurisdiction?
GIVEN `the only reason to divide it is to bring each part within the jurisdiction of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason for dividing your claim to bring the sum claimed in each part within the jurisdiction of the Employment Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 123, may I divide my claim into several claims so that each comes within the Commissioner's jurisdiction` IS
    `s 123 the claim may be divided and pursued in separate proceedings` `the only reason to divide it is to bring each part within the jurisdiction of the Act`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If a relevant authority summons me, or I complain (ss 124 to 126)`
-- Situation: asked of a person who has been summoned, or who has made a complaint.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 124(1).  A person summoned by a relevant authority is legally bound to attend and to furnish information or documents, produce any article or give statements.
@export Under section 124(1), am I legally bound to attend and give information if a relevant authority summons me?
GIVEN `I have been summoned by a relevant authority under section 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been summoned by the Minister, the Parliamentary Secretary to the Minister, the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry of Manpower, the Commissioner or an inspecting officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 124(1), am I legally bound to attend and give information if a relevant authority summons me` IS
    `s 124(1) the person summoned is legally bound to attend and to furnish information or documents, produce any article or give statements` `I have been summoned by a relevant authority under section 124(1)`

-- s 124(1).  A person summoned must answer truthfully all questions the relevant authority puts to them.
@export Under section 124(1), must I answer truthfully the questions a relevant authority puts to me?
GIVEN `I have been summoned by a relevant authority under section 124(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been summoned by a relevant authority?
      `the relevant authority has put the question to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the relevant authority put the question to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 124(1), must I answer truthfully the questions a relevant authority puts to me` IS
    `s 124(1) the person summoned is legally bound to answer the question truthfully` `I have been summoned by a relevant authority under section 124(1)` `the relevant authority has put the question to me`

-- s 124(1)(b).  If you complain to a relevant authority of a breach of the Act, the authority may summon any other person it has reason to believe can give information about the complaint.
@export Under section 124(1)(b), if I complain of a breach of the Act, can the authority summon someone who can give information about it?
GIVEN `I complained to` IS A `s 124(1)(a) Kind of person` @desc Whom did you complain to: the Minister, the Parliamentary Secretary to the Minister, the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry of Manpower, the Commissioner, an inspecting officer, or someone else?
      `I have complained of a breach of a provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complained to that person of a breach of a provision of the Employment Act?
      `the authority has reason to believe that the other person can give information about my complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authority have reason to believe that the other person can give information about your complaint?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 124(1)(b), if I complain of a breach of the Act, can the authority summon someone who can give information about it` IS
    -- the authority has no inquiry of its own to make from my complaint alone, so "reasonable grounds or wishes to inquire" is fixed at FALSE
    `s 124(1) the relevant authority may summon the person` (`s 124(1)(a) "relevant authority" the person is one` `I complained to`) FALSE `I have complained of a breach of a provision of the Act` `the authority has reason to believe that the other person can give information about my complaint`

-- s 124(2).  Obstructing a summons, or neglecting to attend after being summoned, is an offence.
@export Under section 124(2), do I commit an offence if I ignore a summons or obstruct it?
GIVEN `I wilfully obstruct the service of or obedience to the summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you wilfully obstruct the service of the summons, or anyone's obedience to it?
      `I am summoned and neglect to attend as the summons requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having been summoned, would you neglect to attend as the summons requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 124(2), do I commit an offence if I ignore a summons or obstruct it` IS
    `s 124(2) the person is guilty of an offence` `I wilfully obstruct the service of or obedience to the summons` `I am summoned and neglect to attend as the summons requires`

-- s 125(1).  Where proceedings arise from an employee's complaint that is found well founded, the Commissioner is to institute them for and in the name of the employee.
@export Under section 125(1), will the Commissioner bring proceedings in my name for a complaint I made?
GIVEN `an inquiry under section 124 shows that an offence has been committed or that my complaint is well founded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an inquiry under section 124 show that an offence has been committed, or that your complaint is well founded?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 125(1), will the Commissioner bring proceedings in my name for a complaint I made` IS
    -- the complainant is an employee, so "the proceedings arise from a complaint made by an employee or a subcontractor for labour" is fixed at TRUE
    `s 125(1) the Commissioner is to institute the proceedings for and in the name of the employee or subcontractor for labour` (`s 125(1) the Commissioner may institute proceedings, civil or criminal` `an inquiry under section 124 shows that an offence has been committed or that my complaint is well founded`) TRUE

-- s 125(2).  Where several employees make a similar complaint, the Commissioner may consolidate them into one cause of action, if the Commissioner sues in their names.
@export Under section 125(2), can the Commissioner join my complaint with other employees' similar complaints into one proceeding?
GIVEN `other employees make a similar complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do other employees (or subcontractors for labour) make a similar complaint?
      `the Commissioner brings civil proceedings in our names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commissioner bringing civil proceedings for and in the name of all of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 125(2), can the Commissioner join my complaint with other employees' similar complaints into one proceeding` IS
    `s 125(2) the Commissioner may consolidate the complaints into one cause of action and need take out only one summons` `other employees make a similar complaint` `the Commissioner brings civil proceedings in our names`

-- s 126.  No court fees are chargeable in the first instance on proceedings commenced by an employee, or by the Commissioner for the employee, against the employer.
@export Under section 126, must I pay court fees at the start of proceedings against my employer?
GIVEN `the proceedings are commenced by me or by the Commissioner on my behalf against my employer or other person liable under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings commenced by you, or by the Commissioner on your behalf, against your employer or another person liable under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 126, must I pay court fees at the start of proceedings against my employer` IS
    `s 126 court fees are chargeable in the first instance on the proceedings` `the proceedings are commenced by me or by the Commissioner on my behalf against my employer or other person liable under the Act`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If my employer has not kept to the rules on records, key terms and pay slips (ss 126A and 126D)`
-- Situation: asked of an employee whose employer may have failed to keep records, to give a record of key employment terms, or to give pay slips.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 126A(a).  An employer's failure to comply with s 95(1) (records), s 95A(2) (a written record of key employment terms) or s 96(1) (pay slips) is a civil contravention.
@export Under section 126A(a), is my employer's failure to keep records, give me a record of key terms, or give me pay slips a civil contravention?
GIVEN `my employer has failed to make and keep the employee records that section 95(1) requires` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Has your employer failed to make and keep the employee records that section 95(1) requires?
      `my employer has failed to give me the written record of key employment terms that section 95A(2) requires` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Has your employer failed to give you the written record of key employment terms that section 95A(2) requires?
      `my employer has failed to give me the pay slips that section 96(1) requires` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Has your employer failed to give you the pay slips that section 96(1) requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 126A(a), is my employer's failure to keep records, give me a record of key terms, or give me pay slips a civil contravention` IS
    `s 126A(a) the failure is a civil contravention` (`ea3 what I say, as a fact` `my employer has failed to make and keep the employee records that section 95(1) requires`) (`ea3 what I say, as a fact` `my employer has failed to give me the written record of key employment terms that section 95A(2) requires`) (`ea3 what I say, as a fact` `my employer has failed to give me the pay slips that section 96(1) requires`)

-- s 126D(2).  An employer who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an authorised officer's direction is guilty of an offence.
@export Under section 126D(2), is my employer guilty of an offence if it does not comply with an authorised officer's direction?
GIVEN `an authorised officer has given my employer a direction under section 126D(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised officer given your employer a direction under section 126D(1)?
      `my employer has failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer failed to comply with the direction?
      `my employer has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 126D(2), is my employer guilty of an offence if it does not comply with an authorised officer's direction` IS
    `s 126D(2) the employer is guilty of an offence` `an authorised officer has given my employer a direction under section 126D(1)` `my employer has failed to comply with the direction` `my employer has a reasonable excuse`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Prosecutions, fines and service of papers (ss 129 to 137)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 127A.  No liability lies against a person appointed under section 3, or acting under the Commissioner's direction, for what is done with reasonable care and in good faith.
@export Under section 127A, can I hold an officer of the Commissioner liable for something done with reasonable care and in good faith?
GIVEN `the person was appointed under section 3 or acts under the direction of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person appointed under section 3 of the Employment Act, or acting under the direction of the Commissioner?
      `it was done with reasonable care and in good faith in carrying out the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done with reasonable care and in good faith in carrying out the Employment Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 127A, can I hold an officer of the Commissioner liable for something done with reasonable care and in good faith` IS
    `s 127A liability lies against the person` `the person was appointed under section 3 or acts under the direction of the Commissioner` `it was done with reasonable care and in good faith in carrying out the Act`

-- s 129(1).  Convictions and penalties for offences under the Act may be had and recovered before a Magistrate's Court or a District Court on the complaint of a person aggrieved, subject to any special provision to the contrary.
@export Under section 129(1), can I, as a person aggrieved, complain of an offence under the Act to this court?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `ea3 Court` @desc Which court would you complain to?
      `a special provision to the contrary in the Act applies` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Does another provision of the Employment Act say that the complaint must be made somewhere else or in some other way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 129(1), can I, as a person aggrieved, complain of an offence under the Act to this court` IS
    `ea3 the rule's answer whether or not I am sure` `a special provision to the contrary in the Act applies`
        (GIVEN special YIELD `s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` (`ea3 the court I mean` `the court`) `s 129(1) a person aggrieved` special)

-- s 129(2).  A Magistrate's Court may not impose imprisonment exceeding 12 months; a District Court may impose the full punishment the Act prescribes.
@export Under section 129(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment this court may impose for the offence, in months?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `ea3 Court` @desc Which court would try the offence?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the Act prescribes for the offence, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that the Act prescribes for the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 129(2), what is the longest term of imprisonment this court may impose for the offence, in months` IS
    `s 129(2) the longest term of imprisonment the court may impose` (`ea3 the court I mean` `the court`) `the longest term of imprisonment the Act prescribes for the offence, in months`

-- s 131.  In proceedings under Part 15 the onus of proving that a person is not the employer is on the person who alleges it.
@export Under section 131, who must prove that my employer is not my employer?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings under Part 15 of the Act?
      `my employer alleges that it is not my employer or the person whose duty it is under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer allege that it is not your employer, or not the person whose duty it is under the Act to do or abstain from doing the thing in question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131, who must prove that my employer is not my employer` IS
    `s 131 the onus of proving that the person is not the employer is on the person who alleges it` `the proceedings are under Part 15` `my employer alleges that it is not my employer or the person whose duty it is under the Act`

-- s 132.  Nothing in the Act prevents you from enforcing your civil rights and remedies by a suit in court where proceedings under the Act are not instituted or not proceeded with to judgment.
@export Under section 132, can I still sue my employer in court for breach of my contract of service?
GIVEN `no proceedings under the Act were instituted, or those instituted were not proceeded with to judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were no proceedings under the Employment Act instituted, or were the proceedings instituted not proceeded with to judgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 132, can I still sue my employer in court for breach of my contract of service` IS
    `s 132 this Act prevents the employer or employee from enforcing civil rights and remedies by suit in court` `no proceedings under the Act were instituted, or those instituted were not proceeded with to judgment`

-- s 133.  If the Commissioner who took down the evidence cannot finish the inquiry, a successor may deal with the evidence as if taken down by the successor and proceed from where the predecessor left it.
@export Under section 133, can the new Commissioner carry on my inquiry from where the earlier one left it?
GIVEN `the earlier Commissioner or officer took down evidence or made a memorandum in the inquiry into my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commissioner or officer who was inquiring into your claim take down evidence or make a memorandum for the inquiry?
      `the earlier Commissioner or officer is prevented by death, transfer or other cause from finishing the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that Commissioner or officer prevented, by death, transfer or other cause, from concluding the inquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 133, can the new Commissioner carry on my inquiry from where the earlier one left it` IS
    `s 133 the successor may proceed with the inquiry from the stage at which the predecessor left it` `the earlier Commissioner or officer took down evidence or made a memorandum in the inquiry into my claim` `the earlier Commissioner or officer is prevented by death, transfer or other cause from finishing the inquiry`

-- s 134.  The court may direct that a fine be paid to the party complaining, or to the employee where an employer committed an offence in respect of a liability to pay money to that employee.
@export Under section 134, can the court direct that the fine be paid to me?
GIVEN `the court imposes a fine or enforces the payment of a sum secured by a recognizance or bond under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court impose a fine, or enforce the payment of a sum secured by a recognizance or bond, under the Employment Act?
      `I am` IS A `s 134 Recipient of the fine` @desc Are you the party complaining, the employee to whom the offending employer owed money, or someone else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 134, can the court direct that the fine be paid to me` IS
    `s 134 the court may direct that the fine or sum be paid to the person` `the court imposes a fine or enforces the payment of a sum secured by a recognizance or bond under the Act` `I am`

-- s 135.  After imprisonment suffered for not paying a fine, compensation or damages with costs, the amount ordered is deemed liquidated and discharged and the order is annulled.
@export Under section 135, is the sum a court ordered my employer to pay me discharged once my employer has served imprisonment for not paying it?
GIVEN `my employer has served imprisonment for not paying the sum ordered, and the imprisonment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer served imprisonment under the Employment Act for not paying the fine, compensation or damages (with costs) that a court ordered, and has that imprisonment ended?
      `a special provision of the Act says otherwise` IS A `ea3 My answer` @desc Does another provision of the Employment Act say that the sum is still owed after the imprisonment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 135, is the sum a court ordered my employer to pay me discharged once my employer has served imprisonment for not paying it` IS
    `ea3 the rule's answer whether or not I am sure` `a special provision of the Act says otherwise` (GIVEN special YIELD `s 135 the amount ordered is deemed to be liquidated and discharged` `my employer has served imprisonment for not paying the sum ordered, and the imprisonment has ended` special)

-- s 137(1).  A requisition or summons may be served on a person by delivering it to the person or to an adult member of the person's family at the last known residence, or by leaving it at, or posting it by registered post to, the usual or last known residence or place of business.
@export Under section 137(1), may a summons be served on me in this way?
GIVEN `the way` IS A `s 137(1) Way of serving` @desc In which way was it served on you: delivered to you or to an adult member of your family at your last known residence; left at, or posted by registered post to, your usual or last known residence or place of business; delivered to an officer of a body at its registered office; posted by registered post to a body at its registered office; or some other way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 137(1), may a summons be served on me in this way` IS
    -- the employee is an individual, so "the person is a body of persons or a body corporate" is fixed at FALSE
    `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `the way` FALSE

-- s 137(2).  A requisition or summons sent to you by registered post is treated as served when it would in the ordinary course of post be delivered.
@export Under section 137(2), on what day is a summons sent to me by registered post treated as served on me?
GIVEN `it was sent to me by registered post in accordance with section 137(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the requisition or summons sent to you by registered post, as section 137(1) allows?
      `the day it would in the ordinary course of post be delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what day would it in the ordinary course of post be delivered?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 137(2), on what day is a summons sent to me by registered post treated as served on me` IS
    `s 137(2) the requisition or summons sent by registered post is deemed to be duly served at the time` `it was sent to me by registered post in accordance with section 137(1)` `the day it would in the ordinary course of post be delivered`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The First Schedule: am I a workman? (Schedule 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 1 paragraphs (1) to (8).  A person specified in the First Schedule is a workman (s 2(1) "workman" (d)).
@export Under schedule 1 paragraphs (1) to (8), is my job one of those the First Schedule lists as workmen?
GIVEN `my job` IS A `sch 1 Kind of occupation` @desc Which of these is your job: cleaner, construction worker, labourer, machine operator or assembler, metal and machinery worker, train, bus, lorry or van driver, train or bus inspector, a job none of these names, or are you not sure?
      `I am paid piece rates and work in my employer's premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid piece rates, and do you work in your employer's premises?
      `I am a workman because of another part of the definition of "workman"` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman because you do manual labour, drive or maintain passenger or commercial vehicles, supervise while doing manual labour, or have been declared a workman by the Minister?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraphs (1) to (8), is my job one of those the First Schedule lists as workmen` IS
    `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `my job` `I am paid piece rates and work in my employer's premises` `I am a workman because of another part of the definition of "workman"`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The Second Schedule: what a claim costs me (Schedule 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `ea3 I am claiming as` IS ONE OF
    `ea3 an employee`
    `ea3 a subcontractor for labour`

-- Schedule 2 paragraph (a).  The registration fee for a claim by an employee.
@export Under schedule 2 paragraph (a), how much is the registration fee for my claim to the Commissioner, in dollars?
GIVEN `I am claiming as` IS A `ea3 I am claiming as` @desc Are you claiming as an employee, or as a subcontractor for labour?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph (a), how much is the registration fee for my claim to the Commissioner, in dollars` IS
    `sch 2 the registration fee`
        (CONSIDER `I am claiming as`
         WHEN `ea3 an employee` THEN `Claimant who is an employee` -- input mapping
         WHEN `ea3 a subcontractor for labour` THEN `Claimant who is a subcontractor for labour`) -- input mapping

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The Third Schedule: my gross and basic rate of pay for one day (Schedule 3, s 107A)`
-- Situation: asked of an employee paid a monthly rate or piece rates, when a section says "gross rate of pay" or "basic rate of pay" for a day.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 3 item 1, second column.  Piece rates: the total salary (less overtime, bonus, reimbursement, productivity incentive, travelling, food and housing allowances) earned in the 14 days before, divided by the days worked.
@export Under schedule 3 item 1, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid piece rates?
GIVEN `my pay for the work in the 14 days before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, did you earn in the 14 days immediately before the day in question, in dollars?
      `my commissions in the 14 days before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you earn in commissions in those 14 days, in dollars?
      `my other allowances in the 14 days before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you receive in allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances in those 14 days, in dollars?
      `the days I actually worked in those 14 days` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days did you actually work in those 14 days?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 1, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid piece rates` IS
    `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 my piece rate facts` (`ea3 my pay record` `my pay for the work in the 14 days before` `my commissions in the 14 days before` `my other allowances in the 14 days before`) `the days I actually worked in those 14 days`)

-- Schedule 3 item 1, third column.  Piece rates, basic rate: no allowance of any kind counts.
@export Under schedule 3 item 1, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid piece rates?
GIVEN `my pay for the work in the 14 days before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, did you earn in the 14 days immediately before the day in question, in dollars?
      `my commissions in the 14 days before` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you earn in commissions in those 14 days, in dollars?
      `the days I actually worked in those 14 days` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days did you actually work in those 14 days?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 1, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid piece rates` IS
    -- allowances of any other kind are left out of the basic rate, so 0 stands for them
    `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 my piece rate facts` (`ea3 my pay record` `my pay for the work in the 14 days before` `my commissions in the 14 days before` 0) `the days I actually worked in those 14 days`)

-- Schedule 3 item 2, second column.  Monthly rate, the same number of days in every week: 12 x monthly gross rate / (52 x days required in a week).
@export Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week?
GIVEN `my monthly pay for the work` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your monthly pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, in dollars?
      `my monthly commissions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in commissions in a month, in dollars?
      `my monthly allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you receive in a month in allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances, in dollars?
      `the days a week I am required to work for more than 5 hours` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days a week are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days a week I am required to work for 5 hours or less` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days a week are you required to work for 5 hours or less?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week` IS
    `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day`
        (`ea3 my monthly pay facts` `sch 3 item 2 monthly rate, the same number of days in every week`
            (`ea3 my pay record` `my monthly pay for the work` `my monthly commissions` `my monthly allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances`)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days a week I am required to work for more than 5 hours` `the days a week I am required to work for 5 hours or less`)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0)
            `ea3 the weeks that no item reads`
            NOTHING) -- placeholder: read only by item 4

-- Schedule 3 item 2, third column.
@export Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week?
GIVEN `my monthly pay for the work` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your monthly pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, in dollars?
      `my monthly commissions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in commissions in a month, in dollars?
      `the days a week I am required to work for more than 5 hours` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days a week are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days a week I am required to work for 5 hours or less` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days a week are you required to work for 5 hours or less?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 2, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and work the same number of days every week` IS
    `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day`
        (`ea3 my monthly pay facts` `sch 3 item 2 monthly rate, the same number of days in every week`
            (`ea3 my pay record` `my monthly pay for the work` `my monthly commissions` 0)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days a week I am required to work for more than 5 hours` `the days a week I am required to work for 5 hours or less`)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0)
            `ea3 the weeks that no item reads`
            NOTHING) -- placeholder: read only by item 4

-- Schedule 3 item 3, second column.  Monthly rate, a certain number of days one week and a different number the next, in every 2 consecutive weeks: 12 x monthly gross rate / (52 x the average over the 2 weeks).
@export Under schedule 3 item 3, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days alternate over 2 weeks?
GIVEN `my monthly pay for the work` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your monthly pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, in dollars?
      `my monthly commissions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in commissions in a month, in dollars?
      `my monthly allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you receive in a month in allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances, in dollars?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in my first week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the first of the 2 weeks, on how many days are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in my first week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the first of the 2 weeks, on how many days are you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in my second week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the second week, on how many days are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in my second week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the second week, on how many days are you required to work for 5 hours or less?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 3, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days alternate over 2 weeks` IS
    `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day`
        (`ea3 my monthly pay facts` `sch 3 item 3 monthly rate, a certain number of days in one week and a different number in the following week, in every period of 2 consecutive weeks`
            (`ea3 my pay record` `my monthly pay for the work` `my monthly commissions` `my monthly allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances`)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in my first week` `the days of 5 hours or less in my first week`)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in my second week` `the days of 5 hours or less in my second week`)
            `ea3 the weeks that no item reads`
            NOTHING) -- placeholder: read only by item 4

-- Schedule 3 item 3, third column.
@export Under schedule 3 item 3, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days alternate over 2 weeks?
GIVEN `my monthly pay for the work` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your monthly pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, in dollars?
      `my monthly commissions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in commissions in a month, in dollars?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in my first week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the first of the 2 weeks, on how many days are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in my first week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the first of the 2 weeks, on how many days are you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in my second week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the second week, on how many days are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in my second week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the second week, on how many days are you required to work for 5 hours or less?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 3, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days alternate over 2 weeks` IS
    `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day`
        (`ea3 my monthly pay facts` `sch 3 item 3 monthly rate, a certain number of days in one week and a different number in the following week, in every period of 2 consecutive weeks`
            (`ea3 my pay record` `my monthly pay for the work` `my monthly commissions` 0)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in my first week` `the days of 5 hours or less in my first week`)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in my second week` `the days of 5 hours or less in my second week`)
            `ea3 the weeks that no item reads`
            NOTHING) -- placeholder: read only by item 4

-- Schedule 3 items 4 to 6, second column.  Monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks: the average over the 3 weeks before.
-- The seat asks about an employee who has been employed for 3 weeks or more, so the "less than 3 weeks" alternative of item 5 is not asked (fixed at FALSE).
@export Under schedule 3 item 4, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days differ from week to week?
GIVEN `the purpose of the calculation` IS A `sch 3 item 5 Purpose of the calculation` @desc What is the rate for: salary in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1), salary deducted for absence from work under section 28(2), or any other case?
      `my monthly pay for the work` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your monthly pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, in dollars?
      `my monthly commissions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in commissions in a month, in dollars?
      `my monthly allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you receive in a month in allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances, in dollars?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in the first of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In the first of the 3 weeks immediately before, on how many days were you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in the first of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In that week, on how many days were you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in the second of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In the second of the 3 weeks, on how many days were you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in the second of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In that week, on how many days were you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in the third of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In the third of the 3 weeks, on how many days were you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in the third of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In that week, on how many days were you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved another formula for you, what daily rate does it give, in dollars? (0 if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 4, what is my gross rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days differ from week to week` IS
    `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day`
        (`ea3 my monthly pay facts` `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks`
            (`ea3 my pay record` `my monthly pay for the work` `my monthly commissions` `my monthly allowances other than travelling, food and housing allowances`)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0)
            (`ea3 my 3 weeks for the average` `the purpose of the calculation`
                (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in the first of the 3 weeks` `the days of 5 hours or less in the first of the 3 weeks`)
                (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in the second of the 3 weeks` `the days of 5 hours or less in the second of the 3 weeks`)
                (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in the third of the 3 weeks` `the days of 5 hours or less in the third of the 3 weeks`))
            (`ea3 my amount if I know it` `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved`))

-- Schedule 3 items 4 and 6, third column.  Item 6: only paragraph (c) of item 5 applies, so the purpose is not asked.
@export Under schedule 3 item 4, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days differ from week to week?
GIVEN `my monthly pay for the work` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your monthly pay for the work, including wage adjustments and increments, in dollars?
      `my monthly commissions` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in commissions in a month, in dollars?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in the first of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In the first of the 3 weeks immediately before, on how many days were you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in the first of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In that week, on how many days were you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in the second of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In the second of the 3 weeks, on how many days were you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in the second of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In that week, on how many days were you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in the third of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In the third of the 3 weeks, on how many days were you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or less in the third of the 3 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc In that week, on how many days were you required to work for 5 hours or less?
      `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved another formula for you, what daily rate does it give, in dollars? (0 if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 item 4, what is my basic rate of pay for one day if I am paid a monthly rate and my days differ from week to week` IS
    `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day`
        (`ea3 my monthly pay facts` `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks`
            (`ea3 my pay record` `my monthly pay for the work` `my monthly commissions` 0)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0)
            (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` 0 0)
            (`ea3 my 3 weeks for the average` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` -- item 6: paragraphs (a) and (b) are not applicable in the third column
                (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in the first of the 3 weeks` `the days of 5 hours or less in the first of the 3 weeks`)
                (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in the second of the 3 weeks` `the days of 5 hours or less in the second of the 3 weeks`)
                (`ea3 my week for the Third Schedule` `the days of more than 5 hours in the third of the 3 weeks` `the days of 5 hours or less in the third of the 3 weeks`))
            (`ea3 my amount if I know it` `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The Fourth Schedule: my hourly basic rate of pay for overtime (Schedule 4, s 38(6))`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 4 items 1 to 9.  The hourly basic rate of pay for working out overtime pay, by how your pay is fixed.
@export Under schedule 4 items 1 to 9, what is my hourly basic rate of pay for working out my overtime pay?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a workman (see schedule 1 for the list)?
      `my pay is fixed` IS A `ea3 How my pay is fixed` @desc How is your pay fixed: for each month, for each completed piece of work, for each hour, for each day, or in some other way?
      `my monthly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly basic rate of pay, in dollars? (0 if your pay is not fixed for each month.)
      `my total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay, in dollars? (0 if you are not paid piece rates.)
      `the total number of hours I worked in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you work in the week? (0 if you are not paid piece rates.)
      `my actual hourly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your actual hourly basic rate of pay, in dollars? (0 if your pay is not fixed for each hour.)
      `my daily basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your daily basic rate of pay, in dollars? (0 if your pay is not fixed for each day.)
      `the number of hours I work per day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours do you work per day? (0 if your pay is not fixed for each day.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 items 1 to 9, what is my hourly basic rate of pay for working out my overtime pay` IS
    `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay`
        (`sch 4 Facts about the pay` WITH
            `the type of employee` IS
                CONSIDER `my pay is fixed`
                WHEN `ea3 for each month` THEN IF `I am a workman` THEN `sch 4 item 1 a workman employed on a monthly rate of pay` ELSE `sch 4 item 2 a non-workman employed on a monthly basic rate of pay` -- input mapping
                WHEN `ea3 for each completed piece of work` THEN IF `I am a workman` THEN `sch 4 item 4 a workman employed on piece rates` ELSE `sch 4 item 5 a non-workman employed on piece rates` -- input mapping
                WHEN `ea3 for each hour` THEN IF `I am a workman` THEN `sch 4 item 6 a workman employed on an hourly rate of pay` ELSE `sch 4 item 7 a non-workman employed on an hourly rate of pay` -- input mapping
                WHEN `ea3 for each day` THEN IF `I am a workman` THEN `sch 4 item 8 a workman employed on a daily rate of pay` ELSE `sch 4 item 9 a non-workman employed on a daily rate of pay` -- input mapping
                WHEN `ea3 in some other way` THEN `sch 4 a type of employee that the First column does not list` -- input mapping
            `the monthly basic rate of pay` IS `my monthly basic rate of pay`
            `the total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received` IS `my total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received`
            `the total number of hours worked in the week` IS `the total number of hours I worked in the week`
            `the actual hourly basic rate of pay` IS `my actual hourly basic rate of pay`
            `the daily basic rate of pay` IS `my daily basic rate of pay`
            `the number of working hours per day` IS `the number of hours I work per day`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The Fifth Schedule: my days of absence under section 76(1)(c)(ii) (Schedule 5)`
-- Situation: asked of a female employee who has had, or is about to have, a confinement.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 5 items 1 to 5.  The number of days on which a female employee is entitled to absent herself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii), before the 24-day cap that section 76 itself applies.
@export Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)?
GIVEN `my work pattern` IS A `ea3 My work pattern after my confinement` @desc Which describes your work pattern under your contract of service just before the day of your confinement or the first day of your leave, whichever is earlier?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If you work the same number of days every week: on how many days a week are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or shorter in a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If you work the same number of days every week: on how many days a week are you required to work for 5 hours or shorter?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in each fixed week` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc If your pattern repeats over a number of fixed weeks: for each of those weeks in turn, on how many days are you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or shorter in each fixed week` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc If your pattern repeats over a number of fixed weeks: for each of those weeks in turn, on how many days are you required to work for 5 hours or shorter?
      `the days of more than 5 hours in each of the 3 weeks before` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc If you have no regular pattern: for each of the 3 weeks immediately before the day of your confinement or the first day of your leave, whichever is earlier, on how many days were you required to work for more than 5 hours?
      `the days of 5 hours or shorter in each of the 3 weeks before` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc If you have no regular pattern: for each of those 3 weeks, on how many days were you required to work for 5 hours or shorter?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 items 1 to 5, for how many days am I entitled to absent myself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii)` IS
    `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself`
        (`sch 5 Facts about the work pattern` WITH
            `the work pattern` IS
                CONSIDER `my work pattern`
                WHEN `ea3 I work the same number of days in every week` THEN `sch 5 item 1 the number of work days is the same in every week` -- input mapping
                WHEN `ea3 the number of days I work varies from week to week, in a pattern that repeats over a number of fixed weeks` THEN `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` -- input mapping
                WHEN `ea3 the number of days I work varies from week to week, with no regular pattern` THEN `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` -- input mapping
                WHEN `ea3 my work pattern is none of these` THEN `sch 5 a pattern that none of items 1, 2 and 3 describes` -- input mapping
            `the work days in a week when the number is the same in every week` IS `sch 5 Work days in a week` WITH
                `work days of more than 5 hours` IS `the days of more than 5 hours in a week`
                `work days of 5 hours or shorter` IS `the days of 5 hours or shorter in a week`
            `the work days in each of the fixed weeks of the repeated pattern` IS `ea3 my weeks of work days` `the days of more than 5 hours in each fixed week` `the days of 5 hours or shorter in each fixed week`
            `the work days in each of the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of leave` IS `ea3 my weeks of work days` `the days of more than 5 hours in each of the 3 weeks before` `the days of 5 hours or shorter in each of the 3 weeks before`)

-- Pairs two lists of numbers, week by week, into the Fifth Schedule's weeks.  A list of unequal length is cut to the shorter.
GIVEN full IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      short IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 5 Work days in a week`
`ea3 my weeks of work days` MEANS
    CONSIDER full
    WHEN EMPTY THEN LIST
    WHEN f FOLLOWED BY restFull THEN
        CONSIDER short
        WHEN EMPTY THEN LIST
        WHEN s FOLLOWED BY restShort THEN
            (`sch 5 Work days in a week` WITH
                `work days of more than 5 hours` IS f
                `work days of 5 hours or shorter` IS s) FOLLOWED BY (`ea3 my weeks of work days` restFull restShort)
